// AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/build-bible-v205.ts — do not edit by hand.
// Words: Jonathan's canonical commentary txt. Structure: his Notion pages.
import type { V205BookData } from '../types';

export const DATA: V205BookData = {
  book: "Revelation",
  display: "Revelation",
  chapters: {
    "1": {"chapter":1,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"I have accumulated a set of rules that I have applied to myself in my own personal study of this book of the Bible. Many are afraid to come to this book for various reasons, but I have come with an open mind, an open Bible, and an open conversation. My hopes are that (through the reading and studying of this amazing prophetic book) we will see some areas we need to grow and increase in faith and knowledge in our own walks, as well as take the seriousness of the Great Commission extremely personally and vitally. These “rules” are not governed with the intent of keeping us in a box. They are just… thoughts (if you will). Things to keep in mind as we go through this book of the Bible."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot pretend like we understand and know all things written in this book. Some things are not for us to fully understand or know (i.e. we don’t know much about Heaven. In fact, we know more about Hell than we do about Heaven). John makes it a point to try and describe with incredible detail the things that are taking place. He is told several times what he is supposed to write down. I don’t know if he wrote these things while he was seeing the revelation or if he wrote them after they occurred (I believe and understand based on the way it is portrayed that he more than likely wrote them as they were happening). It’s noted that this book was written most likely around his exile to Patmos, and that has to be remembered frequently as we read this account. He is writing during a time of great persecution to the Christian church by the Roman government. The reason he is sent to this island was because of his faith in Jesus Christ being rejected by the ruler of that day. John uses a lot of symbolism from his current time period. Some things that are mentioned are not directly related today, but it was relevant during the time of the writing (though it wouldn’t surprise me if they became places of actual fruition again today). There is a lot of symbolism that is used, and I will do my best to describe what scholars have said, how they line up with the Bible, and what they are more than likely to mean. Not everything will be fully understood (I need to reiterate this point, though I’ve already mentioned it), but that’s the ultimate goal of a study like this. These notes will not be incredibly honed in on a “scholarly” level, and that’s on purpose. These will simply be the best notes I can get or find for the largest of issues or most prominent of information. (I’ve gone through this book in several settings, and I still learn something new each time). I want my notes to be simple for a reason, so that I don’t overcomplicate the gospel message (more on that in a moment). John goes back and forth between things to come and things that had already happened a lot. I will try to reference when he does this, but sometimes he does it without warning. We should be open to researching uncertainties either now or later, so we don’t get caught up in semantics or unnecessary understandings. Lastly (and most importantly), we can read this book of the Bible with the same focus as all of the other books of the Bible, the center being Jesus Christ and His salvation."}],"previously":[],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Prologue","entries":[{"start":1,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is not merely a revelation that John experiences. This is a revelation that Jesus (God in the flesh, who had died and risen again, now ascended into Heaven with God the Father) has proven to John. Not only so, but an angel came to testify of those things that are to come (which we will see more than one angel come into the picture throughout this study, but only one angel is giving testimony and affirmation to John at this point)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Actually, this is a great reminder to the readers that angels have specific jobs from the Lord. Let me say it better… Angels have specific jobs from the LORD. Not from man. Man cannot dictate angels on what to do. Angels are not man’s messengers; they are God’s messengers. This is why we don’t pray to angels, worship angels, or recognize angels as saviors. Angels will do what God bids them, and that is to be respected and expected from us. It was to be respected by John as well, as we will see when we progress through these amazing chapters of Scripture."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"John mentions that this book is a “prophecy,” which insinuates a foretelling of what God has planned. It’s not something that has happened yet. Prophets of the Old Testament did the same thing when they were told to tell people about the things in which God told them were about to come if they didn’t change something quickly. Usually, the prophecies came true because of their disobedience (except for Nineveh when Jonah preached to them, and a few other examples)."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we think about the end of the world, the last thing we think of is being blessed. All things come to an end for eternity, so we know that those things here, on Earth, will eventually end, but those that have Christ will never end. This is why those that read and understand, and keep God’s Word, will be blessed."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":12,"title":"Greetings to the Seven Churches","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The one that was, and is, and is to come is a reference to Hebrews which reads:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus Christ the same yesterday, and to day, and for ever.","ref":"Hebrews 13:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is never changing, yet always changing us. This book is written to the churches of that day. They were not churches for far-future concepts; they were the churches that John contacted once before, and in John’s vision, he can use these seven churches as examples of the ways in which the church will change and grow (or shrink depending on the churches’ movement) over the years to come until the Lord returns."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You are not freed from sin by the church, nor by the pope or priests. You are not freed by your good deeds or works. You cannot free yourself through simply believing in God. You must come to the blood of Christ and allow it to wash away your sins. It’s the only thing that will suffice, for it’s the only thing that has the power to wash us clean."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Come now, and let us reason together, saith the Lord: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.","ref":"Isaiah 1:18"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We are “priests.” It’s not up to the pope or church to choose and decide who is holy enough and acceptable to God. God has chosen us in Him so that we are able to be righteous through His Son’s sacrifice. Otherwise, what was it for?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people; that ye should shew forth the praises of him who hath called you out of darkness into his marvellous light;","ref":"1 Peter 2:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye also, as lively stones, are built up a spiritual house, an holy priesthood, to offer up spiritual sacrifices, acceptable to God by Jesus Christ.","ref":"1 Peter 2:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"The pope is not the high priest."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now of the things which we have spoken this is the sum: We have such an high priest, who is set on the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in the heavens…For every high priest is ordained to offer gifts and sacrifices: wherefore it is of necessity that this man have somewhat also to offer.","ref":"Hebrews 8:1,3"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is recognized through the Mosaic law that whenever a high priest (or lead priest) died, another priest had to take this place (usually within the same family (though all of the Israelites were supposed to be priests…)). However, our High Priest, Jesus Christ, is not dead. He still lives! This means no priest can take His place and therefore (like the Israelites) everyone that is born of Him shall become believer priests with Him."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Even those who “pierced” Him will see Him. I assume they will see Him from eternity, either in heaven or hell. Those who have passed on will still see the coming of the Lord. This was already given to the disciples to be true."},{"kind":"para","text":"Luke writes about this himself, just as someone who simply believes the testimony of these saints. They were already promised by angels that Jesus was coming again in the same manner in which He ascended. They were going to see Him coming with the clouds, and it will be every eye that sees it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Which also said, Ye men of Galilee, why stand ye gazing up into heaven? This same Jesus, which is taken up from you into heaven, shall so come in like manner as ye have seen him go into heaven.","ref":"Acts 1:11"}]},{"start":8,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I know we have already mentioned it, but it’s a good reminder to us either way, especially when it’s Jesus that is speaking. Take every word of Christ seriously, because everything He says stands the test of time."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus Christ the same yesterday, and to day, and for ever.","ref":"Hebrews 13:8"}]}]},{"start":13,"end":20,"title":"Vision of the Son of Man","entries":[{"start":13,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Is it possible that the “son of man,” which is referred to here, be like the image of Christ, or just like a regular man? I believe it’s the image of Christ, for Christ referenced Himself often as the “Son of Man.”"}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s Word is sharper than a two-edged sword, and comes out of His own mouth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the word of God is quick, and powerful, and sharper than any twoedged sword, piercing even to the dividing asunder of soul and spirit, and of the joints and marrow, and is a discerner of the thoughts and intents of the heart.","ref":"Hebrews 4:12"}]},{"start":18,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ has the keys! Not Peter. Peter has the keys only because he believed that Christ was the Son of God. If we look at Matthew 16, we would see the real key that Peter is given is his faith in Jesus Christ being God."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Some say that Revelation is difficult to read, and so they try to avoid it at all costs. They come to it with defenses automatically up because they aren’t sure who is right and wrong in the interpretation of it. However, nothing is written that hadn’t been explained in some fashion or another. Some things you might need to use the rest of the Bible to fully grasp (which I’ve already warned about), but for the most part, it’s pretty easily understood and should not be a book that is too scary for Christians to go to and study."},{"kind":"para","text":"It should be scary to the Christian, however, to assume what scripture is saying without proving it."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20}],"verses":{"1":"The Revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave unto him, to shew unto his servants things which must shortly come to pass; and he sent and signified it by his angel unto his servant John:","2":"Who bare record of the word of God, and of the testimony of Jesus Christ, and of all things that he saw.","3":"Blessed is he that readeth, and they that hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein: for the time is at hand.","4":"John to the seven churches which are in Asia: Grace be unto you, and peace, from him which is, and which was, and which is to come; and from the seven Spirits which are before his throne;","5":"And from Jesus Christ, who is the faithful witness, and the first begotten of the dead, and the prince of the kings of the earth. Unto him that loved us, and washed us from our sins in his own blood,","6":"And hath made us kings and priests unto God and his Father; to him be glory and dominion for ever and ever. Amen.","7":"Behold, he cometh with clouds; and every eye shall see him, and they also which pierced him: and all kindreds of the earth shall wail because of him. Even so, Amen.","8":"I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the ending, saith the Lord, which is, and which was, and which is to come, the Almighty.","9":"I John, who also am your brother, and companion in tribulation, and in the kingdom and patience of Jesus Christ, was in the isle that is called Patmos, for the word of God, and for the testimony of Jesus Christ.","10":"I was in the Spirit on the Lord's day, and heard behind me a great voice, as of a trumpet,","11":"Saying, I am Alpha and Omega, the first and the last: and, What thou seest, write in a book, and send it unto the seven churches which are in Asia; unto Ephesus, and unto Smyrna, and unto Pergamos, and unto Thyatira, and unto Sardis, and unto Philadelphia, and unto Laodicea.","12":"And I turned to see the voice that spake with me. And being turned, I saw seven golden candlesticks;","13":"And in the midst of the seven candlesticks one like unto the Son of man, clothed with a garment down to the foot, and girt about the paps with a golden girdle.","14":"His head and his hairs were white like wool, as white as snow; and his eyes were as a flame of fire;","15":"And his feet like unto fine brass, as if they burned in a furnace; and his voice as the sound of many waters.","16":"And he had in his right hand seven stars: and out of his mouth went a sharp twoedged sword: and his countenance was as the sun shineth in his strength.","17":"And when I saw him, I fell at his feet as dead. And he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not; I am the first and the last:","18":"I am he that liveth, and was dead; and, behold, I am alive for evermore, Amen; and have the keys of hell and of death.","19":"Write the things which thou hast seen, and the things which are, and the things which shall be hereafter;","20":"The mystery of the seven stars which thou sawest in my right hand, and the seven golden candlesticks. The seven stars are the angels of the seven churches: and the seven candlesticks which thou sawest are the seven churches."}},
    "2": {"chapter":2,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 02"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: John receives a vision from the Lord, on the Lord’s Day, and the angel of the Lord has already shown John some pretty insane symbolism of the intensity and powerful cause of Jesus Christ towards His completion of the world and of life starting with the churches. He see’s Jesus between 7 candlesticks (probably on lampstands (which we were told was to represent “seven churches” in which John will be writing this letter too)), holding 7 stars in His hand (which Revelation 1:20 tells us is to represent the 7 angels of the seven churches)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now we come to this chapter which highlights the first 4 churches that John is writing this book too, what they are doing, and why it’s wrong, plus how to fix those specific things to be more fruitful, and to be righteous for the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"Churches, today, are still struggling like many of these churches mentioned in these next couple chapters, in the SAME WAY as these churches were suffering. It goes to show that sin is not generational, but it’s inevitable, and (even in the churches) we are going to see sin creep it’s way in and the Devil WILL trick even those that claim themselves to be Christians. But Christ has the fix. Christ has the turnaround."},{"kind":"para","text":"Let this also be noted, that when John mentions the “churches” throughout these chapters, he is referring to “the people” more specifically. Not a building, but a congregation. We (if we are Christians) are the church. We are not a building. When we preach to a crowd of 20 or 2,000, we are only preaching to ONE, because the assembly of believers are striving together with “one heart” and that’s the heart of Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the intro to each church, I will do my best to give a rundown about Christ’s statement to the church, what they were doing right, what they were doing wrong, how to get it right, what happens if they don’t get it right, and what happens when they do."}],"previously":[", John received a vision from the Lord on the Lord’s Day, and the angel of the Lord had already shown him some intense symbolism representing the power and cause of Jesus Christ towards His completion of the world and life, starting with the churches. He saw Jesus between seven candlesticks, likely on lampstands, which were said to represent the seven churches to which John would write this letter. Additionally, Jesus held seven stars in His hand, which Revelation 1:20 tells us represent the seven angels of the seven churches. Now, we come to this chapter, which highlights the first four churches to which John is writing this book, detailing what they are doing, why it is wrong, and how to fix those specific issues to be more fruitful and righteous for the Lord. Churches today are still struggling like many of these churches mentioned in the next few chapters, in the same way as these churches were suffering. This demonstrates that sin is not generational but inevitable, and even in the churches, we will see sin creep in, and the Devil will trick even those who claim to be Christians. However, Christ has the fix and the turnaround. It should also be noted that when John mentions the “churches” throughout these chapters, he is referring to “the people” more specifically, not a building but a congregation. We, if we are Christians, are the church. We are not a building. When we preach to a crowd of 20 or 2,000, we are only preaching to one, because the assembly of believers is striving together with “one heart,” and that is the heart of Christ. In the introduction to each church, I will do my best to provide a rundown of Christ’s statement to the church, what they were doing right, what they were doing wrong, how to get it right, what happens if they don’t get it right, and what happens when they do."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"The Church in Ephesus","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ to the church: Holds the seven stars in his right hand; walks among the seven golden candlesticks. Commendation: Doctrinal vigilance and endurance. Rebuke: Loss of first love. Solution: Remember, repent, and do the works done at first. Consequence of disobedience: Removal of their candlestick. Promise: Will be given the tree of life in paradise to eat."},{"kind":"para","text":"1 Unto the angel of the church of Ephesus write; These things saith he that holdeth the seven stars in his right hand, who walketh in the midst of the seven golden candlesticks;"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, the one that is speaking in this verse (telling John to write) is Jesus. These are the words of God. If you have a red-letter Bible, it may be easier to interpret that. I don’t have one currently, but it makes the most sense gathered from the previous verses equating to this one. Anytime Jesus speaks, it is wise for us to listen intently. Even if it’s in the form of a revelation."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ starts off by admonishing this church. This is a good thing to be said about a church. A church should stand strong in its doctrine and faith and be cautious towards anyone that would try and preach heresy or falsities opposed to the doctrine of the Bible in our generation and churches. A good leader will always point out, encourage, and admonish those that he leads. He wouldn’t only be the bearer of bad news, but would help those that are doing something that isn’t quite right by showing them love and acknowledging those things that they have already done right!"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Strength in difficult times is a lost commodity today. They are strong against false doctrine, but you hardly see any pushing against the cultural norms of homosexuality and genderism in our era. With that said, strength certainly is a virtue of patience, and I’d argue to say that without patience, you are as weak as they come. When this church labored, it was not through necessity, but it was through their hearts’ desire to preach against the falsities in the same way that Christ preached against it… with patience…"}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There was much to admonish this church over, but… they lacked in one very important area that many have crumbled under today. This is a MAJOR issue with this church age in which we live. We see some who are extremely zealous to fight against the cultural norms, stand up for truth and doctrine, and have courage during trying times, but those same few have no love for the Lord. They mean well, but they play the part of soldier in the Lord’s army. We have no room to hate our enemies. It goes against the mandates set for us through Christ, when we are literally commanded, by HIM, to LOVE our enemies and pray for them that hate us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you;","ref":"Matthew 5:44"},{"kind":"para","text":"This church may have shown patience and love towards others, but their hearts were not toward God. They may have shown a Christ-like attitude in their ministries, but they were not ministering for the Lord. There is a great deal of difference between working ministry for the people and working ministry for the Lord, and I have reason to believe that most ministers have gotten this mixed up and have fallen out of love with the Lord and His work."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In Matthew, Jesus tells us we are light, and we must LET our light SHINE before the entire world."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.","ref":"Matthew 5:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Churches are to be lighthouses for the Lord and His people. They are to glow as a beacon of safety to a hurt and dying world. They are to represent comfort and love for the lost and be a safe haven for Christians to establish their faith, prepare their artillery, and go back out into the world of spiritual warfare, continuing to fight on. It’s a place of refreshing, equipping, and caring. May our churches resemble such today."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve seen many churches fall apart because they have not repented and gone back to the love of Christ. They are accustomed to traditions or feel forced into ministry by necessity, when the only thing that is necessary for Christ is preaching the gospel. Ministry is not just necessary; it’s important! We must understand that ministry without love is damnable heresy, and Jesus will remove a “candlestick” (or lighthouse as I’ve mentioned) when it’s not fixed or taken care of. The lighthouse may still stand, but the light will no longer shine… What a sad sight for the lighthouse to exist and not do what it was designed for…"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Nicolaitans were a somewhat unknown heretical group. They seduced God’s people to participate in idolatry and sexual immorality (as we will soon read). They have presented immorality as freedom in Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"All things are lawful unto me, but all things are not expedient: all things are lawful for me, but I will not be brought under the power of any. Meats for the belly, and the belly for meats: but God shall destroy both it and them. Now the body is not for fornication, but for the Lord; and the Lord for the body. And God hath both raised up the Lord, and will also raise up us by his own power. Know ye not that your bodies are the members of Christ? shall I then take the members of Christ, and make them the members of an harlot? God forbid. What? know ye not that he which is joined to an harlot is one body? for two, saith he, shall be one flesh. But he that is joined unto the Lord is one spirit. Flee fornication. Every sin that a man doeth is without the body; but he that committeth fornication sinneth against his own body. What? know ye not that your body is the temple of the Holy Ghost which is in you, which ye have of God, and ye are not your own? For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God's.","ref":"1 Corinthians 6:12-20"}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This tree isn’t to be mistaken for Genesis’ tree of the knowledge of good and evil. This tree was a tree that offered eternal life to pure bodies. Once humanity fell, all access to it was banned, and it then reappears in the new Jerusalem (or heaven, if you will (spoiler alert))."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the LORD God said, Behold, the man is become as one of us, to know good and evil: and now, lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever: Therefore the LORD God sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken. So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.","ref":"Genesis 3:22-24"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of God and of the Lamb. In the midst of the street of it, and on either side of the river, was there the tree of life, which bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month: and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.","ref":"Revelation 22:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, we will talk more about that in the last chapter of this book, but as you can tell, everything in Revelation intertwines together. We know that those that put their faith and trust in Christ are offered eternal life."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.","ref":"Romans 6:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"They have eaten from the “tree (as Christ would call Himself the vine)” and are then granted eternal life for good from that moment, forever."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":11,"title":"The Church in Smyrna","entries":[{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ to the church: The first and last, who died and came to life. Commendation: Spiritually rich, enduring persecution. Rebuke: There was none… Solution: Be faithful unto death. Consequence of disobedience: None, they were faithful… Promise: Will be given the crown of life and will not be hurt by the second death."},{"kind":"para","text":"8 And unto the angel of the church in Smyrna write; These things saith the first and the last, which was dead, and is alive; 9 I know thy works, and tribulation, and poverty, (but thou art rich) and I know the blasphemy of them which say they are Jews, and are not, but are the synagogue of Satan. 10 Fear none of those things which thou shalt suffer: behold, the devil shall cast some of you into prison, that ye may be tried; and ye shall have tribulation ten days: be thou faithful unto death, and I will give thee a crown of life. 11 He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; He that overcometh shall not be hurt of the second death."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, this church in Smyrna was doing things well. They were being mistreated during this time by the Roman government, as most churches were, and the Romans were trying to find any reason possible to destroy this church in heinous and (sometimes) inhumane ways. However, this church remained faithful even through great tribulations."},{"kind":"para","text":"Churches that remain faithful through great trials and testing are stronger than any churches with thousands of members sitting comfortably. Give me a church that’s been through major grief, still continuing to strive for the love of Christ, and I guarantee you will see God’s blessings upon it. You will meet some of the strongest, gentlest Christians in the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"The crown of life is not a gift solemnly given to us. Though we may receive these crowns for things that we have achieved in this life, those crowns give us access to the one that truly deserves it. For without Him, we would not be worthy to receive such amazing heavenly rewards. Those crowns belong to Him, and it’s why we will lay them down at His feet when we enter eternity."}]}]},{"start":12,"end":17,"title":"The Church in Pergamum","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ to the church: Has the sharp two-edged sword. Commendation: Holding fast Christ’s name, not denying their faith. Rebuke: False teaching. Solution: Repent, and stop teaching false doctrine. Consequence for disobedience: War against them with the sword of Christ’s mouth (His Word). Promise: Will be given hidden manna and a white stone with a new name on it."},{"kind":"para","text":"12 And to the angel of the church in Pergamos write; These things saith he which hath the sharp sword with two edges;"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Word of God is sharper than a two-edged sword, but it’s a good idea to make sure you are behind the blade cutting, rather than being cut. His Word can wound, and it can heal. Let us be dividing the word in such a way that wounds and heals at the same time. Tearing down and building up. One without the other is hazardous."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The reason that Pergamum is labeled “Satan’s seat” is because they made temples that were dedicated to worshipping false idols. They had a temple for Augustus and Roma, one for Asklepios (the god of healing), and even an altar dedicated to Zeus. But in the middle of all of this false worship, a believer named Antipas came to tell them the truth of Christ and God’s Word. When they heard this, apparently they killed him because they didn’t want to stop worshipping their false gods that made them feel good about themselves. But he (Antipas) was labeled as a “faithful witness.”"}]},{"start":14,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Balaam was an Old Testament prophet who advised Moab’s king to tempt Israel into sexual and spiritual adultery."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Israel abode in Shittim, and the people began to commit whoredom with the daughters of Moab. And they called the people unto the sacrifices of their gods: and the people did eat, and bowed down to their gods.","ref":"Numbers 25:1-2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, these caused the children of Israel, through the counsel of Balaam, to commit trespass against the LORD in the matter of Peor, and there was a plague among the congregation of the LORD.","ref":"Numbers 31:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, the Nicolaitans were causing others to dip into this same model of worship. Christ points out that the church, here, is allowing such practices to start infecting the congregation. This is why He has a few things against them. God takes note of all church leadership and doctrine. If you are teaching falsities or you are not filled with His Spirit, God will not leave that unchecked, and He will not allow you to do it without conviction."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine being a church that loves the Lord and is surrounded by idolatry. You find it difficult to connect with the culture because they do not believe in the God you are teaching, which you believe is the true God. In an attempt to make others feel more comfortable, you decide to incorporate some of the beliefs from other churches. However, the problem is that a church is not a house for “other people’s beliefs.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"The church is a place where people go to worship the God of the Bible and the God of the Bible only. It is a place that Jesus died for, not so that we can incorporate beliefs, but so that we can worship His death and resurrection. Jesus is justified in threatening this church for their falsities, and any churches that would practice such disgraceful worship. The church should never take lightly the threatening of the Lord."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For this cause many are weak and sickly among you, and many sleep. For if we would judge ourselves, we should not be judged. But when we are judged, we are chastened of the Lord, that we should not be condemned with the world.","ref":"1 Corinthians 11:30-32"}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Just like God gave manna to Israel in the wilderness, Christ supplies hidden manna to those who conquer. I picture this church allowing false worship into their doors simply because it meant they could survive in a land that was trying to snuff out their worship. They weren’t reliant on Christ’s provision. A white stone was given to winners of athletic contests to gain entrance to banquets. White stones were (supposedly) used by jurors to vote for acquittal as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"These are obviously rewards of eternal blessings! The new name is given to every believer who trusts in Christ alone, for salvation alone, and doesn’t worship anyone but God alone. We can sing with the hosts of heaven, “There’s a new name written down in glory, and it’s mine. O, yes, it’s mine.” Christ gives His believers a new name. Though people may have always known you by that name, when you become saved, your name changes drastically. It’s no longer associated with the sins of your past. It’s associated with “bible thumper” and “Jesus freak.” Which, to me, is far better than “liar” or “fornicator.” We should desire a new name, and when we trust Christ, He gives it to us. All things are new."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For whom he did foreknow, he also did predestinate to be conformed to the image of his Son, that he might be the firstborn among many brethren.","ref":"Romans 8:29"}]}]},{"start":18,"end":29,"title":"The Church in Thyatira","entries":[{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ to the church: Has eyes like a flame of fire, feet like burnished bronze. Commendation: Growing love, evidenced in deeds of service. Rebuke: Lack of discernment, toleration of heresy. Solution: Hold fast and keep Christ’s works until the end. Consequences of disobedience: Each given as their works deserve. Promise: Will be given the morning star and authority over the nations."},{"kind":"para","text":"18 And unto the angel of the church in Thyatira write; These things saith the Son of God, who hath his eyes like unto a flame of fire, and his feet are like fine brass; 19 I know thy works, and charity, and service, and faith, and thy patience, and thy works; and the last to be more than the first. 20 Notwithstanding I have a few things against thee, because thou sufferest that woman Jezebel, which calleth herself a prophetess, to teach and to seduce my servants to commit fornication, and to eat things sacrificed unto idols."},{"kind":"para","text":"May it be noticed that these churches seemed to be doing things that were pleasing to the Lord. Every single one of them had good things said about them, but they were ruining all of those good things because of a sin they were committing against Him as well. They started off strong and then turned away to idols and false doctrine."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, nothing has changed in the church house today. We have so many different branches of each religion because the same problems still persist and will persist when the end of times (as we know it) comes."},{"kind":"para","text":"21 And I gave her space to repent of her fornication; and she repented not. 22 Behold, I will cast her into a bed, and them that commit adultery with her into great tribulation, except they repent of their deeds. 23 And I will kill her children with death; and all the churches shall know that I am he which searcheth the reins and hearts: and I will give unto every one of you according to your works."},{"kind":"para","text":"The children spoken of here are not blood-related. Her children represent those she has influenced. Just as John calls his churches his “children” through the faith of God (or Paul calls Timothy his son, or Peter calls Mark his son…), because they were taught and brought up by John’s faith and witness, Jezebel is claiming the same name. However, she is teaching them false doctrines and abusing the people at church for sexual gain."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, this too is a common problem in churches today. We see many pastors, youth workers, and priests alike using the church for sexual gain rather than pointing people to Christ. The house of God is established as a holy sanctuary of worship. We must be zealous about the house of God to keep it that way. And when we see something that is not right happening in God’s house, we must have the same righteous anger as Christ did."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Jesus went into the temple of God, and cast out all them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves, And said unto them, It is written, My house shall be called the house of prayer; but ye have made it a den of thieves.","ref":"Matthew 21:12-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s house suffers from the thieves that fill their pockets today. The desire for a paycheck rather than desiring to preach, teach, and minister. Preaching is all part of it, but simply because the church is paying him. How I wish and long that the ministers saw the church in the proper light."},{"kind":"para","text":"24 But unto you I say, and unto the rest in Thyatira, as many as have not this doctrine, and which have not known the depths of Satan, as they speak; I will put upon you none other burden."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ knows they have enough problems to deal with, and Christ will give them the power to deal with those problems. Extra burdens are given to those that are not focused on the right thing (that being Christ)."},{"kind":"para","text":"25 But that which ye have already hold fast till I come."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s a wild ride. Christ has supplied us with our needs. He is telling us to “hold fast” to those things that are already given to us through Him. Hold fast… I love those two words. God uses the term “hold fast” a lot through His book, and it’s wise to listen to those things which are repeated…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Prove all things; hold fast to that which is good.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 5:21"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let us hold fast the profession of our faith without wavering; (for he is faithful that promised;)","ref":"Hebrews 10:23"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Take fast hold of instruction; let her not go: keep her; for she is thy life.","ref":"Proverbs 4:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My righteousness I hold fast, and will not let it go: my heart shall not reproach me so long as I live.","ref":"Job 27:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Hold fast the form of sound words, which thou hast heard of me, in faith and love which is in Christ Jesus.","ref":"2 Timothy 1:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Seeing then that we have a great high priest, that is passed into the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us hold fast our profession.","ref":"Hebrews 4:14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But Christ as a son over his own house; whose house are we, if we hold fast the confidence and the rejoicing of the hope firm unto the end.","ref":"Hebrews 3:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"Hold fast to sound teaching, to true doctrine, to proven things. Hold fast to that which is good, pure, and right. Hold fast to faith, to preaching, to reading, and exhorting. Hold fast to prayer, fellowship, and love. Hold fast to it until we see Christ return!"},{"kind":"para","text":"26 And he that overcometh, and keepeth my works unto the end, to him will I give power over the nations: 27 And he shall rule them with a rod of iron; as the vessels of a potter shall they be broken to shivers: even as I received of my Father. 28 And I will give him the morning star."},{"kind":"para","text":"The morning star is Christ. He is ruler and rescuer. He was predicted to rise by Balaam."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I shall see him, but not now: I shall behold him, but not nigh: there shall come a Star out of Jacob, and a Sceptre shall rise out of Israel, and shall smite the corners of Moab, and destroy all the children of Sheth.","ref":"Numbers 24:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus will also clarify that He is the morning star in the last chapter of Revelation. Those who conquer the trials and false doctrines are promised everything about Christ. It’s promised to these people in these churches, but we, too, get to read these accounts and take these promises upon ourselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must endure false teaching, false religions, and false ideologies of modern culture that try their hardest to sway people away from the church. Though many churches suffer from false preaching and doctrine, there are some who don’t, and those in the church who know the truth must take charge in leading others in the same truth, “holding fast” to the words of Christ. The Bible is a book of salvation. Through its words, page after page, you will not find anything but the salvation of the Lord. You will see God save, and those who are saved receive the morning star; they receive Christ. Those who keep to God’s Word alone as instruction and hold this whole book in high reverence will be able to stand strong in the last days."},{"kind":"para","text":"29 He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we have ears to hear these things, then there is no reason we should not be taking them to heart and following through with them."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.","ref":"James 1:22"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18}],"verses":{"2":"I know thy works, and thy labour, and thy patience, and how thou canst not bear them which are evil: and thou hast tried them which say they are apostles, and are not, and hast found them liars:","3":"And hast borne, and hast patience, and for my name's sake hast laboured, and hast not fainted.","4":"Nevertheless I have somewhat against thee, because thou hast left thy first love.","5":"Remember therefore from whence thou art fallen, and repent, and do the first works; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will remove thy candlestick out of his place, except thou repent.","6":"But this thou hast, that thou hatest the deeds of the Nicolaitans, which I also hate.","7":"He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of God.","13":"I know thy works, and where thou dwellest, even where Satan's seat is: and thou holdest fast my name, and hast not denied my faith, even in those days wherein Antipas was my faithful martyr, who was slain among you, where Satan dwelleth.","14":"But I have a few things against thee, because thou hast there them that hold the doctrine of Balaam, who taught Balac to cast a stumblingblock before the children of Israel, to eat things sacrificed unto idols, and to commit fornication.","15":"So hast thou also them that hold the doctrine of the Nicolaitans, which thing I hate.","16":"Repent; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will fight against them with the sword of my mouth.","17":"He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the hidden manna, and will give him a white stone, and in the stone a new name written, which no man knoweth saving he that receiveth it."}},
    "3": {"chapter":3,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 03"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: We last saw Jesus tell John to write some help to seven churches which were mentioned in the first chapter. John was able to write to the first four churches with some of the commendations, and some of the problems, how they can be fixed and what happens if they aren’t fixed."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now John finishes up this chapter by writing to the last three of the prominent church types of that day. Please don’t hate me for coming off too Calvinistic in this particular chapter… I would prefer not to be tied into that category, but there’s certainly a lot of areas that I tend to agree with more, and that’s just the title that was given to it."}],"previously":["We last saw Jesus tell John to write some help to seven churches which were mentioned in the first chapter. John was able to write to the first four churches with some of the commendations, and some of the problems, how they can be fixed, and what happens if they aren’t fixed. Now John finishes up this chapter by writing to the last three of the prominent church types of that day. Please don’t hate me for coming off too Calvinistic in this particular chapter… I would prefer not to be tied into that category, but there’s certainly a lot of areas that I tend to agree with more, and that’s just the title that was given to it."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":6,"title":"To The Church in Sardis","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ to the church: Has the seven spirits of God and the seven stars. Commendation: A few remain pure and loyal. Rebuke: Dead works. Solution: Keep the Word and Repent. Consequence of disobedience: Christ will come like a thief. Promise: They will be clothed with white garments; name never blotted out of the book of Life; name confessed before God and angels."},{"kind":"para","text":"1 And unto the angel of the church in Sardis write; These things saith he that hath the seven Spirits of God, and the seven stars; I know thy works, that thou hast a name that thou livest, and art dead."},{"kind":"para","text":"The number “seven” always attributes to the all-powerful God. Seven is known to be “God’s lucky number” to some scholars and is seen throughout much of His Word always representing His love and power for us. The number “seven” attributes “perfection” or “completeness.” We know that the Holy Spirit is one person."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"There is one body, and one Spirit, even as ye are called in one hope of your calling; One Lord, one faith, One God and Father of all, who is above all, and through all, and in you all.","ref":"Ephesians 4:4-6"},{"kind":"para","text":"But we see that John often reveres God’s completeness with the number “seven.” We will see this several (no pun intended) times through Revelation with depictions like “seven torches of fire,” or “seven eyes.” These descriptions are supposed to show God as all-powerful and all-knowing, tried and tested seven times through, and proven continuously. I will not spend much time on the symbolism of numbers, but I will reference a few thoughts as we proceed."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This church is close to death and may never experience revival unless they allow Christ to revive them. We, too, can experience this same style of revival in our spirits and bodies if we would just let Christ revive us. We are close to death, but Christ is giving us a chance to take His Spirit of revival to start fresh and build stronger."},{"kind":"para","text":"God frequently gives us commands through His Word: be watchful, be vigilant, be sober, be on guard, be ready. A church that isn’t anticipating the Lord’s Word and Will is not a church that is ready for the Lord’s use."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"You cannot lay hold on Jesus being a sinner. When we think of being robbed, or we think of someone being a thief, we think of them as the bad guy. But Jesus has every right to allow a church that doesn’t show forth His faith and love to die. He has every right to steal the life of that church so that it doesn’t continue on to destroy more lives. This term for thief is used several times in the New Testament."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And this know, that if the goodman of the house had known what hour the thief would come, he would have watched, and not have suffered his house to be broken through. Be ye therefore ready also: for the Son of man cometh at an hour when ye think not.","ref":"Luke 12:39-40"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For yourselves know perfectly that the day of the Lord so cometh as a thief in the night. For when they shall say, Peace and safety; then sudden destruction cometh upon them, as travail upon a woman with child; and they shall not escape. But ye, brethren, are not in darkness, that that day should overtake you as a thief.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 5:2-4"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the day of the Lord will come as a thief in the night; in the which the heavens shall pass away with a great noise, and the elements shall melt with fervent heat, the earth also and the works that are therein shall be burned up.","ref":"2 Peter 3:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus only robs those that are not prepared for Him. Those that feel robbed never actually knew the value of their eternity. They never actually thought they would be robbed of it… How sad of a thought if this is said about the church we attend. How scary it would be if we were involved with a near-death church that just simply won’t turn to Christ in faith and assurance. How miserable we would be for not loving Christ while we have the chance to."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"John usually writes extremely encouraging and informational letters, but this letter is obviously inspired because John is not exactly using the same terms as “little children” for these people in the church. Jesus is clearly giving fair warning to the churches to act up and start using the church as a church, rather than a pedestal."},{"kind":"para","text":"There will be a “few” names that are there that will know better, but a few and many are far apart from each other. If Christ won’t have many, may we be one of the few."}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I won’t get too far into the meaning of “the book of life” and our names being “blotted out.” But I will say, I don’t believe that Jesus will blot ANY names from the book of Life at this juncture. I believe that God knew from the beginning who would be saved, wrote their names down, and it was secured ever since then."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And all that dwell upon the earth shall worship him, whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world.","ref":"Revelation 13:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"According as he hath chosen us in him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blame before him in love: Having predestinated us unto the adoption of children by Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will,","ref":"Ephesians 1:4-5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For whom he did foreknow, he also did predestinate to be conformed to the image of his Son, that he might be the firstborn among many brethren.","ref":"Romans 8:29"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,","ref":"1 Peter 1:20"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom also we have obtained an inheritance, being predestinated according to the purpose of him who worketh all things after the counsel of his own will:","ref":"Ephesians 1:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"The list goes on… I believe our God is wise enough, smart enough, powerful enough, and organized enough to know all things, all the time, for all of eternity. He plans each and every step of every single organism, person, and purpose throughout the oracles of our timeline and beyond. He can do that and know this because He doesn’t bend to our perception of time and space."},{"kind":"para","text":"Then there are those who believe that God puts our names down into the book of life after salvation. There is merit to accepting this idea as well, which would rule out the idea that God can, and will, take your name out of the “Book of Life.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the LORD said unto Moses, Whosoever hath sinned against me, him will I blot out of my book","ref":"Exodus 32:33"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let them be blotted out of the book of the living, and not be written with the righteous.","ref":"Psalm 69:28"},{"kind":"para","text":"These verses would attest to an idea or notion (rather) of “righteous anger.” Being so upset with someone or others that you pray for their names to be LITERALLY taken out of the book of life. I believe that Jesus would never remove our names, but I also believe that He has the right and power to do so as well. Our God is not limited to our idea of justice and righteousness. Our access to heaven does not rely on our desire for moral acceptance. It’s all up to God. He saves US, not the other way around."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise,","ref":"Ephesians 1:13"}]}]},{"start":7,"end":13,"title":"To The Church in Philadelphia","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ to the church: The holy one, the true one, who has the keys of David. Commendation: Patiently enduring, keeping God’s word and not denying His name. Rebuke: None Solution: Continue to hold fast to what they have. Consequence of disobedience: None, they seem to desire to obey. Promise: Will be made a pillar in the temple of God, inscribed with the names of God, promised the New Jerusalem, and Christ Himself."},{"kind":"para","text":"7 And to the angel of the church in Philadelphia write; These things saith he that is holy, he that is true, he that hath the key of David, he that openeth, and no man shutteth; and shutteth, and no man openeth;"},{"kind":"para","text":"Further addressing the implication of foreknowledge and predestination, this term for “key of David” gives reference to the fact that Christ has absolute authority to admit or exclude anyone He pleases from God’s kingdom."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the key of the house of David will I lay upon his shoulder; so he shall open, and none shall shut; and he shall shut, and none shall open.","ref":"Isaiah 22:22"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.","ref":"Matthew 16:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"SIDENOTE: Can I also just say, as this verse suggests, that Christ is able to open doors that no one can shut, and close doors that no one can open? Some have said that you can force open opportunities from the Lord that you won’t necessarily like. They told this to me when I had the call to ministry before moving to Texas. We CANNOT overpower Christ’s calling or opening for the Christian. He has all-power. This verse insinuates that it would be impossible for us to close the doors He opens, and open the doors He closes, for He controls all things, and it should be desirous for us that He do so."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For a great door and effectual is opened unto me, and there are many adversaries.","ref":"1 Corinthians 16:9"}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obedience to God does not mean power and strength. Obedience to God means blessings and usefulness. You can have little strength, and still have strong faith. Physical gain can never replace spiritual growth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore I take pleasure in infirmities, in reproaches, in necessities, in persecutions, in distresses for Christ’s sake: for when I am weak, then am I strong.","ref":"2 Corinthians 12:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Our weakness is the only way to receive God’s strength."}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The key to Christian ministry is patience and endurance. If you do not have that type of spirit, don’t minister."}]},{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Pillars of the faith are getting harder to find every day. We see so much of the world crumble under the pressure of society, and they leave truth and right behind to just appease the masses because they are tired of fighting, and they don’t desire to cause disunity. I’m sorry, but if you have to lie and cheat and steal to keep unity, then you don’t need to unite with people who are not okay with that. It’s better to be alone, pure, and living for God than to be miserable, unfaithful, and untrustworthy living with the world."}]}]},{"start":14,"end":22,"title":"To The Church in Laodicea","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Christ to the church: The Amen, the faithful and true witness, the beginning of God’s creation. Commendation: None (Scary thought, not one nice thing to say about this church). Rebuke: Spiritually blind, bankrupt, naked, lukewarm. Solution: Buy gold, white garments, and salve from Christ; be zealous and repent. Consequence for disobedience: Will be spit out of Christ’s mouth. Promise: Will dine with Christ; will be granted to sit with Christ on His throne."},{"kind":"para","text":"14 And unto the angel of the church of the Laodiceans write; These things saith the Amen, the faithful and true witness, the beginning of the creation of God; 15 I know thy works, that thou art neither cold nor hot: I would thou wert cold or hot."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Laodiceans were a somewhat wealthy city, serving as the center of all imports and commercial gain. They had plenty of medical and textile supplies that were traded in neighboring cities. They were well-to-do and extremely rich, yet Jesus found nothing of value in it."},{"kind":"para","text":"America has become very rich in the resources we have accumulated. However, due to our lack of faith in the Lord, Jesus may picture our country in a lot of the same ways."},{"kind":"para","text":"16 So then because thou art lukewarm, and neither cold nor hot, I will spue thee out of my mouth."},{"kind":"para","text":"I love cold water and enjoy cold drinks in general. I know that if my wife were to get me a drink on a hot summer’s day and tell me that it was cold, but it was lukewarm or room temperature, I would probably hate that. I would desire to spit it out and pop the bottle in the fridge."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now, there are special occasions when I like hot drinks more than cold. I enjoy hot coffee or hot chocolate on a cold day. I also enjoy hot soup. Imagine going to drink your “hot” coffee, chocolate, or soup and finding it room temperature or lukewarm. It is not nearly as enjoyable. I’d have a harder time finishing these things."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus doesn’t like His church to be lukewarm. He doesn’t like them to just call themselves “Christians” but not actually do anything that is “Christ-like.” He wants them to either be Christ-like or not be part of Christ at all. He’s disgusted by middle-of-the-road religionists. He’s not looking for a church that wavers on every issue of the world to try and please the masses. Nobody likes a church that wavers. Either stand strong in your convictions and proven truth or back down from the church. We can’t afford people to enter into spiritual warfare without knowing which side they want to be on. Friendly fire is the real issue with Christianity today, and it’s always caused by lukewarm Christians."},{"kind":"para","text":"17 Because thou sayest, I am rich, and increased with goods, and have need of nothing; and knowest not that thou art wretched, and miserable, and poor, and blind, and naked:"},{"kind":"para","text":"You can have everything in this world, but still have nothing if you don’t have Christ. The worst kind of pride is one that thinks it’s better off without the help of the Lord. A rich pig is still a pig. You can give the pig as much money as you want, and dress him in the nicest set of clothes you can dream possible, give him a fancy little hat and monocle if you’d like, but in the end it’s still a pig, and it will only do pig things."},{"kind":"para","text":"18 I counsel thee to buy of me gold tried in the fire, that thou mayest be rich; and white raiment, that thou mayest be clothed, and that the shame of thy nakedness do not appear; and anoint thine eyes with eyesalve, that thou mayest see."},{"kind":"para","text":"Only God can provide those things that are truly fulfilling. Anything we achieve on our own is but a flimsy stick compared to the mighty sword God can give you. And God will provide every means possible to give you what you need so that you cannot ever blame Him for not being there. He desires all to know Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"19 As many as I love, I rebuke and chasten: be zealous therefore, and repent."},{"kind":"para","text":"If God is correcting you, it’s simply because He loves you. I would worry if He doesn’t correct you."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If ye endure chastening, God dealeth with you as with sons; for what son is he whom the father chasteneth not? But if ye be without chastisement, whereof all are partakers, then are ye bastards, and not sons.","ref":"Hebrews 12:7-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Take this personally… Be zealous and repent. Love God more and repent for not trusting Him. Pray more and repent for not praying. Study more and repent for not studying. Please God more and repent for pleasing yourself."},{"kind":"para","text":"20 Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me."},{"kind":"para","text":"The invitation to accept Christ is still available, but there will be a day when He stops knocking. No man should wait until that day, for it will be too late. Accept Him now, while you still have time."},{"kind":"para","text":"21 To him that overcometh will I grant to sit with me in my throne, even as I also overcame, and am set down with my Father in his throne."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ implies that He will allow some ruling authority to His people. We will not sit idly in Heaven. Christ will have jobs for us to do, and when we are faithful to Him now, we will have greater authority when we get to eternity."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said unto him, Well, thou good servant: because thou has been faithful in a very little, have thou authority over ten cities.","ref":"Luke 19:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Know ye not that we shall judge angels? How much more things that pertain to this life?","ref":"1 Corinthians 6:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If we suffer, we shall also reign with him: if we deny him, he also will deny us:","ref":"2 Timothy 2:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"22 He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches."},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ reminds us once again to listen and pay attention. He reminds us that those that have an ear will hear. Only those that know Him, love Him, serve Him, and desire to glorify Him will have ears to hear His words in the proper light and context."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14}],"verses":{"2":"Be watchful, and strengthen the things which remain, that are ready to die: for I have not found thy works perfect before God.","3":"Remember therefore how thou hast received and heard, and hold fast, and repent. If therefore thou shalt not watch, I will come on thee as a thief, and thou shalt not know what hour I will come upon thee.","4":"Thou hast a few names even in Sardis which have not defiled their garments; and they shall walk with me in white: for they are worthy.","5":"He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.","6":"He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches.","8":"I know thy works: behold, I have set before thee an open door, and no man can shut it: for thou hast a little strength, and hast kept my word, and hast not denied my name.","9":"Behold, I will make them of the synagogue of Satan, which say they are Jews, and are not, but do lie; behold, I will make them to come and worship before thy feet, and to know that I have loved thee.","10":"Because thou hast kept the word of my patience, I also will keep thee from the hour of temptation, which shall come upon all the world, to try them that dwell upon the earth.","11":"Behold, I come quickly: hold that fast which thou hast, that no man take thy crown.","12":"Him that overcometh will I make a pillar in the temple of my God, and he shall go no more out: and I will write upon him the name of my God, and the name of the city of my God, which is new Jerusalem, which cometh down out of heaven from my God: and I will write upon him my new name.","13":"He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches."}},
    "4": {"chapter":4,"intro":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved.","ref":"Romans 10:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the pattern of salvation. Grace is also one of God’s patterns. A person that repents (even those that are saved) will receive a gift of grace towards those that truly understand how sick and disgusting their sins are and turn from them. God’s mercy is displayed, and we understand we don’t deserve it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.","ref":"James 4:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"Trials are a part of God’s pattern:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That the trial of your faith, being much more precious than gold that perisheth, though it be tried with fire, might be found unto praise and honor and glory at the appearing of Jesus Christ:","ref":"1 Peter 1:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus’ continuous prayers are a pattern:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who is he that condemneth? It is Christ that died, yea rather, that is risen again, who is even at the right hand of God, who also maketh intercession for us.","ref":"Romans 8:34"},{"kind":"para","text":"I could go on… Satan has patterns too, to try and mimic God or try and subtract from God’s patterns. His patterns are always opposite of God’s. His pattern is to destroy:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.","ref":"John 8:44"},{"kind":"para","text":"His pattern is to deceive:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.","ref":"Revelation 12:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"His pattern is to confuse:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom the god of this world hath blinded the minds of them which believe not, lest the light of the glorious gospel of Christ, who is the image of God, should shine unto them.","ref":"2 Corinthians 4:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"Sadly, many of us tend to pull towards the patterns of Satan than we do the patterns of God. So it’s safe to say that the events taking place in this particular chapter (as John is seeing them) are things that are currently taking place in Heaven. With that said, there are things in this that may be hard to understand in regards to our more modern vernacular. Not many of us know what a “Jasper” or “Sardine” stone is, and why it’s important."},{"kind":"para","text":"Hopefully through this study, as we look at this, we will see some patterns that God has laid out for us throughout the generations, and use them to develop a more strategic and careful consideration to what God would have us to do in this life."}],"previously":["We get the sight of how the churches of John’s time had been going, and they (honestly) aren’t much different than how many churches today are going. Jesus is warning these churches that if they continue this way, then these coming events which we will read about in this chapter will unfold. It’s no wonder why they will unfold when the church has gone back into the sins that Jesus has been warning about. In this chapter (though it’s short), there is quite a lot for us to take in. We must remember the background of this particular book here, and remember that this was also a vision of things to come. Whether or not the things that are mentioned in this particular chapter were in the present or in the future is not fully disclosed, but we can assume that the things taking place here are more than likely continual and repetitive. I homeschool my daughter, and one of the things she has learned recently is about the different seasons of the year. We talked in depth about weather patterns, why it gets colder or hotter in certain parts of the year, what a leap year is, the purpose for time change and day/night cycles. We had a project that was due for her school that had to explain how this works. I used a flashlight and a few Styrofoam balls to show how it would work. God has a pattern that is extremely easy to follow. Salvation has a pattern, which is to understand you are a sinner in need of a Savior, place your faith in Jesus Christ, and (after salvation) repent from your sin."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":11,"title":"The Throne of Heaven","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I am going to split this first verse up (something I don’t do very often) simply because there’s a lot to explore here."},{"kind":"para","text":"1 After this I looked, and, behold, a door was opened in heaven…"},{"kind":"para","text":"In the last chapter, we are told by Jesus that he will open a door…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I know thy works: behold, I have set before thee an open door, and no man can shut it: for thou hast a little strength, and hast kept my word, and hast not denied my name.","ref":"Revelation 3:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the key of the house of David will I lay upon his shoulder; so he shall open, and none shall shut; and he shall shut, and none shall open.","ref":"Isaiah 22:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a great reminder to us that the things that are about to take place, and the future in which God has planned for humanity, is not something we can control. Like the thought of the COVID pandemic in our age, the world’s pandemic that this book will speak about will be far bigger, greater, and scarier. It will be something that we won’t be able to handle without God. But God has promised that if a door is opened, no one can shut it. It’s something that needs to happen simply because of the sin nature in which we find ourselves and how much worse it is going to get."},{"kind":"para","text":"…and the first voice which I heard was as it were of a trumpet talking with me;…"},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t know about you, but a voice like a trumpet talking to me would be… interesting… It would be something very loud, no doubt, and I imagine it would be long-winded or seemingly powerful. It’s understood that the voice that is speaking is more than likely an angel of some sort. This is the assumption we will go with, for these words are not written in red like our previous chapter to indicate that it’s Christ speaking at this particular moment."},{"kind":"para","text":"We could also indicate that this is the “last trumpet” that will sound. But that’s a discussion for a later chapter."},{"kind":"para","text":"…which said, Come up hither, and I will shew thee things which must be hereafter."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is wise to listen to the people of God in regards to the future. We see time after time when people ignored the prophets of the Old Testament and faced extreme consequences for doing so. Now John (a disciple of Jesus Christ, one who cannot lie, and anyone who is in Christ cannot lie, and can only mimic what Paul says:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I say the truth in Christ, I lie not, my conscience also bearing me witness in the Holy Ghost.","ref":"Romans 9:1)"},{"kind":"para","text":"John was receiving instructions (from the Lord specifically) to write down everything he was about to see, and it wasn’t simply so John could have an account of what had just happened. These writings were meant for the future of the church. These writings were meant for us to behold ourselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"God reveals things to people through His Word today so that we are warned, and are able to follow the correct doctrine without wavering. In fact, I’d argue to say that this book couldn’t be any more perfect if we tried to edit it ourselves (actually, we would probably ruin it if we tried to edit and change it; some translators have done this for us already, giving proof to that fact). The New Testament scripture is extremely important to this generation. Jesus spoke nearly the same words here in John’s gospel as well, if you don’t remember:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"…and he [the spirit] will shew you things to come.","ref":"John 16:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even Peter himself gave praise and significance to the New Testament teachings, and how important and secure they were for the modern-day Christians to follow. He gave credence to the fact that these words were proven and tried. Credence to the idea that we can dwell in confidence with what the complete word of God says. Credence to the simple stance that this was now complete. God’s Word, from Genesis to Revelation, is flawless and undeniably perfect."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"We have also a more sure word of prophecy; where unto ye do well that ye take heed, as unto a light that shineth in a dark place, until the day dawn, and the day star arise in your hearts:","ref":"2 Peter 1:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"The voice in this chapter is surely something to behold, and John had a perfect chance to hear it. My guess is it was just as loud as the image of this angel in verse 10 of Chapter 1."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw another mighty angel come down from heaven, clothed with a cloud: and a rainbow was upon his head, and his face was as it were the sun, and his feet as pillars of fire:","ref":"Revelation 1:10"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The best way to understand biblical language is in the spirit of God. If we do not possess God’s Spirit, the things which are about to take place will mean nothing to us. We will never understand it. Nor can we ever understand it. Jesus also gives credence to this through John’s gospel once again:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Howbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he will guide you into all truth: for he shall not speak of himself; but whatsoever he shall hear, that shall he speak: and he will shew you things to come.","ref":"John 16:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even Paul understood that the Spirit of God gives us understanding…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But God hath revealed them unto us by his Spirit: for the Spirit searcheth all things, yea, the deep things of God.","ref":"1 Corinthians 2:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s Spirit allows us to understand every part of God’s desires. One of the greatest concerns a father has (if he has a daughter) is who she will end up marrying or end up in a relationship with. I remind my daughter that if she ever gets a boyfriend, she has the upper hand because she has a standard that is set for what to look for. Someone who has the Spirit of God working in them, and is able to love her in a Godly way, rather than in a selfish or fleshly way. Someone who can bear Godly fruit, and prove His love for Christ. She must be with someone who loves Jesus as much as Jesus loves His church."},{"kind":"para","text":"We do not receive the knowledge of spiritual things through teachings, through readings, through personal interpretation. We receive it strictly from God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For I neither received it of man, neither was I taught it, but by the revelation of Jesus Christ.","ref":"Galatians 1:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"Let’s continue looking at this verse…"},{"kind":"para","text":"“…and one sat on the throne…”"},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t believe I have to explain who sits on the throne…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"God reigneth over the heathen: God sitteth upon the throne of his holiness.","ref":"Psalm 47:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus is the only King worthy to have rule over everything. God’s throne should be of highest reverence in the life of a Christian. In the olden days, people weren’t allowed to be near the throne of the king unless they were summoned. If someone was near the king’s throne without being invited, they were kicked out of the city or executed. God’s throne is sacred, and it must be something of highest reverence to a truly born-again Christian that we get to come before Him and ask Him for anything."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let us therefore come boldly unto the throne of grace, that we may obtain mercy, and find grace to help in time of need.","ref":"Hebrews 4:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"This verse is extremely important to remember in our lives today. Without it, we would be miserably lost and doomed."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We should never mistake the jewels in Revelation to mean more than what John is trying to portray. John is pretty good at displaying when there is symbolism or deeper meanings in things that he sees as we go through this book. This particular part (where stones are mentioned) is to point out the visible features of God. They display bright colors and vivid imagery so that you understand that the vision in which John was seeing was nothing less than majestic; and God was displaying His awe and splendor."},{"kind":"para","text":"A jasper stone and a sardine stone have a reddish-orange color to them. I’m sure you know what an emerald looks like. The point he’s trying to convey is that God’s glory is bright and colorful. There is no human perception to even come close to being able to describe God’s glory except to compare it to precious stones."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In the Old Testament, God split the children of Israel up into 12 tribes, which is half of twenty four (which is what four and twenty equals)…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"All these are the twelve tribes of Israel: and this is it that their father spake unto them, and blessed them; every one according to his blessing he blessed them.","ref":"Genesis 49:28"},{"kind":"para","text":"Then the New Testament depicts 12 Apostles of Christ, though one was used by Satan and never saved."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now the names of the twelve apostles are these; The first, Simon, who is called Peter, and Andrew his brother; James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother; Philip, and Bartholomew; Thomas, and Matthew the publican; James the son of Alphaeus, and Lebbaeus, whose surname was Thaddaeus; Simon the Canaanite, and Judas Iscariot, who also betrayed him.","ref":"Matthew 10:2-4"},{"kind":"para","text":"It should be noted that Judas was later replaced…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they appointed two, Joseph called Barsabas, who was surnamed Justus, and Matthias. And they prayed, and said, Thou, Lord, which knowest the hearts of all men, shew whether of these two thou hast chosen, That he may take part of this ministry and apostleship, from which Judas by transgression fell, that he might go to his own place. And they gave forth their lots; and the lot fell upon Matthias; and he was numbered with the eleven apostles.","ref":"Acts 1:23-26"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s possible this is a picture of the Old and New Testament meeting together around God’s glory, as to show the importance of one with the other. This will be displayed more later on in this book… The Old Testament must meet in unison with the New, otherwise the Bible cannot work as God promised. Some have said that these elders are just angels, and are not included with the redeemed. But because the Old Testament and New Testament line up so well together, and have made a complete revelation and understanding of history and spirituality, I like to think it’s the former, rather than just angels."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There’s a significance to the number seven that shows up quite a bit. I still won’t go into the details of it (at least not yet), but the main thing we must remember is that seven signifies completeness."}]},{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These are actually not new creatures spoken about here. These are terrifying for us to envision, and many have tried to create renderings of what these could possibly look like, but they are difficult for us to comprehend. It’s another one of God’s creations that would astound us, and have astounded several already."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Above it stood the seraphims: each one had six wings; with twain he covered his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly. And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory.","ref":"Isaiah 6:2-3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"As for the likeness of their faces, they four had the face of a man, and the face of a lion, on the right side: and they four had the face of an ox on the left side; they four also had the face of an eagle…As for their rings, they were so high that they were dreadful; and their rings were full of eyes round about them four.","ref":"Ezekiel 1:10;18"},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s not much information about what these creatures do, or why they exist in the way they do, but we are confident that these creatures have been noticed, and they are obviously so bizarre to those that experience them that they are vividly remembered by each person that sees them. These creatures are the least amazing things found in Heaven, because it’s amazing that any of us would even be there ourselves."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This may, or may not, be the only purpose of these creatures. They may exist just to show God’s holiness, repeating “holy, holy, holy, Lord God Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come.” This is certainly something amazing and unreal to see. It displays the awesome creation of God, and these things give Him due reverence. Our minds can’t even imagine what John is trying to describe here, and I think, even if we saw this with our own eyes, we would still have had a hard time describing this amazing creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"May this be an example to us as well. God could have created us like these creatures with no choice but to show forth His praises and constant worship. He could have made us simply repeat the same things over and over again for all of eternity. He chose not to, however, and gave us a very different purpose and design than what He had designed these beings for."}]},{"start":9,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a great thought to implement in our daily lives. There are many things in this life we will see redundant patterns of. God has given us the ability to see who He is, and He has allowed us to behold His majesty even while we are living here on Earth. We have somehow become so stale and calloused to God’s glory here that we hardly notice it anymore. But for all of eternity we will be repeating our worship daily."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will be more available, and without excuse once we are before Him. We will get to worship, not have to worship. In Heaven, we will be in constant worship to God. It would never end, and this will be something joyous for us, because of how great, powerful, gracious, and amazing He truly is."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"O come, let us worship and bow down: let us kneel before the LORD our maker.","ref":"Psalm 95:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"By him therefore let us offer the sacrifice of praise to God continually, that is, the fruit of our lips giving thanks to his name.","ref":"Hebrews 13:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Give unto the LORD the glory due into his name; worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness.","ref":"Psalm 29:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"You might not have the ability to fall to your knees 24/7, and you may not have the opportunity to read your Bibles nonstop, but we all have the ability to worship anytime we choose. May we get into the pattern of worship now, so we are prepared for it in Heaven."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But the hour cometh, and now is, when the true worshippers shall worship the Father in spirit and in truth: for the Father seeketh such to worship him.","ref":"John 4:23"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":11}],"verses":{"2":"And immediately I was in the spirit: and, behold, a throne was set in heaven, and one sat on the throne.","3":"And he that sat was to look upon like a jasper and a sardine stone: and there was a rainbow round about the throne, in sight like unto an emerald.","4":"And round about the throne were four and twenty seats: and upon the seats I saw four and twenty elders sitting, clothed in white raiment; and they had on their heads crowns of gold.","5":"And out of the throne proceeded lightnings and thunderings and voices: and there were seven lamps of fire burning before the throne, which are the seven Spirits of God.","6":"And before the throne there was a sea of glass like unto crystal: and in the midst of the throne, and round about the throne, were four beasts full of eyes before and behind.","7":"And the first beast was like a lion, and the second beast like a calf, and the third beast had a face as a man, and the fourth beast was like a flying eagle.","8":"And the four beasts had each of them six wings about him; and they were full of eyes within: and they rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy, Lord God Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come.","9":"And when those beasts give glory and honour and thanks to him that sat on the throne, who liveth for ever and ever,","10":"The four and twenty elders fall down before him that sat on the throne, and worship him that liveth for ever and ever, and cast their crowns before the throne, saying,","11":"Thou art worthy, O Lord, to receive glory and honour and power: for thou hast created all things, and for thy pleasure they are and were created."}},
    "5": {"chapter":5,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 05"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we got a glimpse of some interesting things taking place and existing in Heaven. We see God’s throne which is radiant in color and brightness, some strange beasts that are hard to describe or understand, and a lot of glory given to God."},{"kind":"para","text":"This chapter will really focus on the praise of God and the build up of the things that are sure to come in the future of the world. We will be experiencing a lot of trials and judgements throughout the readings of each chapter, but God has provided brief pauses to those things here and there to effectively remind us what it’s for, and it reveals God’s ultimate glory. This is one of those chapters."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we got a glimpse of some interesting things taking place and existing in Heaven. We see God’s throne, which is radiant in color and brightness, some strange beasts that are hard to describe or understand, and a lot of glory given to God. This chapter will really focus on the praise of God and the build-up of the things that are sure to come in the future of the world. We will be experiencing a lot of trials and judgments throughout the readings of each chapter, but God has provided brief pauses to those things here and there to effectively remind us what it’s for, and it reveals God’s ultimate glory. This is one of those chapters."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":14,"title":"The Scroll and the Lamb","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In case you don’t know, God is sitting on the throne. Jesus Christ is the only one who deserves the throne. He has led His children into salvation and paid the ultimate price for all of mankind, so that we don’t end up in an eternity away from Him in suffering and torment."},{"kind":"para","text":"This depiction of Him holding the book, whose contents will be revealed in the chapters to come, displays that He is the one who controls what is to come. Ezekiel, the prophet of the Old Testament, also received a scroll that resembled this one:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when I looked, behold, an hand was sent unto me; and, lo, a roll of a book was therein; and he spread it before me; and it was written within and without: and there was written therein lamentations, and mourning, and woe. Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, eat that thou findest; eat this roll, and go speak unto the house of Israel. So I opened my mouth, and he caused me to eat that roll. And he said unto me, Son of man, cause thy belly to eat, and fill thy bowels with this roll that I give thee. Then did I eat it; and it was in my mouth as honey for sweetness.","ref":"Ezekiel 2:9-3:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"Supposedly, it resembles the same type of documentation as a Roman Will or Contract deed, which were also sealed with seven seals. When a document was sealed (especially back then, as we can’t trust sealed documents anymore today…), those mandates or covenants (dictations) were not to be broken, or there would be grave consequences."},{"kind":"para","text":"What is written on the seal is not disclosed, but it was obviously important to John because he took note of it. It could signify what the Lord Himself is to do, sealed seven times by the Lord, or it could signify the plagues and diseases that were to come because of our breaking of the signed covenant (obviously signed and sealed in the blood of Christ)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God signs and seals the believer as well:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye are our epistle written in our hearts, known and read of all men:","ref":"2 Corinthians 3:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise,","ref":"Ephesians 1:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever God signs into a covenant, no man can break. Even if you fall away from God, and you are no longer serving Him like you should be, you cannot go anywhere because God has already sealed you. St. Augustine said, “You lose none but the one who leaves You. And the one who leaves has nowhere to run.” Where do you go when God sees you?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Whither shall I go from thy spirit? Or whither shall I flee from thy presence? If I ascend up into heaven, thou art there: if I make my bed in hell, behold, thou art there. If I take the wings of the morning, and dwell in the uttermost parts of the sea; Even there shall thy hand lead me, and thy right hand shall hold me. If I say, Surely the darkness shall cover me; even the night shall be light about me. Yea, the darkness hideth not from thee; but the night shineth as the day: the darkness and the light are both alike to thee.","ref":"Psalm 139:7-12"},{"kind":"para","text":"Run all you want, but God will not disappear from your life. He can’t do it. He won’t do it. He loves you too much to allow you to ruin your life without warning. This is a good Father, and a good Father will be there when their children mess up anyway, and they will make sure they are able to get back up and continue forward."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I imagine something like a Sword in the Stone. In such a tale, you can see person after person try and take this sword out of the stone and continue to fail. But there’s one that comes along, who pulls it out without an issue."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t imagine this angel was trying to find someone who would step forward to try. Maybe there will be some who will (though in a minute John seems to not like this idea). I think the angel wants to display that it’s impossible for anyone to do what only God is able to do. It’s an indication to LEAN on God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, and my high tower.","ref":"Psalm 18:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a reminder to look to God!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I love them that love me; and those that seek me early shall find me.","ref":"Proverbs 8:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"We must depend on God! So who is worthy to open the book and lose the seals thereof? None. The answer is that simple. Only Jesus can break the seals, and He died to seal the fate of all mankind!"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Our feeble works can do nothing to ultimately bring salvation to others. We can do nothing for our salvation but sin. That’s literally all we bring to the table. Men and women will come far and wide to preach this message and that message, and they will sound appealing and enticing, but in the end, no man in heaven, nor on earth, nor under the earth, can do what only God can do."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"John saw this book as extremely important. He was given a task to write down everything he sees in these visions, and yet he comes to a point where he doesn’t even know what is in this book to write the account down. He’s probably thinking that there’s no hope for all of humanity. Man after man failed to successfully open this book. Even the angels in Heaven were failing, and John was taking witness to it. “This is how the world ends?” John probably thought. “This is what we must rely on? The fact that this book is impossible to open, and there’s no solidity to our future?”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For his anger endureth but a moment…weeping may endure for a night…","ref":"Psalm 30:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"There is always hope with our God. There is always a solution to the tough tests of issues with God. God has all things prepared, and He has all things ready for His creation. He never leaves us without. John must have forgotten this as he witnessed all of these failed attempts, and so he wept."},{"kind":"para","text":"This must remind us that we will always see man fail, but we do not depend on man’s strength."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Men’s hearts failing them for fear, and for looking after those things which are coming on the earth: for the powers of heaven shall be shaken.","ref":"Luke 21:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"You will always see Heavenly hosts fall, but you do not depend on the angels to rescue you."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But though we, or an angel from heaven, preach any other gospel unto you than that which we have preached unto you, let him be accursed. As we said before, so say I now again, If any man preach any other gospel unto you than that ye have received, let him be accursed.","ref":"Galatians 1:8-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"You will always see hatred for Christianity, but we do not depend on the world to encourage us!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If the world hate you, ye know that it hated me before it hated you. If ye were of the world, the world would love his own: but because ye are not of the world, but I have chosen you out of the world, therefore the world hateth you.","ref":"John 15:18-19"},{"kind":"para","text":"Depend on God! He is the only one that can succeed, and He is the only one that can be certain will always have a solution to every issue, no matter how seemingly big the problem may seem. We may have big problems today, but we serve a bigger God. Even more so, the plagues and terrors that are about to be introduced through this book are far bigger than what we are facing today, but we know that GOD is bigger. God will never make anything bigger than Him. If He did, He would cease to be God. It is impossible for God to overthrow Himself."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am the LORD, and there is none else, there is no God beside me: I girded thee, though thou hast not known me:","ref":"Isaiah 45:5"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The angel reminds John to keep his focus! Why was it so easy for John to forget that Jesus can do all things? It is God that has the utmost power to do whatever He pleases, and if it is Christ that holds the seal, John should not have cried for the sake of the seal not being opened, but simply looked to Jesus. We think that John may have taken his eyes off the most important thing, but so have many of us when it comes to difficult tasks that belong to the Lord. How can we take our eyes off the one who holds the seal of our eternities?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is set down at the right hand of the throne of God","ref":"Hebrews 12:2"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The seven spirits are more than likely resemblant to Zechariah’s prophecy."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For who hath despised the day of small things? For they shall rejoice, and shall see the plummet in the hand of Zerubbabel with those seven; they are the eyes of the LORD, which run to and fro through the whole earth.","ref":"Zechariah 4:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously the dead lamb depicts Jesus’ sacrifice on the cross."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The next day John seeth Jesus coming unto him, and saith, Behold the Lamb of God, which taketh away the sin of the world.","ref":"John 1:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"As a lamb, without spot or blemish, Jesus died to take away our sins. As a lion, powerful and victorious over the enemy, Jesus conquers all, including death and the grave, and is fully capable of breaking the seal signed by His own blood and sacrifice for us, so that we have an eternity with Him and His strength forever."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Preparations are underway to open this book and see what is inside. As much as I’d love to get into the details of what the scroll says and what each seal represents, I don’t have the time to do it in this chapter, which is why we must continue to come back to this book and see what happens next in the chapters to come."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We see a lot happening here, and we know that God has a busy plate even at this moment as He’s preparing this vision for John to write down. Yet we still see people worshipping, and we still see prayers being answered. It is quite evident that God hears your prayers, no matter how busy things are in your life or in His. He desires your continued prayers. He has people in Heaven still praying. We must continue to pray to Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you:","ref":"Matthew 7:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore I say unto you, What things soever ye desire, when ye pray, believe that ye receive them, and ye shall have them.","ref":"Mark 11:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"John cries over the idea of not succeeding in this eternity’s seal, and he looks to Jesus in prayer and thankfulness, knowing that Jesus died to break the seal of the covenants that we have already disobeyed. His judgement is true and right, and when we come to Him in prayer, we know that Jesus mediates for us so that our prayers will always be heard and our cries will always be answered."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For there is one God, and one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus;","ref":"1 Timothy 2:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"May we never forget the importance of prayer, even when we enter into eternity. Though we may be in constant communion with the Lord in Heaven, prayer is still key in the afterlife, and it’s something that allows us, and reminds us, of how helpless we are without the Lord."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Priests in our modern day are not biblical. I say this with love and kindness for the community of false worshippers, not to try and destroy their faith, but to point them to what the Bible says. He didn’t make certain people priests. That was not an occasion in the New Testament (or the Old). Jesus didn’t single out one specific person to be a priest in the church. As we have already mentioned, there is only ONE mediator and that is Jesus."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the Old Testament, priests were to give sacrifices daily for the sins of the people (and God desired that EVERY Israelite would be a priest). They would sacrifice for themselves first, and then for the rest of the people."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For such an high priest became us, who is holy, harmless, undefiled, separate from sinners, and made higher than the heavens; Who needeth not daily, as those high priests, to offer up sacrifice, first for his own sins, and then for the people’s: for this he did once, when he offered up himself.","ref":"Hebrews 7:26-27"},{"kind":"para","text":"When Christ came, He made every believer a priest, not to give sacrifices, but to give glory to the sacrifice God gave through His own Son."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people; that ye should shew forth the praises of him who hath called you out of darkness into his marvellous light:","ref":"1 Peter 2:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because God gave His only Son to die for our sins (the whole world’s sins), there is no sacrifice that is good enough for us to trump that or give to Him. He has already paid it. To sacrifice anything for sins is to mock Christ’s death, as did the murderer on the cross next to Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I do not frustrate the grace of God: for if righteousness come by the law, then Christ is dead in vain.","ref":"Galatians 2:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"Christ gave the FINAL sacrifice, so that all we must do is believe in Him, and we are saved. There is nothing more we can do. We cannot get involved with our church. We cannot have someone else pray over us or forgive us. No one else can mediate for us. We cannot give to receive salvation. The price has been paid, and the love of God was displayed from the cross with Christ’s final words:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"It is finished…","ref":"John 19:30"}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, the number here was too high for John to count. The angel, nor Jesus, made mention of how many there were, and so John just wanted to point out that there was a lot! Imagine we will see this much in Heaven. I don’t know for sure (John seems to be astounded by the things he is seeing), but it seems like it may be a common occurrence when we leave this world to join God in Heaven. May it be a reminder as well that this revelation is not given to anyone else on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"John was very specific about the things he saw and wrote down for a reason, so that anyone who claims to have seen heaven while they are still on Earth is without excuse. This is what it is, and there’s no reason to argue with God’s word on it. Not to mention, it’s all being proven right now as we speak."},{"kind":"para","text":"SIDENOTE: There have been people who have acclaimed to have seen heaven, or who have died and have witnessed for themselves what Heaven was like, but nothing compares to what John has written and said. In fact, they don’t even match up nine times out of ten to what John is saying here. They may have seen something, but it might not have been heaven. Their brains could have been playing tricks on them, or they may have made the story up based on a dream or on a thought that occurred to them."},{"kind":"para","text":"We don’t have much unity here on Earth, nor even in many of our churches, but when we are coming to worship God in Heaven, it will be tens of thousands of people all worshipping in unity, and it will be quite the sight to behold."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine thousands of people praising God like this at the same time. They didn’t just say it as a repetitive tradition; it says they said it with a LOUD VOICE. In other words, they were so excited that they were shouting these praises to God as loudly as they could, all at once. We should be just as excited to see the Lord while we are here that we can’t help ourselves but to shout to the Lord in praise."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"O praise the LORD, all ye nations: praise him, all ye people.","ref":"Psalm 117:1"}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Can you imagine that? “Every creature…” Picture this for a moment… Animals, fish, birds… all singing this tune to the Lord. We can’t fathom the idea of fish talking, yet it’s something we will experience in Heaven, and they only speak the words that give praise to God. May it be so with His human creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"We do a lot of talking, and the fish bring bigger praise than most of us. Look at Jonah as an example. The whale was more obedient to the will of God than the prophet of God was."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Which made heaven, and earth, the sea, and all that therein is: which keepeth truth for ever:","ref":"Psalm 146:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth; And that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.","ref":"Philippians 2:10-11"}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We must prepare our worship now for that is what we are going to be doing for all of eternity after this life. Do we worship like we should be? Are we excited about the Lord’s Word and work in our lives? Or are we worried about what He’s going to do soon? Maybe we are worried we are not ready for His coming and for the things that He is about to reveal to us… May it not be so."},{"kind":"para","text":"We must correct this now before continuing on. We should be as the fish, birds, animals, and all the hosts of Heaven in this chapter in our worship. May we be excited about the Lord’s Work of righteousness, and may we lean on Him knowing He is the only one who has control of everything that is going to follow."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14}],"verses":{"1":"And I saw in the right hand of him that sat on the throne a book written within and on the backside, sealed with seven seals.","2":"And I saw a strong angel proclaiming with a loud voice, Who is worthy to open the book, and to loose the seals thereof?","3":"And no man in heaven, nor in earth, neither under the earth, was able to open the book, neither to look thereon.","4":"And I wept much, because no man was found worthy to open and to read the book, neither to look thereon.","5":"And one of the elders saith unto me, Weep not: behold, the Lion of the tribe of Juda, the Root of David, hath prevailed to open the book, and to loose the seven seals thereof.","6":"And I beheld, and, lo, in the midst of the throne and of the four beasts, and in the midst of the elders, stood a Lamb as it had been slain, having seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven Spirits of God sent forth into all the earth.","7":"And he came and took the book out of the right hand of him that sat upon the throne.","8":"And when he had taken the book, the four beasts and four and twenty elders fell down before the Lamb, having every one of them harps, and golden vials full of odours, which are the prayers of saints.","9":"And they sung a new song, saying, Thou art worthy to take the book, and to open the seals thereof: for thou wast slain, and hast redeemed us to God by thy blood out of every kindred, and tongue, and people, and nation;","10":"And hast made us unto our God kings and priests: and we shall reign on the earth.","11":"And I beheld, and I heard the voice of many angels round about the throne and the beasts and the elders: and the number of them was ten thousand times ten thousand, and thousands of thousands;","12":"Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing.","13":"And every creature which is in heaven, and on the earth, and under the earth, and such as are in the sea, and all that are in them, heard I saying, Blessing, and honour, and glory, and power, be unto him that sitteth upon the throne, and unto the Lamb for ever and ever.","14":"And the four beasts said, Amen. And the four and twenty elders fell down and worshipped him that liveth for ever and ever."}},
    "6": {"chapter":6,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 06"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"Previously: Our last chapter saw the necessity placed on opening this book (or scroll) with no person in heaven or earth that could even come close. This reminded us of the one who is holding the book which was Jesus Christ. There was some symbolism with the Lamb, and the rulership of people with the Lord. We studied some things to expect in the future chapters (which was kept somewhat short because we didn’t want to spoil anything yet) and this last chapter really opens up chapter 6 and the revelation of the future to come (which is evidently still coming because the churches back then are matching many of the churches today)."},{"kind":"para","text":"John has already witnessed quite a bit in this short vision that we’ve gone through, but this is really only the tip of the iceberg before the real craziness sets in. Starting out with the seven churches that Jesus speaks about, I don’t believe John is fully prepared for what he is about to see, though the angel, and Jesus Himself tried their best to calm him down and get him to look at what is to come."},{"kind":"para","text":"These seven churches and their characteristics that were spoken of, pave the way for destruction because they chose to turn from worshipping Christ and were not looking out for the things that go against God. Self worship runs rampant in America (I have to assume in other countries as well) and the church has not gotten better since this warning from Christ written by John came into the world."},{"kind":"para","text":"No doubt, the world has experienced its mountain top experiences. Great revivals have taken place across the land, but they were well before we were in the world, and now we see the world slowly falling apart because they have taken their eyes off of the one thing that matters."},{"kind":"para","text":"I find it interesting, that during those times of great revival (like during the time of D.L. Moody) there was great war (the civil war specifically) but during the latter part of it we see people really trusting Christ and our land quickly being healed from such hatred and hurt. The civil war started when racist America fought against free America, and free America won! Though people today have a distaste for racist America (as they should) they didn’t experience half the battle that their ancestors had to face. But even during a time like this, it is possible to see great revival if someone would simply continue to preach the gospel."},{"kind":"para","text":"No doubt, D.L. Moody had no idea he would be a major face of the next great moving of God, but he was willing either way just to show love and be there for his neighbors. It was said that Moody ran into battle to pull wounded soldiers off the front lines into safety all the while asking “Have you been saved?” (Speaking of their spiritual salvation of course). True or not, it is certainly a testament to Moody’s character, for that was the type of man he was. He was labelled “Crazy Moody” because of his tactics on talking to everyone about the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"But maybe we don’t see revival… Maybe God is done moving across our land because of how far gone we are and we have decided that we don’t WANT to be saved. If this be the case, what happens to us? What happens to those that love the Lord and still desire His salvation? What happens to the rest of the world that hates Him and turns from Him? That’s what I believe our chapter comes to today, this is what happens when the world decides they are done with God."}],"previously":["Our last chapter saw the necessity placed on opening this book (or scroll) with no person in heaven or earth that could even come close. This reminded us of the one who is holding the book, which was Jesus Christ. There was some symbolism with the Lamb and the rulership of people with the Lord. We studied some things to expect in the future chapters (which was kept somewhat short because we didn’t want to spoil anything yet), and this last chapter really opened up for chapter 6 and the revelation of the future to come (which is evidently still coming because the churches back then are matching many of the churches today). John has already witnessed quite a bit in this short vision that we’ve gone through, but this is really only the tip of the iceberg before the real craziness sets in. Starting out with the seven churches that Jesus speaks about, I don’t believe John is fully prepared for what he is about to see, though the angel and Jesus Himself tried their best to calm him down and get him to look at what is to come. These seven churches and their characteristics that were spoken of pave the way for destruction because they chose to turn from worshipping Christ and were not looking out for the things that go against God. Self-worship runs rampant in America (I have to assume in other countries as well), and the church has not gotten better since this warning from Christ (written by John) came into the world. No doubt, the world has experienced its mountain-top experiences. Great revivals have taken place across the land, but they were well before we were in the world, and now we see the world slowly falling apart because they have taken their eyes off of the one thing that matters. I find it interesting that during those times of great revival (like during the time of D.L. Moody), there was great war (the Civil War specifically), but during the latter part of it, we see people really trusting Christ and our land quickly being healed from such hatred and hurt. The Civil War started when racist America fought against free America, and free America won! Though people today have a distaste for racist America (as they should), they didn’t experience half the battle that their ancestors had to face. But even during a time like this, it is possible to see great revival if someone would simply continue to preach the gospel. No doubt, D.L. Moody had no idea he would be a major face of the next great moving of God, but he was willing either way just to show love and be there for his neighbors. It was said that Moody ran into battle to pull wounded soldiers off the front lines into safety all the while asking “Have you been saved?” (Speaking of their spiritual salvation, of course). True or not, it is certainly a testament to Moody’s character, for that was the type of man he was. He was labelled “Crazy Moody” because of his tactics on talking to everyone about the Lord. But maybe we don’t see revival… Maybe God is done moving across our land because of how far gone we are, and we have decided that we don’t WANT to be saved. If this be the case, what happens to us? What happens to those that love the Lord and still desire His salvation? What happens to the rest of the world that hates Him and turns from Him? That’s what I believe our chapter comes to today; this is what happens when the world decides they are done with God."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"The First Seal","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again we come across the number seven, and it won’t be the last time we see this number represented in the end of times. I still won’t give great significance to the number seven, but I don’t believe that seven was an accidental number for God to use. We must remember that “seven” is the number that shows “completeness.” It’s been coincided with the “lucky number” of the Lord. Even in casinos today, they reference seven as a lucky number."},{"kind":"para","text":"Once the first seal is opened, because of the last chapter of Revelation (where John and most of Heaven and Earth is seen crying because the book can’t be opened), it seems (now that they have hope, because Jesus is able to open the book) they are far more interested in what this book has to say, and each seal has a specific meaning and purpose. There’s a reason to believe that this will be the beginning of the tribulation. If not, it will certainly be a warning of what is to come."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For then shall be great tribulation, such as was not since the beginning of the world to this time, no, nor ever shall be.","ref":"Matthew 24:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s also a common theme to each (of the first four) seals being opened, and I want to see if you notice it before I give it away."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"So we start off with a white horse. White horses are revered and usually rare. They have been used to picture strength and stability, like those knights of old. They usually rode upon a white horse. Because of what we come to read in this verse, we have reason to believe that this “white horse” would symbolize political and military leaders making their kingdoms larger and taking over land. This would no doubt cause a rise in division and wars, much like we have seen with Hamas and Israel, or Russia and Ukraine, and many other countries around the world (North and South Korea, etc.)."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"The Second Seal (Peace Taken From Earth)","entries":[{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another horse description is given, but this time it’s red. Red horses are the most common color of horses out of all of them. The rider of this horse will be given a great sword and given the commission to take away peace from the Earth so that we have no moral obligations to kill one another. Some theologians suggest that the reason the color of the horse was “red” was to resemble the blood that would be shed through the power of this horse’s rider. Of course, when you have nations that are divided (which the white horse represents), bloodshed will ensue, and people will have no quarrels against killing one another. That’s how war has always worked, and it will be no different (albeit on a larger scale) during the end of time."}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"The Third Seal (Famine)","entries":[{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Black horses are not that common either (though not as rare as white horses). The rider of this horse is carrying scales or “balances.” This one is pretty significant because it shows how life is going to be after all these great and terrible things start to take place. This is how costly living will be."},{"kind":"para","text":"A “penny” of barley, for the typical cost (back then) would have given you 10 times the amount. In other words, inflation will take place (because of wars and because of how rare some items will start to become (especially when most of your items are traded by other countries)) and the cost of living will start to become unbearable."},{"kind":"para","text":"Right now, our country is facing some pretty serious inflation issues because of the leadership in our country currently. But comparatively, during the end times, this is just a small fraction of the idea that will come into fruition when the tribulation happens. This is just a reminder that the things we are reading right now are extremely possible, and it wouldn’t take much to allow it to happen."},{"kind":"para","text":"Inflation is something that has taken place often throughout the Bible and has been proven time and time again through dishonoring and disobeying God. Famines, wars, and inflation are always God’s way to refocus His children back to Him. Even during a time of famine, God can still do a great miracle if we trusted in Him like Joseph did. The land of Egypt was the only land with any kind of providence, simply because of one man’s faith and trust in the Lord. All it takes is ONE to change lives, and if our nation (as a whole) would turn to God, He would bless us. Even furthermore, God gives us plenty of accounts of inflation to show the necessity we must lay to lean on Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The LORD shall bring a nation against thee from far, from the end of the earth, as swift as the eagle flieth; a nation whose tongue thou shalt not understand; A nation of fierce countenance, which shall not regard the person of the old, nor shew favour to the young: And he shall eat the fruit of thy cattle, and the fruit of thy land, until thou be destroyed: which also shall not leave thee either corn, wine, or oil, or the increase of thy kine, or flocks of thy sheep, until he have destroyed thee. And he shall besiege thee in all thy gates, until thy high and fenced walls come down, wherein thou trustedst, throughout all thy land: and he shall besiege thee in all thy gates throughout all thy land, which the LORD thy God hath given thee. And thou shalt eat the fruit of thine own body, the flesh of thy sons and of thy daughters, which the LORD thy God hath given thee, in the siege, and in the straitness, wherewith thine enemies shall distress thee: So that the man that is tender among you, and very delicate, his eye shall be evil toward his brother, and toward the wife of his bosom, and toward the remnant of his children which he shall leave: So that he will not give to any of them of the flesh of his children whom he shall eat: because he hath nothing left him in the siege, and in the straitness, wherewith thine enemies shall distress thee in all thy gates. The tender and delicate woman among you, which would not adventure to set the sole of her foot upon the ground for delicateness and tenderness, her eye shall be evil toward the husband of her bosom, and toward her son, and toward her daughter, And toward her young one that cometh out from between her feet, and toward her children which she shall bear: for she shall eat them for want of all things secretly in the siege and straitness, wherewith thine enemy shall distress thee in thy gates.","ref":"Deuteronomy 28:49-57"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And it came to pass after this, that Benhadad king of Syria gathered all his host, and went up, and besieged Samaria. And there was a great famine in Samaria: and, behold, they besieged it, until an ass's head was sold for fourscore pieces of silver, and the fourth part of a cab of dove's dung for five pieces of silver...Then Elisha said, Hear ye the word of the LORD; Thus saith the LORD, To morrow about this time shall a measure of fine flour be sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria. Then a lord on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God, and said, Behold, if the LORD would make windows in heaven, might this thing be? And he said, Behold, thou shalt see it with thine eyes, but shalt not eat thereof.","ref":"2 Kings 6:24-25;7:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Based on Deuteronomy, we must assume that when they say “Don’t hurt the oil and wine,” they are referring to their most prized resources. Oil and wine (during the Old (and possibly most likely the New as well) Testaments) were extremely valuable, and only the people with a decent amount of money had this in their possession. So it’s assumed that those that are saying “don’t hurt the oil and wine” are the upper class who are very cautious and illegitimately owned by their materialistic properties."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"title":"The Fourth Seal (Death)","entries":[{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now we see the fourth seal being opened, and this time it’s a pale horse. Now, if you’ve never seen a pale horse, that’s probably because they don’t exist. If your horse is pale, it’s either dying or it’s dead. Pale horses are never a good thing, and in these particular verses in this particular chapter, they ARE… still not a good thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems, however, that this rider only had authority to kill (by means of war, or means of famine and disease) ONLY a quarter of the earth. I say “only,” but honestly, that’s a lot of the earth’s population that will die from something seriously deadly. This will seemingly all kind of happen at once."},{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, it seems we are experiencing something as astronomical as what they are writing into the page here, but still, COVID is not as large to scale as the plague that is promised to come. A quarter of the world has not been killed off like this description suggests will happen, and there isn’t any major territorial overtaking happening at the moment. Either way, this is just a glimpse at some of the things that are going to take place in the end."},{"kind":"para","text":"So obviously, this pale horse gives the description of exactly what has always happened during times of great tribulation, war, famine, and evil workings of people that don’t care about anybody or anything but themselves. This is nothing new. The horse depicts what will happen (whether they will be literal horses or not (once again) doesn’t matter to the overall problem at hand). But we also see that this rider was given authority to kill people with “beasts of the earth.” This purpose is to depict the same punishments given to Jerusalem in their exile when they broke covenants."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The word of the LORD came again to me, saying, Son of man, when the land sinneth against me by trespassing grievously, then will I stretch out mine hand upon it, and will break the staff of the bread thereof, and will send famine upon it, and will cut off man and beast from it: Though these three men, Noah, Daniel, and Job, were in it, they should deliver but their own souls by their righteousness, saith the Lord GOD. If I cause noisome beasts to pass through the land, and they spoil it, so that it be desolate, that no man may pass through because of the beasts: Though these three men were in it, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, they shall deliver neither sons nor daughters; they only shall be delivered, but the land shall be desolate. Or if I bring a sword upon that land, and say, Sword, go through the land; so that I cut off man and beast from it: Though these three men were in it, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, they shall deliver neither sons nor daughters, but they only shall be delivered themselves. Or if I send a pestilence into that land, and pour out my fury upon it in blood, to cut off from it man and beast: Though Noah, Daniel, and Job, were in it, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, they shall deliver neither son nor daughter; they shall but deliver their own souls by their righteousness. For thus saith the Lord GOD; How much more when I send my four sore judgments upon Jerusalem, the sword, and the famine, and the noisome beast, and the pestilence, to cut off from it man and beast?","ref":"Ezekiel 14:12-21"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, things will not be very good, and it will seem as though it couldn’t get much worse. You might think to yourself, “Most of the population is being killed off by complete madness, that we could have stopped if we respected one another and actually listened to the teachings of God, there’s no way it could get any worse.” But that would be wrong. I told you at the beginning of the chapter that there was a common theme to these first four seals, can you think of what they are?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Each beast says, “Come.” They are saying, “Don’t just be a bystander, and don’t just hear about what is happening, but actually see it.” Many have said that “seeing is believing,” and they aren’t entirely wrong. But God is pleased with faith."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But without faith it is impossible to please him: for he that cometh to God must believe that he is, and that he is a rewarded of them that diligently seek him.","ref":"Hebrews 11:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Jesus saith unto him, Thomas, because thou hast seen me, thou hast believed: blessed are they that have not seen, and yet have believed.","ref":"John 20:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"Faith is more important to God than actually seeing."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.","ref":"Hebrews 11:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, John couldn’t go any further forward unless he believed in Christ first. First for the vision, and then again for the seals to be opened. It took faith. Because of his faith, he was granted a front-row seat to those things that are surely to take place. And because of our faith, we too get to take a look at what John looked at."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":11,"title":"The Fifth Seal (The Martyred Remnant)","entries":[{"start":9,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These verses are heavy. There have been many who had died for the Word of God and for preaching the gospel of Jesus Christ as salvation through faith alone, and they are and have been waiting for a very long time to see God exact revenge. Thankfully, our God is a patient God and desires that all would come to repentance."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.","ref":"2 Peter 3:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"If we had the power of God, and we exacted justice as soon as someone did us wrong, we would be terrible, and all of eternity would be empty. In fact, even some of our family wouldn’t be in Heaven because of how hateful we are. But God is patient, and we are going to see much of His patience through these chapters to come, and God continuously gives them chance after chance to be saved, and the people continue to reject and forsake God, even battling against Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"This seal really gives the best description as to why God must do those things to come…. The death of His saints. The purposeful killing of His children because of their love and belief in Him alone for salvation. Our world HATES God. This verse proves how much it hates God, by the fact that there are ANY (let alone thousands) who have died for their belief and faith in Jesus Christ alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even more so, they are placed under the altar (verse 9 says). In the Old Testament, that is where they would store the sacrifice. These martyrs of the faith were sacrificed for this specific purpose. God does not waste a death. He does not waste the trials and hurts of those that face them here on Earth. Even through pain and torment, we are glorifying God if it’s for His love and for His purpose. These saints are questioning “how long?”"},{"kind":"para","text":"We often question too… “How long?” Our questions of “How long?” seem so small compared to these saints who were killed and have been waiting for generations to see justice served, and to see God finally accomplish and finish His will and purpose for the Earth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"How long wilt thou forget me, O LORD? For ever? How long wilt thou hide thy face from me?","ref":"Psalm 13:1"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"How long, LORD? Wilt thou hide thyself for ever? Shall thy wrath burn like fire?","ref":"Psalm 89:46"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"LORD, how long shall the wicked, how long shall the wicked triumph?","ref":"Psalm 94:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"How much longer must we wait? How much more pain do we have to see before you finally end it all? How many more people have to die before you put a stop to all of humanity as we know it? How much longer do people have to live in their sins? When will your patience run out, Lord? God reassures them in verse 11…"},{"kind":"para","text":"“…And white robes were given unto every one of them; and it was said unto them, that they should rest yet for a little season…”"},{"kind":"para","text":"They are given white robes and told to rest a little longer. A white robe is a symbol of purity and victory, as we’ve already seen in our study and will see continuously."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou hast a few names even in Sardis which have not defiled their garments; and they shall walk with me in white: for they are worthy. He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and i will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.","ref":"Revelation 3:4-5"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even with our small problems and questions of “how long?” God comforts us and tells us “there are things that must be done first…” He promises us, as well, “it will be worth it when it’s over.”"}]}]},{"start":12,"end":17,"title":"The Sixth Seal (Anarchy)","entries":[{"start":12,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now we come to the last seal of the chapter, seal number 6. As if the wars, pestilence, and famine (let alone all the death) were not enough to prove God’s righteousness, He darkens the sun and turns the moon red. This is the complete destruction of the first heaven and Earth (which we will get into more detail on in the coming chapters), but I will give you a bit of a sneak peek:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them.","ref":"Revelation 20:11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea.","ref":"Revelation 21:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Not only will the moon prove God’s judgement, and the sun, but the whole earth will shake with a “great earthquake.” Every time God does something huge in the Bible, there is an earthquake to prove His power. When Jesus died and rose again:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from top to the bottom; and the earth did quake, and the rocks rent; And the graves were opened; and many bodies of the saints which slept arose, And came out of the graves after his resurrection, and went into the holy city, and appeared unto many.","ref":"Matthew 27:51-53"},{"kind":"para","text":"When God descended onto Mount Sinai, preparing to give Moses the Ten Commandments:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And mount Sinai was altogether on a smoke, because the LORD descended upon it in fire: and the smoke thereof ascended as the smoke of a furnace, and the whole mount quaked greatly.","ref":"Exodus 19:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"When God reveals His wrath against the enemy:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For in my jealousy and in the fire of my wrath have I spoken, Surely in that day there shall be a great shaking in the land of Israel; So that the fishes of the sea, and the fowls of the heaven, and the beasts of the field, and all creeping things that creep upon the earth, and all the men that are upon the face of the earth, shall shake at my presence, and the mountains shall be thrown down, and the steep places shall fall, and every wall shall fall to the ground.","ref":"Ezekiel 38:19-20"},{"kind":"para","text":"When He gets the focus of His children back to Him and off of material possession:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For thus saith the LORD of hosts; Yet once, it is a little while, and I will shake the heavens, and the earth, and the sea, and the dry land; And I will shake all nations, and the desire of all nations shall come: and I will fill this house with glory, saith the LORD of hosts. The silver is mine, and the gold is mine, saith the LORD of hosts.","ref":"Haggai 2:6-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"His voice shook the earth:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Whose voice then shook the earth: but now he hath promised, saying, Yet once more I shake not the earth only, but also heaven. And this word, Yet once more, signifieth the removing of those things that are shaken, as of things that are made, that those things which cannot be shaken may remain.","ref":"Hebrews 12:26-27"},{"kind":"para","text":"I think we get the point… Earthquakes are God’s great invention to get His people’s attention. We are more alert during an Earthquake than we are in any other time."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be earthquakes in divers places, and there shall be famines and troubles: these are the beginnings of sorrows.","ref":"Mark 13:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"SIDENOTE: When I lived in Texas, there were a lot of questions that were asked of me about what life was like in California. “Did you know the Red Hot Chili Peppers?” “Is In-N-Out really better than What-A-Burger?” “Have you ever had Tex-Mex?” But the question that always got me was “How do you deal with earthquakes?” My rebuttal to that question was “How do you deal with tornadoes?!” They were more afraid of earthquakes than they were of tornadoes. It has always baffled my mind, but you get to thinking about this: in a tornado, you know to move away from it. You have a chance to escape a tornado. In an earthquake, where do you go?"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, during those times, people have no idea what to do. It’s not like you can just run from an earthquake. You can’t even really detect when an earthquake will come. Even with all of our technology and scientific advancements, we still miss a majority of earthquakes’ origins. We know there was an earthquake AFTER the earthquake. Sometimes it can be caught beforehand, but not often enough."},{"kind":"para","text":"God gives warning about the earthquakes to come, and it says that people will still be worried and scared and hiding themselves (verse 15). What’s even worse, because they know they can’t run from God and they know that there is nothing they can do to stop God’s judgement and wrath, is (instead of them repenting and trusting in Christ) they ask the rocks to LITERALLY FALL ON THEM (verse 16)… They are so terrified of what they are experiencing, and instead of believing in the one that is making this to happen, they continue to pridefully ignore and reject Him. Then the great question is asked:"},{"kind":"para","text":"“…who shall be able to stand?”"},{"kind":"para","text":"The answer is simple, yet it’s something that wouldn’t have to be asked if they would just simply repent and turn to God. The answer is… No one. We are all doomed to suffer for the wages of our sin. We have lived a life of sin and are getting paid for the work we have put into that sin. So then it’s over… it’s done, and there is nothing more that can be said… But there is still ONE more seal! We only read about six seals opened in this chapter, and it seemingly looks to just forget about the last seal. Actually, the seventh seal is not even mentioned in the next chapter either. But there’s a reason for that, and we will have to keep studying further to see what happens."},{"kind":"para","text":"I will say, though, it isn’t going to get any easier. The next chapter does give some hope. It’s one of those pauses of relief that God gives throughout this book of the Bible. The great takeaway from this chapter, however, is that we see God has patience even with those that are against Him. All we must do is repent and trust in Him alone for salvation, and He will grant it. We are saved from the wrath to come."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Much more then, being now justified by his blood, we shall be saved from wrath through him.","ref":"Romans 5:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"A quarter of the world could be killed off, but you won’t be one of them, for you are saved, and your life is bought with a price."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God’s.","ref":"1 Corinthians 6:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"God takes care of His children, and even during the last days, He continues to give chance after chance for salvation. But eventually, chances will run out. There will be nothing left to give chances to…"},{"kind":"para","text":"If you have already received Christ, that’s great, and you have reason to rejoice! However, there are those you work with, those that are in your family, those that you are friends with, even those that you walk past daily who have no idea what Christ did for them. They need a chance to know and understand before it’s too late. We see our world closely related to the major events pictured in this chapter in our age today, so we know exactly how sick and twisted things are going to get, and it won’t just end here. We still have 16 chapters to go, and it doesn’t get easier. In fact, much of what we are going to read in the coming chapters mirrors our current culture now, but on a grander scale. This is our chance to give the gospel to as many as possible before it’s too late."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":17}],"verses":{"1":"And I saw when the Lamb opened one of the seals, and I heard, as it were the noise of thunder, one of the four beasts saying, Come and see.","2":"And I saw, and behold a white horse: and he that sat on him had a bow; and a crown was given unto him: and he went forth conquering, and to conquer.","3":"And when he had opened the second seal, I heard the second beast say, Come and see.","4":"And there went out another horse that was red: and power was given to him that sat thereon to take peace from the earth, and that they should kill one another: and there was given unto him a great sword.","5":"And when he had opened the third seal, I heard the third beast say, Come and see. And I beheld, and lo a black horse; and he that sat on him had a pair of balances in his hand.","6":"And I heard a voice in the midst of the four beasts say, A measure of wheat for a penny, and three measures of barley for a penny; and see thou hurt not the oil and the wine.","7":"And when he had opened the fourth seal, I heard the voice of the fourth beast say, Come and see.","8":"And I looked, and behold a pale horse: and his name that sat on him was Death, and Hell followed with him. And power was given unto them over the fourth part of the earth, to kill with sword, and with hunger, and with death, and with the beasts of the earth.","9":"And when he had opened the fifth seal, I saw under the altar the souls of them that were slain for the word of God, and for the testimony which they held:","10":"And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Lord, holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?","11":"And white robes were given unto every one of them; and it was said unto them, that they should rest yet for a little season, until their fellowservants also and their brethren, that should be killed as they were, should be fulfilled.","12":"And I beheld when he had opened the sixth seal, and, lo, there was a great earthquake; and the sun became black as sackcloth of hair, and the moon became as blood;","13":"And the stars of heaven fell unto the earth, even as a fig tree casteth her untimely figs, when she is shaken of a mighty wind.","14":"And the heaven departed as a scroll when it is rolled together; and every mountain and island were moved out of their places.","15":"And the kings of the earth, and the great men, and the rich men, and the chief captains, and the mighty men, and every bondman, and every free man, hid themselves in the dens and in the rocks of the mountains;","16":"And said to the mountains and rocks, Fall on us, and hide us from the face of him that sitteth on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb:","17":"For the great day of his wrath is come; and who shall be able to stand?"}},
    "7": {"chapter":7,"intro":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he is the head of the body, the church: who is the beginning, the firstborn from the dead; that in all things he might have the preeminence.","ref":"Colossians 1:18"}],"previously":["In our previous chapter, we saw the opening of the seven seals take place, leaving off with only one more seal to open. It seemed that every seal that was broken led to a greater problem compared to the last. We seem to take a bit of a break from opening seals in this chapter to highlight some really fascinating information about the saved during the end times, and will get back to seal breaking in the next chapter. This brief pause from the destruction and ruin of mankind and the world helps the reader remember what this is all for. A good reminder to consider while we continue to read through this book of the Bible is that the main theme of every book in the Bible is Jesus Christ."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":8,"title":"The 144,000 of Israel Sealed","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Seemingly taking a step back from the previous chapter, there is a pause from opening up the final seal. When we think of the wind (especially living in the Antelope Valley (which could be considered the Windy City, not unlike Chicago, which was named such for seemingly no reason…), there’s no doubt in my mind that the Antelope Valley is far more windy than Chicago), but when we think of the wind, we don’t think of peace and calmness."},{"kind":"para","text":"Though God can show Himself mighty through the wind, we don’t look to the wind to show God’s peace. In fact, the wind usually brought terrible trials, and it was the last place you wanted to find yourself when you were trying to relax."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he saith unto them, Why are ye fearful, O ye of little faith? Then he arose, and rebuked the winds and the sea; and there was a great calm. But the men marvelled, saying, What manner of man is this, that even the winds and the sea obey him!","ref":"Matthew 8:26-27"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, Go forth, and stand upon the mount before the LORD. And, behold, the LORD passed by, and a great and strong wind rent the mountains, and brake in pieces the rocks before the LORD; but the LORD was not in the wind: and after the wind an earthquake; but the LORD was not in the earthquake: And after the earthquake a fire; but the LORD was not in the fire: and after the fire a still small voice. And it was so, when Elijah heard it, that he wrapped his face in his mantle, and went out, and stood in the entering in of the cave. And, behold, there came a voice unto him, and said, What doest thou here, Elijah?","ref":"1 Kings 19:11-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Here, we see the angels stopping the wind or “holding back the winds of the earth.” My assumption is that they are allowing a short window of calmness and stillness before breaking the last seal (which will be mentioned in a moment)."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The power to harm “earth and sea” is not quite understood yet, because that hasn’t come to fruition. So far, the unfolding of the seals that we have experienced in the last chapter have all been a part of what God foreknows, but has not specifically caused yet. Though all things are allowed by God, these things that took place (aside from the sky rolling back, the island and the mountains being removed, the great earthquakes taking place, and the moon becoming red, and the stars falling… and the sun becoming black…) they took place because of the world’s sinful desire to have more than what they deserve or need, and they are willing to do whatever it takes to get it (including murder and stealing). The angels are held back here, though, because God is allowing another chance for salvation."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are still some who are able to be saved. I take into consideration that this may not be quite the beginning of the “tribulation” as we will come to know it. Some have claimed that there may not have been a “rapture” as of yet. It should be understood that we are told there is to be one."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air: and so shall we ever be with the Lord.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 4:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Immediately after the tribulation of those days shall the sun be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light, and the stars shall fall from heaven, and the powers of the heavens shall be shaken: And then shall appear the sign of the Son of man in heaven: and then shall all the tribes of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of man coming in the clouds of heaven with power and great glory. And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.","ref":"Matthew 24:29-31"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But of that day and that hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels which are in heaven, neither the Son, but the Father.","ref":"Mark 13:32"},{"kind":"para","text":"They’ve likened the current events from our last chapter to the “tribulation” and then the coming events after to “The Great Tribulation.” We will talk a little more about this standpoint later on, but there are many who believe that we will experience a “pre-tribulation” rapture, and would assume we would be taken up somewhere around the first seal being broken."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever the case may be, Jesus had made it clear that no one will know the day or hour on purpose. We can debate when the rapture and tribulation take place until we are blue in the face and neither one of us will be right because we aren’t supposed to know!"},{"kind":"para","text":"In this verse (and the ones we will read in a moment) we see that God has stopped the last seal from being broken and is now “sealing” the servants of God on their “foreheads.” This seal is promised to everyone who conquers the trials by faith."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Him that overcometh will I make a pillar in the temple of my God, and he shall go no more out: and I will write upon him the name of my God, and the name of the city of my God, which is new Jerusalem, which cometh down out of heaven from my God: and I will write upon him my new name.","ref":"Revelation 3:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"While God may be breaking seals to prepare the way for judgement, He is finalizing the “seal” of the Holy Spirit over those that turn to Him before the great tribulation is to happen. Not only so, but also showing it forth with the seal pressed upon their foreheads. In the Old Testament, the proven seal of the children of Israel was through circumcision:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he received the sign of circumcision, a seal of the righteousness of the faith which he had yet being uncircumcised: that he might be the father of all them that believe, though they be not circumcised; that righteousness might be imputed unto them also:","ref":"Romans 4:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"And for us (living in this church age from the “New Testament” era), we are sealed with the Holy Spirit."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise, Which is the earnest of our inheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession, unto the praise of his glory.","ref":"Ephesians 1:13-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"But for those in the times during the tribulation, they are presumably sealed on their foreheads, so as not to be mistaken for who they are. We will see that they will be remaining on Earth as well (in the coming chapters). Those that are sealed will be the only ones to answer the question in Revelation 6:17:"},{"kind":"para","text":"“For the great day of wrath is come; and who shall be able to stand?”"},{"kind":"para","text":"They will probably stand, for God will keep His children standing even through great pain and trouble."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Labour not for the meat which perisheth, but for that meat which endureth unto everlasting life, which the Son of man shall give unto you: for him hath God the Father sealed.","ref":"John 6:27"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand. Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness;","ref":"Ephesians 6:13-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes it will seem that the child of God (those that have been sealed by God) will often stand alone. We stand alone because we understand that Christ has the preeminence. Anything we do without Him will be a waste of time. Everything we do with Him will multiply."},{"kind":"para","text":"John Bunyan said, “What God says is best, is best, though all men in the world are against it.” Of all the men in the world to utter such a quote, John Bunyan would have known more about standing alone for God than any other. But as is the day in which we live, I find it hard that there are many in the church today that (if faced with real Godly burdens) would continue to stand. Not because they are too weary to stand, but because they were never really sealed by God’s Spirit to begin with."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is where it gets dicey for some scholars. The Bible is specific about the number of people who are sealed (144,000) and from what lineage they will be sealed from (sons of Israel). They go even further to implicate that these sons of Israel will be from very specific tribes. 12 tribes to be exact."}]},{"start":5,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We understand that the Old Testament split the people of Israel up into 12 different and specific tribes, who were the sons of Jacob. However, it is assumed (and rightfully so) that these are not the same 12 tribes from the sons of Jacob because Dan is taken out, and Manasseh is included. They also can’t be the tribes that had inherited land in Canaan, because Dan is left out, Levi (the priestly tribe) is included, and Joseph is listed instead of his son Ephraim."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not only so, but the tribes of Gad, Asher, and Naphtali would assume that (because these children were the children of concubines) that those who were once excluded from privilege (because of their seemingly small role in the world and sinful lineage) were now included. Almost as if to say that no matter your background or where you come from, salvation belongs to the Lord and He alone gets to save who He pleases."},{"kind":"para","text":"With that said, this doesn’t mean that these tribes are not specific to our day and age (though they probably will not be, more than likely). I do have to make the assumption that these tribes are more of a reference to the fact that God will save whoever calls upon His name. That means that the total “144,000” will probably not be a literal amount of people, but rather a symbol of a small remnant of (mostly) Jewish people who will be saved during this time."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whether they are specifically from these tribes is not well understood. We DO know that there were 12 tribes, indicating the 12 lineages from Jacob:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These shall stand upon mount Gerizim to bless the people, when ye are come over Jordan; Simeon, and Levi, and Judah, and Issachar, and Joseph, and Benjamin: And these shall stand upon mount Ebal to curse; Reuben, Gad, and Asher, and Zebulun, Dan, and Naphtali.","ref":"Deuteronomy 27:12-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"We understand that those twelve tribes were responsible for the growth and population of much of the world, and we understand that through this lineage (specifically Judah, and the lineage of the Messiah), Jesus Christ would be born. We know that God saved His people (specifically Israel) whenever they needed Him and looked to Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land.","ref":"2 Chronicles 7:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"But we also understand that Jesus chose twelve specific people to be His disciples too."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when it was day, he called unto him his disciples: and of them he chose twelve, whom also he named apostles; Simon (whom he also named Peter,) and Andrew his brother, James and John, Philip and Bartholomew, Matthew and Thomas, James the son of Alphaeus, and Simon called Zelotes, and Judas the brother of James, and Judas Iscariot, which also was the traitor.","ref":"Luke 6:13-16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Aside from seven, twelve was another number that God used quite often to show completeness."},{"kind":"para","text":"I see it like this… God uses seven to show HIS completeness…"},{"kind":"para","text":"He rests on the seventh day."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thus the heavens and the earth were finished, and all the host of them. And on the seventh day God ended his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had made.","ref":"Genesis 2:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus gives us 7 specific examples of who He is."},{"kind":"para","text":"The bread of life (John 6:35) The light of the world (John 8:12) The door of salvation (John 10:9) The Good Shepherd (John 10:11) The resurrection and life (John 11:25-26) The way, the truth, and the life (John 14:6) The vine (John 15:5)"},{"kind":"para","text":"God tries His word seven times."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The words of the LORD are pure words: as silver tried in a furnace of earth, purified seven times.","ref":"Psalm 12:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"When it has to do with spiritual matters, we understand that He is very specific about the number seven. More examples would include seven colors in the rainbow, being told to forgive 70x7 times, seven churches in Revelation, seven seals, seven trumpets, seven angels, seven candlesticks, seven bowls (or vials) of wrath. Seven ascribes to GOD’S perfection."},{"kind":"para","text":"TWELVE (on the other hand), I believe, ascribes to OUR perfection through God. We’ve already mentioned the twelve tribes of Judah, then the twelve disciples, both of which are human instruments of perfection. Judah being the perfect amount of tribes for the amount of people they had to look over. Twelve disciples being the perfect amount of disciples, to start the church with."},{"kind":"para","text":"We look at the twelve new tribes of Revelation, and from each tribe was twelve thousand. The New Jerusalem will have twelve gates made of pearl, with the names of Israel’s twelve tribes. Also not to mention the units that each gate and wall will be measured by is in increments of twelve. We could go on and on, but the point is, God uses twelve to signify perfectness to US, where He uses seven to signify HIS perfection. It helps give us a better understanding of His holiness and our dependency."},{"kind":"para","text":"The point of all of this is to say that we don’t necessarily have to give significance to ALL numbers in the Bible. There are some numbers that should be reported and taken literal (like the measuring of heaven, for instance, whether that is a literal measurement or not, we will not know for now) but others that should not be taken quite as seriously (like the number of colors in the rainbow, or how many times we should forgive someone). This accumulation of one hundred and forty-four thousand doesn’t have to necessarily mean “144,000,” but an estimate to how many people were seemingly saved."},{"kind":"para","text":"When we take the number one hundred and forty-four thousand and we subtract it to the amount of people currently living on Earth (7.753 billion) we don’t even see the amount of people left of those who are not sealed by God. That, in itself, should make us all terribly miserable. And that’s AFTER a rapture for those of us who assume there will be one before the tribulation. For we are saved from the wrath to come."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Much more then, being now justified by his blood, we shall be saved from wrath through him.","ref":"Romans 5:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"There will still be a lot of people left on earth though, and we will see that in the coming chapters. But it’s not all hopeless and lost."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":17,"title":"A Great Multitude From Every Nation","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a beautiful sight. Too many to number, worshipping, all from different nations, in different languages, singing the same praises. Someone said, “There are three things that will surprise you in Heaven. 1) People will be there that you didn’t think would be. 2) People who won’t be there that you thought would be. 3) That you will be there.” But I would like to add a fourth, “Everyone worshipping in unison for the first time ever, knowing that His time has come to put a stop to suffering that this world continuously offers its people.”"}]},{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Every creation will worship God, including the angels. Why (at this moment) are they worshipping though? What was it that God did to cause them to worship like this once again? I believe it’s because He saved the last of them."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Likewise, I say unto you, there is joy in the presence of the angels of God over one sinner that repenteth.","ref":"Luke 15:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is it. These are the final saved from the Earth. Not because God would have them be the last:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.","ref":"2 Peter 3:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe it will be the last ones saved, because God knows no one else (even though they will have multiple chances even after this) who will turn to the Lord. Some have said that no one will have a chance to be saved after this, but I don’t believe that’s true. They have said that the rapture was their last chance, but as we will see through these chapters, God prolongs these trials and judgments for a specific reason, and I believe it’s the same reason He prolongs His return from the Earth. More chances."}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I laughed when I read this for the first time. The elder asks John, “Who are these people in the white robes, and how did they get here?” And John simply replies, “You know!” As if to say, “Well, of course I know, but I just want to see if YOU know, so why don’t you say it first, and I’ll let you know if you are correct…” Of course, the elder gives the answer."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are those who have been saved AFTER the tribulation. Think of this for a second, does this not line up to what we said before? They more than likely died during the time of judgement (which those who are saved today are currently saved from), but they trusted in Christ DURING the tribulation. They fought in the war of Armageddon. They were killed for their faith. Their clothes were bloodied. Their scars were numerous. Their burdens were heavy. But the blood of the Lamb washes away all these things!"},{"kind":"para","text":"“…They have washed their robes and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanseth us from all sin.","ref":"1 John 1:7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Take heed therefore unto yourselves, and to all the flock, over the which the Holy Ghost hath made you overseers, to feed the church of God, which he hath purchased with his own blood.","ref":"Acts 20:28"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In whom we have redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of sins, according to the riches of his grace;","ref":"Ephesians 1:7"}]},{"start":15,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When we have run our course, we find shelter with God. We may continue to live on in Paradise, but it will never be burdensome again. He gives us shelter, He keeps us warm, we never have to hunger or thirst, and we will never shed one more tear… And it’s all because they kept Christ preeminent…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Brethren, I count not myself to have apprehended: but this one thing I do, forgetting those things which are behind, and reaching forth unto those things which are before, I press toward the mark for the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus.","ref":"Philippians 3:13-14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Jesus said unto him, No man, having put his hand to the plough, and looking back, is fit for the kingdom of God.","ref":"Luke 9:62"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And it came to pass, when they had brought them forth abroad, that he said, Escape for thy life; look not behind thee, neither stay thou in all the plain; escape to the mountain, lest thou be consumed.","ref":"Genesis 19:17"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":17}],"verses":{"1":"And after these things I saw four angels standing on the four corners of the earth, holding the four winds of the earth, that the wind should not blow on the earth, nor on the sea, nor on any tree.","2":"And I saw another angel ascending from the east, having the seal of the living God: and he cried with a loud voice to the four angels, to whom it was given to hurt the earth and the sea,","3":"Saying, Hurt not the earth, neither the sea, nor the trees, till we have sealed the servants of our God in their foreheads.","4":"And I heard the number of them which were sealed: and there were sealed an hundred and forty and four thousand of all the tribes of the children of Israel.","5":"Of the tribe of Juda were sealed twelve thousand. Of the tribe of Reuben were sealed twelve thousand. Of the tribe of Gad were sealed twelve thousand.","6":"Of the tribe of Aser were sealed twelve thousand. Of the tribe of Nepthalim were sealed twelve thousand. Of the tribe of Manasses were sealed twelve thousand.","7":"Of the tribe of Simeon were sealed twelve thousand. Of the tribe of Levi were sealed twelve thousand. Of the tribe of Issachar were sealed twelve thousand.","8":"Of the tribe of Zabulon were sealed twelve thousand. Of the tribe of Joseph were sealed twelve thousand. Of the tribe of Benjamin were sealed twelve thousand.","9":"After this I beheld, and, lo, a great multitude, which no man could number, of all nations, and kindreds, and people, and tongues, stood before the throne, and before the Lamb, clothed with white robes, and palms in their hands;","10":"And cried with a loud voice, saying, Salvation to our God which sitteth upon the throne, and unto the Lamb.","11":"And all the angels stood round about the throne, and about the elders and the four beasts, and fell before the throne on their faces, and worshipped God,","12":"Saying, Amen: Blessing, and glory, and wisdom, and thanksgiving, and honour, and power, and might, be unto our God for ever and ever. Amen.","13":"And one of the elders answered, saying unto me, What are these which are arrayed in white robes? and whence came they?","14":"And I said unto him, Sir, thou knowest. And he said to me, These are they which came out of great tribulation, and have washed their robes, and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.","15":"Therefore are they before the throne of God, and serve him day and night in his temple: and he that sitteth on the throne shall dwell among them.","16":"They shall hunger no more, neither thirst any more; neither shall the sun light on them, nor any heat.","17":"For the Lamb which is in the midst of the throne shall feed them, and shall lead them unto living fountains of waters: and God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes."}},
    "8": {"chapter":8,"intro":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"Men’s hearts failing them for fear, and for looking after those things which are coming on the earth: for the powers of heaven shall be shaken. And then shall they see the Son of man coming in a cloud with power and great glory. And when these things begin to come to pass, then look up, and lift up your heads; for your redemption draweth nigh.","ref":"Luke 21:26-28"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In a moment, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trump: for the trumpet shall sound, and the dead shall be raised incorruptible, and we shall be changed.","ref":"1 Corinthians 15:52"},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, this is a warping of the actuality that is happening in the end times. The verses in Luke tell us to wait and anticipate the Lord’s coming, something that many scholars have an issue with today as well, but I won’t get into that debate here. The verse in 1 Corinthians is taken completely out of context, and we can assume several ideas about it, but assuming that this means the rapture won’t happen until nearly all of the tribulation has taken place is incongruent with what we have already studied throughout the book of Revelation, and it simply won’t hold weight the more we read. You want to talk about trumpets, we can easily determine that this “last trumpet” is the Lord’s voice simply by this book alone!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I was in the Spirit on the Lord’s day, and heard behind me a great voice, as of a trumpet,","ref":"Revelation 1:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even more so, when we read what Jesus says in Luke, He ends it with, “When these things begin to come to pass…” We are told how the world is going to be during the last days of Earth:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But as the days of Noah were, so shall the coming of the Son of man be.","ref":"Matthew 24:37"},{"kind":"para","text":"It will happen quickly, and none of us will actually be prepared for it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For as in the days that were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noe entered into the ark, And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.","ref":"Matthew 24:38-39"},{"kind":"para","text":"And because of this, we should have hope, and it should encourage us to stand more strongly on our faith, allowing Him to guide our motives into warning others about the things to come. That’s what we should continuously keep in mind while we study through this book of Revelation."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we spoke about the 144,000 saved during the tribulation period, how it was the “remnant of Israel” sealed, and the preparation for the worst parts of the tribulation to take place. We also focused on the tears that would be wiped away for eternity. (More on the 144,000 and the wiping away of tears later in this book.) A lot of scholars believe that the rapture has not taken place yet (which we spoke about in the last couple of chapters happening before the first seal, around the sixth seal, or during the last trumpet). They have used verses like:"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":1,"title":"The Seventh Seal","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Keeping people silent for less than 10 minutes is an impossible feat in and of itself. Even if there were like 20 people in there, there would no doubt be someone either coughing, laughing, thinking about something else and being completely distracted, or whispering about something completely unrelated to why they are trying to be silent in the first place. But this has multitudes of people sitting…waiting…patiently as this last seal is opened."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are anticipating what is to come next. They have seen so much already, what more could this seal possibly hold?! It says they wait for HALF AN HOUR! This was too exciting not to wait for. Anything the Lord is planning on doing is worth the wait and patience."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Wait on the Lord: be of good courage, and he shall strengthen thine heart: wait, I say, on the Lord.","ref":"Psalm 27:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Too many of us miss the moving of God because we grow so impatient in waiting on Him. But we know that the waiting period will be worth it, and in this chapter it is no different."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing instant in prayer;","ref":"Romans 12:12"}]}]},{"start":2,"end":6,"title":"The High Priest","entries":[{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Everything starts to come alive at this moment. Trumpets don’t seem like much, but they are a great indicator of the start of the ultimate tribulation. Many believe that the trumpets will symbolize the rapture."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God: and the dead in Christ shall rise first:","ref":"1 Thessalonians 4:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In a moment, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trump: for the trumpet shall sound, and the dead shall be raised incorruptible, and we shall be changed.","ref":"1 Corinthians 15:52"},{"kind":"para","text":"At the risk of sounding like a broken record, we also understand and know that nobody knows when the rapture will take place."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But of that day and that hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels which are in heaven, neither the Son, but the Father. Take ye heed, watch and pray: for ye know not when the time is.","ref":"Mark 13:32-33"},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, not knowing refreshes my faith. It’s the exciting part to me. We don’t know, and this is why we must always be ready, waiting, and watching. It’s even commanded to us to watch by Jesus Himself. Watching and waiting is not just a suggestion; it’s a command."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, I want to break down the terms used here for “trumpets.” We are given two types of trumpets in the Old Testament."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Make thee two trumpets of silver; of a whole piece shalt thou make them: that thou mayest use them for the calling of the assembly, and for the journeying of the camps.","ref":"Numbers 10:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"Each trumpet had a significance to them that was used for different things. One trumpet was for bringing the people together (which is the same terminology that Paul is using to describe the “last trump” in 1 Corinthians; it is the last call that Christ makes to the church, so therefore it is the last trump…), while the other trumpet is used for the wilderness march (somewhat of an alarm if you will) to prepare for battle/for preparing for the moving of the people."},{"kind":"para","text":"The first trumpet (that of the Lord) in Revelation is a call for the people to gather together (which is exactly what Paul speaks of). This second trumpet (the first of seven) is the initiation of war."},{"kind":"para","text":"Let’s put it into this perspective to get the full picture, because I feel there will still be many who would try and doubt the usefulness (and the scriptural significance) of the trumpets. Let’s look to the walls of Jericho."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now Jericho was straitly shut up because of the children of Israel: none went out, and none came in. And the LORD said unto Joshua, See, I have given into thine hand Jericho, and the king thereof, and the mighty men of valour. And ye shall compass the city, all ye men of war, and go round about the city once. Thus shalt thou do six days. And seven priests shall bear before the ark seven trumpets of rams' horns: and the seventh day ye shall compass the city seven times, and the priests shall blow with the trumpets. And it shall come to pass, that when they make a long blast with the ram's horn, and when ye hear the sound of the trumpet, all the people shall shout with a great shout; and the wall of the city shall fall down flat, and the people shall ascend up every man straight before him.","ref":"Joshua 6:1-5"},{"kind":"para","text":"The trumpets were multifunctional. The trumpet was sounded first for the gathering of the people."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And it came to pass, when Joshua had spoken unto the people, that the seven priests bearing the seven trumpets of rams’ horns passed on before the LORD, and blew with the trumpets: and the ark of the covenant of the LORD followed them. And the armed men went before the priests that blew with the trumpets, and the rereward came after the ark, the priests going on, and blowing with the trumpets.","ref":"Joshua 6:8-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"We understand and know that God designed the trumpets for gathering the people (as we read in Numbers), but we also understand that they were used to signify war (as we read in Numbers 10:9-10). The horns keep everything in order and airlock tight! It seems that Moses (or someone later on) eventually made SEVEN horns to split between the multiple tribes (two horns wouldn’t cut it for the amount of people). The trumpets were blown, and the shouts were proclaimed, the walls fell, and the people went in. It seems the same amount of horns will have to be made around the world for the same victory to take place…"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even still today, bugle calls are a traditional use for our military (granted we have advanced technology like radios to get people in proper order, but in places where you can’t radio, or where you don’t have a radio, a horn is still an extremely useful tool). In those days, there was no other way for a commander to give orders during a time of battle. It was common in the military to get people in order through trumpets."},{"kind":"para","text":"These trumpets are significant of these same things. Order, and then preparation for attack. I wouldn’t see God preparing us for generations the same way just to give up at the last call to battle and do it completely different from what He has always done. Especially (like I’ve said) because it doesn’t line up with everything else we are able to read in Revelation which is an exact replica and display of things that God has done in the past (granted on smaller scales before)."}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I don’t know if you’ve ever used incense before, but it makes it very difficult to smell anything else when you have it lit. It doesn’t always smell bad, but more times than not it’s way too strong, especially if it’s in a small place with not much room for the scent to go. Here we see the angel offer up prayers to the Lord with incense. I believe this symbolizes a few things."},{"kind":"para","text":"In the Old Testament sanctuaries, the priests had two alters. One for the sacrifice of the animals for sins, the other was for incense near the Holy place (Exodus 27:1-8)(Exodus 30:1-10). But John sees only ONE altar in Heaven fulfilling BOTH functions. Which is stated in verse 4… The incense (even during the Old Testament) represented the prayers of the saints:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let my prayer be set forth before thee as incense; and the lifting up of my hands as the evening sacrifice.","ref":"Psalm 141:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"I also believe the incense gave the prayers a sweet-smelling savor to God. When we think of it this way, we see that God’s senses are pleased by things that are specifically lenient on Him. This even depicts the sacrifice of His own Son on the cross for it was the altar in which all sin was forgiven forever!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And walk in love, as Christ also hath loved us, and hath given himself for us an offering and a sacrifice to God for a sweetsmelling savour.","ref":"Ephesians 5:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"But then, these prayers mixed with the fire from the altar (the one in which the prayers and sacrifices of the saints of God were held) are then flung to Earth in answer to their prayers."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"In case you don’t remember the chapter 6 prayer:"},{"kind":"para","text":"“And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Lord, holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?”"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is now answering the prayers of the martyred saints on the altar, which gives the understanding and conclusion of its existence. Their sacrifice was to fulfill the time of God’s waiting, so that His wrath will be poured out on those that have still continued to disobey and have turned the earth into a nightmare."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The angels were ready to start this, and this is the time in which the war would commence. This is when things begin to get serious, and the Earth will look for a solution to stopping God’s plan, which they will find in (spoiler alert) Satan in the chapters to come. But these angels were ready, and God already knew the full outcome of this war that was about to commence."},{"kind":"para","text":"He, honestly (if I may say), didn’t even have to know. He would still win… Because He’s God… It’s funny to me when people argue with the Bible. They are always proven wrong, and then they look dumb for fighting with God. Which is a great reminder to us, by the way. When someone is angry with you for referring to God’s Word, they aren’t really angry with you (you didn’t write the Bible), they are angry with God, but you are just the person they take it out on."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"title":"The First Trumpet","entries":[{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These coming trials are interestingly familiar. This same type of trial, “hail and fire, mixed with blood,” is found in the seventh plague of Egypt when Moses is trying to free God’s people to go worship Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"So there was hail, and fire mingled with the hail, very grievous, such as there was none like it in all the land of Egypt since it became a nation.","ref":"Exodus 9:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"Granted, this will be for a different cause and time, but it just goes to show that the God of the Old Testament is the same as the God of the New Testament, and He will never change even at the end of the world. That’s how we know we can trust Him, because He is always faithful."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"title":"The Second Trumpet","entries":[{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The sea becoming blood also represents a type of plague in the story of Moses as well. But this seemingly also echoes something from the book of Jeremiah."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, I am against thee, O destroying mountain, saith the Lord, which destroyest all the earth: and I will stretch out mine hand upon thee, and roll thee down from the rocks, and will make thee a burnt mountain… The sea is come up upon Babylon: she is covered with the multitude of the waves thereof.","ref":"Jeremiah 51:25;42"},{"kind":"para","text":"Mind you, if God has done these things before, it should not be surprising to us if He is able to do them again at the end of the world. We are always often dumbfounded by miracles all the time, yet we know that God has always performed miracles, and He will always do them with or without our belief. He does what is right. Period."}]}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"title":"The Third Trumpet","entries":[{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Wormwood is a bitter-tasting plant with a poisonous extract. Apparently, a star with these same kinds of attributes will make a third of the rivers and springs completely undrinkable, exactly like the Nile when Moses turned it to blood."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And all the Egyptians digged round about the river for water to drink; for they could not drink of the water of the river.","ref":"Exodus 7:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"Usually, when a city was under attack, they would surrender when their water supply was polluted or cut off because that was their main source of living. You can live without many things in this life, but water is the most needful."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the rest of the acts of Hezekiah, and all his might, and how he made a pool, and a conduit, and brought water into the city, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?","ref":"2 Kings 20:20"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"This same Hezekiah also stopped the upper watercourse of Gihon, and brought it straight down to the west side of the city of David. And Hezekiah prospered in all his works.","ref":"2 Chronicles 32:30"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"There is a river, the streams whereof shall make glad the city of God, the holy place of the tabernacles of the most High.","ref":"Psalm 46:4"}]}]},{"start":12,"end":13,"title":"The Fourth Trumpet","entries":[{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Yet again, this mimics the same as the ninth plague of Egypt during the time when Moses was trying to free God’s people."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the Lord said unto Moses, Stretch out thine hand toward heaven, that there may be darkness over the land of Egypt, even darkness which may be felt. And Moses stretched forth his hand toward heaven; and there was a thick darkness in all the land of Egypt three days: They saw not one another, neither rose any from his place for three days: but all the children of Israel had light in their dwellings.","ref":"Exodus 10:21-23"},{"kind":"para","text":"Some scholars believe that this may take place around the same time as the sixth seal…which reads (in case we don’t remember):"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the stars of heaven fell unto the earth, even as a fig tree casteth her untimely figs, when she is shaken of a mighty wind.","ref":"Revelation 6:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Some also believe that the sky will be darkened because of all the smoke from the burning cities once the stars fall and a third of the Earth is completely left useless."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Yet again, leaving us on a low note, without the last three trumpets, an angel prepares us for what is about to happen next without revealing the details quite yet. It seems these first four trumpets were to reveal the Earth’s hopelessness, God forcing them to be backed into a corner with nowhere to go. It seemingly looks impossible to survive on this Earth at this point."},{"kind":"para","text":"The angel says, “Woe, woe, woe” indicating that the last three trumpets are even worse (one trumpet for each woe)! These things that have taken place so far are merely warnings compared to what is about to happen with the last three trumpets. Even still, there are some key factors that God is brushing over and hasn’t revealed yet that will cause all of this to become as bad as it seems."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s not just that God’s angry because the people have sinned against Him. It’s worse than that. See, it’s possible to sin against God, we understand that. David realizes that, when he sleeps with someone else’s wife and then kills her husband. He feels guilty and prays to God:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Against thee, thee only, have I sinned, and done this evil in thy sight: that thou mightest be justified when thou speakest, and be clear when thou judgest.","ref":"Psalm 51:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"But he also sinned against this other woman, in which he killed her husband over. I’m sure there was a time when he apologized to her, but it’s far worse to sin against God than it is to sin against others. However, God is not pleased when we are doing evil and wicked things against other people too! It’s because of this (and the fact that we sin against Him combined) that God’s judgement must be executed. We could look to Sodom and Gomorrah for a small picture of this…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Abraham drew near, and said, Wilt thou also destroy the righteous with the wicked? Peradventure there be fifty righteous within the city: wilt thou also destroy and not spare the place for the fifty righteous that are therein? That be far from thee to do after this manner, to slay the righteous with the wicked: and that the righteous should be as the wicked, that be far from thee: Shall not the Judge of all the earth do right? And the LORD said, If I find in Sodom fifty righteous within the city, then I will spare all the place for their sakes. And Abraham answered and said, Behold now, I have taken upon me to speak unto the Lord, which am but dust and ashes: Peradventure there shall lack five of the fifty righteous: wilt thou destroy all the city for lack of five? And he said, If I find there forty and five, I will not destroy it. And he spake unto him yet again, and said, Peradventure there shall be forty found there. And he said, I will not do it for forty's sake. And he said unto him, Oh let not the Lord be angry, and I will speak: Peradventure there shall thirty be found there. And he said, I will not do it, if I find thirty there. And he said, Behold now, I have taken upon me to speak unto the Lord: Peradventure there shall be twenty found there. And he said, I will not destroy it for twenty's sake. And he said, Oh let not the Lord be angry, and I will speak yet but this once: Peradventure ten shall be found there. And he said, I will not destroy it for ten's sake.","ref":"Genesis 18:23-32"},{"kind":"para","text":"During the time of Noah, things were extremely bad:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God saw that the wickedness of man was great in the earth, and that every imagination of the thoughts of his heart was only evil continually. And it repented the LORD that he had made man on the earth, and it grieved him at his heart. And the LORD said, I will destroy man whom I have created from the face of the earth; both man, and beast, and the creeping thing, and the fowls of the air; for it repenteth me that I have made them. But Noah found grace in the eyes of the LORD.","ref":"Genesis 6:5-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even during the time of Judges:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In those days there was no king in Israel: every man did that which was right in his own eyes.","ref":"Judges 21:25"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because everyone did what THEY thought was right, famine, war, and trials of all kinds came to God’s children, and God could not meet with them. You could take several other accounts as well, during the time of Jonah with Nineveh; God saved that city because they repented at Jonah’s preaching. During all of these times, they all had one thing in common. God found one family of justified people in Sodom and Gomorrah and got them to safety, but the city had to be destroyed. During the time of Noah, He found favor in Noah’s family, so He saved that one family alone. During the judges, they finally turned back to the Lord, and God visited them once again. During the time of Nineveh, Jonah preaches to them, and they take it seriously, saving their city. During the last days… No one will turn to God. No one will even try."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even though God proves Himself before them and continuously gives them chance after chance, they simply won’t do it. They would rather die in destruction than believe in the Lord. They would rather spend an eternity in suffering and pain and hope that it doesn’t exist, over taking the obvious signs of God’s wrath and repenting. And it’s because of this that there will be none left for salvation on this Earth. Man is not getting less sinful, only more. As time comes by, we become more and more accepting of sin and that lifestyle, and it should not be a surprise to us that the Bible is being proven right every second that passes on this Earth."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13}],"verses":{"1":"And when he had opened the seventh seal, there was silence in heaven about the space of half an hour.","2":"And I saw the seven angels which stood before God; and to them were given seven trumpets.","3":"And another angel came and stood at the altar, having a golden censer; and there was given unto him much incense, that he should offer it with the prayers of all saints upon the golden altar which was before the throne.","4":"And the smoke of the incense, which came with the prayers of the saints, ascended up before God out of the angel's hand.","5":"And the angel took the censer, and filled it with fire of the altar, and cast it into the earth: and there were voices, and thunderings, and lightnings, and an earthquake.","6":"And the seven angels which had the seven trumpets prepared themselves to sound.","7":"The first angel sounded, and there followed hail and fire mingled with blood, and they were cast upon the earth: and the third part of trees was burnt up, and all green grass was burnt up.","8":"And the second angel sounded, and as it were a great mountain burning with fire was cast into the sea: and the third part of the sea became blood;","9":"And the third part of the creatures which were in the sea, and had life, died; and the third part of the ships were destroyed.","10":"And the third angel sounded, and there fell a great star from heaven, burning as it were a lamp, and it fell upon the third part of the rivers, and upon the fountains of waters;","11":"And the name of the star is called Wormwood: and the third part of the waters became wormwood; and many men died of the waters, because they were made bitter.","12":"And the fourth angel sounded, and the third part of the sun was smitten, and the third part of the moon, and the third part of the stars; so as the third part of them was darkened, and the day shone not for a third part of it, and the night likewise.","13":"And I beheld, and heard an angel flying through the midst of heaven, saying with a loud voice, Woe, woe, woe, to the inhabiters of the earth by reason of the other voices of the trumpet of the three angels, which are yet to sound!"}},
    "9": {"chapter":9,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 09"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In chapter 8, we see the entrance of the seven trumpets after opening up the last of the seven seals. This last seal brings a lot of suffering and sorrow at this point. We only got to read about the first 4 trumpets, and there’s a large indication that the last three trumpets will be the worst of them all by the last verse of our last chapter."},{"kind":"para","text":"The first trumpet led to hail and fire mixed with blood falling on the Earth, causing a third of the earth’s trees and grass to burn up."},{"kind":"para","text":"The second trumpet led to a third of the sea becoming blood and useless, and a third of the creatures in the sea were killed, also devastating a third of the ships that were in the sea as well."},{"kind":"para","text":"The third trumpet led to a star falling from the sky and making a third of all drinkable water completely undrinkable and poisonous."},{"kind":"para","text":"The fourth trumpet led to a third of the sun, moon, and stars being darkened and a third of the day was made to be night. So the night will last longer than the day."},{"kind":"para","text":"The three woe’s indicated at the end of the chapter suggest that the non-Christians will experience woe’s (W-O-E’s) whereas the Christians will experience woah’s (W-O-A-H’s). We will be left on yet another cliffhanger in this chapter, but we should be use to that by now."}],"previously":["In chapter 8, we see the entrance of the seven trumpets after opening up the last of the seven seals. This last seal brings a lot of suffering and sorrow at this point. We only got to read about the first 4 trumpets, and there’s a large indication that the last three trumpets will be the worst of them all by the last verse of our last chapter. The first trumpet led to hail and fire mixed with blood falling on the Earth, causing a third of the Earth’s trees and grass to burn up. The second trumpet led to a third of the sea becoming blood and useless, and a third of the creatures in the sea were killed, also devastating a third of the ships that were in the sea as well. The third trumpet led to a star falling from the sky and making a third of all drinkable water completely undrinkable and poisonous. The fourth trumpet led to a third of the sun, moon, and stars being darkened and a third of the day was made to be night. So the night will last longer than the day. The three woe’s indicated at the end of the chapter suggest that the non-Christians will experience woe’s (W-O-E’s) whereas the Christians will experience woah’s (W-O-A-H’s). We will be left on yet another cliffhanger in this chapter, but we should be used to that by now."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":12,"title":"The Fifth Trumpet","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This key was given to Satan to open up hell so that the demons could be set free to do what they pleased (more on this later). I understand this to be Satan because it’s mentioned in verse 11 (which we will get to), but he is also seen coming into the picture the same way he fell from heaven the first time."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said unto them, I beheld Satan as lightning fall from heaven.","ref":"Luke 10:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"This was not by accident either. God allows this to happen (I believe) for a few reasons."},{"kind":"para","text":"To show us that He can control all demons including Satan himself."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Jesus came and spake unto them, saying, All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth.","ref":"Matthew 28:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"So the devils besought him, saying, If thou cast us out, suffer us to go away in the herd of swine. And he said unto them, Go. And when they were come out, they went into the herd of swine: and, behold, the whole herd of swine ran violently down a steep place into the sea, and perished in the waters.","ref":"Matthew 8:31-32"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou believest that there is one God; thou doest well: the devils also believe, and tremble.","ref":"James 2:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"To give the people what they desire."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe a great majority of people during this time will look for idols to worship. They will continue to live their lives in false worship just like they did before. They will shun God and create whatever idol that makes them feel good about their bad decisions. Nothing will ultimately change at the end of the world because they still won’t follow God even after God gets their attention through the first FOUR trumpets!"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is literally how it is today. People have viewed this COVID pandemic and thought to themselves “It’s this person’s fault, it’s that person’s fault, it’s this city or that city, it’s this state or that state. This person is overreacting, that person is being too paranoid, this person hates everyone, that person is too accepting of vaccines…” etc. When in reality, God has control of all things, including what types of diseases are in the world. He could literally take away cancer if He saw fit to do so. He could take COVID away. He could have made it possible to continue our mundane everyday lives without us ever experiencing something like this. Yet He didn’t."},{"kind":"para","text":"He allowed us to experience it, and one of the first places that was attacked was the church for a reason. God tested the world’s faith, and nearly the entire world failed already! And this isn’t even the final test which is written about here in the Bible. If this is how we are acting at this significantly smaller test now, what makes us think we will be any better or different when this comes?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations; Knowing this, that the trying of your faith worketh patience. But let patience have her perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, wanting nothing.","ref":"James 1:2-4"},{"kind":"para","text":"We’ve missed the mark altogether. If COVID has revealed anything, it has revealed how little patience Christians actually have. It has revealed who is walking by grace, and who is faking it. Those with grace won’t just show it to those that are saved, they will show it to those that aren’t. Those that walk by grace desire all men to be saved, and would be willing to do whatever it took to make sure they heard the gospel. They can’t save others, but they can certainly show grace. It’s easy to tell who is walking by grace and who is not. God’s grace labors through us, and gives us the desire to do God’s work and will."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But by the grace of God I am what I am: and his grace which was bestowed upon me was not in vain; but I laboured more abundantly than they all: yet not I, but the grace of God which was with me.","ref":"1 Corinthians 15:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s grace helps us know the right direction, and the right words to say to those that don’t know Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Walk in wisdom toward them that are without, redeeming the time. Let your speech be alway with grace, seasoned with salt, that ye may know how ye ought to answer every man.","ref":"Colossians 4:5-6"},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s grace allows us to pray promptly in the way that we should, knowing that God hears us and desires to converse with us."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let us therefore come boldly unto the throne of grace, that we may obtain mercy, and find grace to help in time of need.","ref":"Hebrews 4:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s grace doesn’t just end at salvation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou therefore, my son, be strong in the grace that is in Christ Jesus.","ref":"2 Timothy 2:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"God bestows grace on us so we know how to be graceful to others. Jesus demonstrates this through a parable…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then came Peter to him, and said, Lord, how oft shall my brother sin against me, and I forgive him? till seven times? Jesus saith unto him, I say not unto thee, Until seven times: but, Until seventy times seven. Therefore is the kingdom of heaven likened unto a certain king, which would take account of his servants. And when he had begun to reckon, one was brought unto him, which owed him ten thousand talents. But forasmuch as he had not to pay, his lord commanded him to be sold, and his wife, and children, and all that he had, and payment to be made. The servant therefore fell down, and worshipped him, saying, Lord, have patience with me, and I will pay thee all. Then the lord of that servant was moved with compassion, and loosed him, and forgave him the debt. But the same servant went out, and found one of his fellowservants, which owed him an hundred pence: and he laid hands on him, and took him by the throat, saying, Pay me that thou owest. And his fellowservant fell down at his feet, and besought him, saying, Have patience with me, and I will pay thee all. And he would not: but went and cast him into prison, till he should pay the debt. So when his fellowservants saw what was done, they were very sorry, and came and told unto their lord all that was done. Then his lord, after that he had called him, said unto him, O thou wicked servant, I forgave thee all that debt, because thou desiredst me: Shouldest not thou also have had compassion on thy fellowservant, even as I had pity on thee? And his lord was wroth, and delivered him to the tormentors, till he should pay all that was due unto him. So likewise shall my heavenly Father do also unto you, if ye from your hearts forgive not every one his brother their trespasses.","ref":"Matthew 18:21-35"},{"kind":"para","text":"May we bring this to memory when it involves what kind of grace we desire from the Lord. Whatever type of grace we give to others is a direct reflection of the type of grace we will receive from the Father of all grace."}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The smoke coming out of the ground like a “great furnace” is a representation of what hell will more than likely be like. We already heard several descriptions of hell being told throughout scripture, but there is never really any clear-cut imagery that lets us know how Hell will be. We understand it will be hot:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And shall cast them into the furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.","ref":"Matthew 13:50"},{"kind":"para","text":"We understand that those who do not accept salvation will end up there rather than Heaven."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But I will forewarn you whom ye shall fear: Fear him, which after he hath killed hath power to cast into hell; yea, I say unto you, Fear him.","ref":"Luke 12:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.","ref":"Revelation 20:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"We understand that it was not made for us, but for Satan and his demons, and the only reason we end up there is because of our disobedience to God and the rejection of His gift from Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then shall he say also unto them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels:","ref":"Matthew 25:41"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s a pretty good assumption that the imagery here is the angel opening up hell to allow demons to roam and hunt on Earth, freely. These people will never accept Christ, and they are continuing to live in sin and destruction, which is exactly what demons enjoy feeding on. Satan and his demons love to kill. God and Jesus love to give life."},{"kind":"para","text":"First, we see these creepy locust-like things. This is another plague that mimics the eighth plague of Egypt."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the locust went up over all the land of Egypt, and rested in all the coasts of Egypt: very grievous were they; before them there were no such locusts as they, neither after them shall be such. For they covered the face of the whole earth, so that the land was darkened; and they did eat every herb of the land, and all the fruit of the trees which the hail had left: and there remained not any green thing in the trees, or in the herbs of the field, through all the land of Egypt.","ref":"Exodus 10:14-15"},{"kind":"para","text":"It seems God continues to use those same plagues already provenly used in the Old Testament as a lesser example of what is to come. Locusts, however, usually eat up the vegetation and food supply that are growing throughout the land. Throughout the years, we have seen many locusts plague countries and destroy nearly everything."},{"kind":"para","text":"In 2020, there was a plague of locusts that came to Ethiopia, destroying everything in their path. Somalia in 2019. Israel in 2013. And we could go on a whole list all the way back to Egypt in the Old Testament."},{"kind":"para","text":"My point is, these locust attacks are going to be very different compared to what God has in store here. These locusts will not even touch the vegetation and food supply. They won’t even look like locusts; they will just swarm like them. They will more than likely be demonic spirits that will attack, rather than insects. And we assume this by the description that will be revealed in the coming verses."}]},{"start":4,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a terrible experience. God will make them live in agony for five months, and they won’t even be able to die. They may even try to kill themselves but won’t be successful. While this seems harsh and cruel, it will be well deserved for the kinds of lives these people will live, and the disgusting acts they have caused to those that love God (more on how that was later). It will be more than deserved."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of his saints.","ref":"Psalm 116:15"}]},{"start":7,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These creatures will be awfully disgusting. I wouldn’t expect anything less from demons, though, to be honest. Maybe this is truly how demons will look? They will show their actual selves at the end of the world. Satan will look different, too. He used to look like an angel, as these demons looked as well. When they decided to live for sin, it changed their appearance into something frightening. Sin always reveals how people really look."}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“Apollyon” means “destroyer.” We understand this name to be Satan’s because that is all Satan does. He destroys."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy: I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly.","ref":"John 10:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of God was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.","ref":"1 John 3:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"It should not be hard for us to be able to tell who is used by Satan and who is not."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is just the first woe, and it already seems awful enough. But, of course, it can still get much worse. When I was younger, I was told that every bad situation could always be worse. I said, “Well, what if I’m homeless?” They said, “It could be raining.” So I said, “Well, what if I’m homeless in the rain?” They said, “You could be hungry.” So I said, “What if I’m homeless, in the rain, and hungry?” They said, “You could be cold.” So I said, “What if I’m homeless, in the rain, hungry, and cold?” They said, “You could be dead.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"The point was, it could always look worse. But how much worse could the end of the world and an eternity in Hell be?"}]}]},{"start":13,"end":21,"title":"The Sixth Trumpet","entries":[{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This golden alter is the same one that held the prayers of the saints in chapter eight."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the smoke of the incense, which came with the prayers of the saints, ascended up before God out of the angel’s hand. And the angel took the censer, and filled it with fire of the altar, and cast it into the earth: and there were voices, and thunderings, and lightnings, and an earthquake.","ref":"Revelation 8:4-5"}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Great River Euphrates marked the eastern boundary of Rome’s influence during the time that John was writing this. If you went past the river, there were great armies who threatened the empire. The river is to represent the only thing holding back chaos and destruction. The releasing of the four angels was to represent unprecedented amounts of bloodshed and suffering."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God is working in thirds. Not everyone will be killed off, but a THIRD of everyone will be killed by these four angels. These angels’ whole purpose for existence was for this specific reason. They were waiting for this specific moment."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The number of troops is equivalent to two hundred million. These troops are to represent demons, not the humans who were on Earth (we will learn more about that in a second). Though the demons may have two hundred million troops, it is nothing compared to those who worship God, in case you don’t remember…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"After this I beheld, and, lo, a great multitude, which no man could number, of all nations, and kindreds, and people, and tongues, stood before the throne, and before the Lamb, clothed with white robes, and palms in their hands;","ref":"Revelation 7:9"}]},{"start":17,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These are obviously not normal people, and they are not normal horses. The demons that have been released think they might have one over on God and are capable of sticking up for themselves. But we will soon see how that plays out for them."}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s no surprise. Mankind is addicted to sin and idols. Even if everything seems to fall apart, they will be seen cleaving to their addictions."},{"kind":"para","text":"I read a book about mummies to Melody for one of her school lessons in history, and we talked about how they found King Tut’s tomb. One of the most interesting things to Melody was that they found a bunch of treasures and golden things buried with him. She asked, “Why did they place all of his precious belongings with him?” That’s a fair question. I explained, “Back then, they believed that they would receive their possessions in the afterlife if they were buried with them.” They thought that their earthly possessions were worth eternal rewards."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, this is nothing new, and it’s something that will never stop until everything is completely destroyed and sin is completely vanquished."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Repentance means nothing if we are not turning to God. They cannot repent unless they trust in Christ. A phony repentance will not save a man, and it will not open their eyes to the truth that is all around them. They could see a third of everything on Earth completely destroyed and still hold to their sins because they simply don’t want to believe in God. They will get what they desire, but they will only receive what they desire here. They cannot take what they want with them after they die. And even if they are buried with it and think they could take it like the mummies in their tombs, God will burn everything up with fire eventually anyway so that there is nothing left here on Earth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will bring the third part through the fire, and will refine them as silver is refined, and will try them as gold is tried: they shall call on my name, and I will hear them: I will say, It is my people: and they shall say, The Lord is my God.","ref":"Zechariah 13:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Every man’s work shall be made manifest: for the day shall declare it, because it shall be revealed by fire; and the fire shall try every man’s work of what sort it is. If any man’s work abide which he hath built thereupon, he shall receive a reward. If any man’s work shall be burned, he shall suffer loss: but he himself shall be saved; yet so as by fire.","ref":"1 Corinthians 3:13-15"},{"kind":"para","text":"Those that have faith in God, even after being tried with fire, will stand. How will that look for us? It is possible to go into Heaven with nothing to show for it. It’s possible to go into Heaven without sowing seeds. But is it possible for a Christian to live comfortably without applying God’s Will to their lives? Is it possible to live freely in this life without owing everything to the Lord? What will your life look like when everything is tried by fire?"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21}],"verses":{"1":"And the fifth angel sounded, and I saw a star fall from heaven unto the earth: and to him was given the key of the bottomless pit.","2":"And he opened the bottomless pit; and there arose a smoke out of the pit, as the smoke of a great furnace; and the sun and the air were darkened by reason of the smoke of the pit.","3":"And there came out of the smoke locusts upon the earth: and unto them was given power, as the scorpions of the earth have power.","4":"And it was commanded them that they should not hurt the grass of the earth, neither any green thing, neither any tree; but only those men which have not the seal of God in their foreheads.","5":"And to them it was given that they should not kill them, but that they should be tormented five months: and their torment was as the torment of a scorpion, when he striketh a man.","6":"And in those days shall men seek death, and shall not find it; and shall desire to die, and death shall flee from them.","7":"And the shapes of the locusts were like unto horses prepared unto battle; and on their heads were as it were crowns like gold, and their faces were as the faces of men.","8":"And they had hair as the hair of women, and their teeth were as the teeth of lions.","9":"And they had breastplates, as it were breastplates of iron; and the sound of their wings was as the sound of chariots of many horses running to battle.","10":"And they had tails like unto scorpions, and there were stings in their tails: and their power was to hurt men five months.","11":"And they had a king over them, which is the angel of the bottomless pit, whose name in the Hebrew tongue is Abaddon, but in the Greek tongue hath his name Apollyon.","12":"One woe is past; and, behold, there come two woes more hereafter.","13":"And the sixth angel sounded, and I heard a voice from the four horns of the golden altar which is before God,","14":"Saying to the sixth angel which had the trumpet, Loose the four angels which are bound in the great river Euphrates.","15":"And the four angels were loosed, which were prepared for an hour, and a day, and a month, and a year, for to slay the third part of men.","16":"And the number of the army of the horsemen were two hundred thousand thousand: and I heard the number of them.","17":"And thus I saw the horses in the vision, and them that sat on them, having breastplates of fire, and of jacinth, and brimstone: and the heads of the horses were as the heads of lions; and out of their mouths issued fire and smoke and brimstone.","18":"By these three was the third part of men killed, by the fire, and by the smoke, and by the brimstone, which issued out of their mouths.","19":"For their power is in their mouth, and in their tails: for their tails were like unto serpents, and had heads, and with them they do hurt.","20":"And the rest of the men which were not killed by these plagues yet repented not of the works of their hands, that they should not worship devils, and idols of gold, and silver, and brass, and stone, and of wood: which neither can see, nor hear, nor walk:","21":"Neither repented they of their murders, nor of their sorceries, nor of their fornication, nor of their thefts."}},
    "10": {"chapter":10,"intro":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"Neither repented they of their murders, nor their sorceries, nor of their fornication, nor of their thefts.","ref":"Revelation 9:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"In this chapter of Revelation, there is quite a bit of symbolism here. There’s a slight pause from the trumpets of the angels to reveal something that isn’t quite opened up here in this chapter. There is more information about this in the chapters to come, but this chapter gives some prerequisites about the things that are eventually coming."},{"kind":"para","text":"We understand that, so far, nothing has been that great for the people that are remaining on Earth, and it doesn’t seem to get much better. Yet, we still see God’s grace bestowed upon an Earth and people who are openly mocking and rejecting Him."}],"previously":["We saw in our last chapter the fifth trumpet sound which brought these crazy ScorpionHorseLocustPeopleOutOfHell-like things, and ruined the lives of those that were against God and His people. The angel who opened up the bottomless pit’s name is Apollyon. Then the 6th trumpet sounded which brought death to a third part of the humans of the earth, allowing for God to continually show the open door of salvation even still, but people will continue to reject Christ as the last verse indicates:"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":7,"title":"The Mighty Angel and the Little Book","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I think it really helps if we read the last two verses from our last chapter."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the rest of the men which were not killed by these plagues yet repented not of the works of their hands, that they should not worship devils, and idols of gold, and silver, and brass, and stone, and of wood: which neither can see, nor hear, nor walk: Neither repented they of their murders, nor of their sorceries, nor of their fornication, nor of their thefts.","ref":"Revelation 9:20-21"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we look at these verses, we (who are saved) instantly think that “these people are stupid for turning their backs on God even though God has shown Himself through all these plagues and tribulations!” While it may seem stupid, it’s also nothing new."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The thing that hath been, it is that which shall be; and that which is done is that which shall be done: and there is no new thing under the sun.","ref":"Ecclesiastes 1:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In those days there was no king in Israel: every man did that which was right in his own eyes.","ref":"Judges 21:25"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"As it is written, There is none righteous, no, not one: There is none that understandeth, there is none that seeketh after God.","ref":"Romans 3:10-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Bible is filled with story after story of people turning away from God, even though God showed Himself mighty, and even after God literally had just PROTECTED them and FREED them!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he gave unto Moses, when he had made an end of communing with him upon mount Sinai, two tables of testimony, tables of stone, written with the finger of God…And when the people saw that Moses delayed to come down out of the mount, the people gathered themselves together unto Aaron, and said unto him, Up, make us gods, which shall go before us; for as for this Moses, the man that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we wot not what is become of him. And Aaron said unto them, Break off the golden earrings, which are in the ears of your wives, of your sons, and of your daughters, and bring them unto me. And all the people brake off the golden earrings which were in their ears, and brought them unto Aaron. And he received them at their hand, and fashioned it with a graving tool, after he had made it a molten calf: and they said, These be thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.","ref":"Exodus 32:18;32:1-4"}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This gives a great picture of God’s presence and holiness in the life of a believer. Like God on the throne, this angel is surrounded by a rainbow."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he that sat was to look upon like a jasper and a sardine stone: and there was a rainbow round about the throne, in sight like unto an emerald.","ref":"Revelation 4:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he had in his right hand seven stars: and out of his mouth went a sharp twoedged sword: and his countenance was as the sun shineth in his strength.","ref":"Revelation 1:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Like God’s glory and presence in the wilderness, his legs were like pillars of fire!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the Lord went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light; to go by day and night: He took not away the pillar of the cloud by day, nor the pillar of fire by night, from before the people.","ref":"Exodus 13:21-22"},{"kind":"para","text":"Like the Lion of Judah, His voice was as if it were a roaring lion!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And of the elders saith unto me, Weep not: behold, the Lion of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, hath prevailed to open the book, and to loose the seven seals thereof.","ref":"Revelation 5:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"This angel was created to display the splendid attributes of God’s glory, His presence, His authority, and His salvation (or promises if you will). No doubt, a sight to behold by John here. Even while this angel spoke, there were seven thunders that sounded."},{"kind":"para","text":"This picture of the angel’s left foot being on land, and right foot being in water displays the size of the angel. We come under the assumption that this was not a normally sized being. And when it speaks about the scroll, John says the scroll is “little” once again insinuating that, in the portion of the size of this angel, this was not any normally sized being."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Some heavenly secrets will not be revealed in this life. We will have to wait for Heaven to hear and see the things in which God has not fully revealed to us now. Sometimes the things that God doesn’t reveal to us are for our own benefit (maybe even leading us in the way that He wants us to go, and we wouldn’t go that way if we saw the things God has kept secret). Sometimes the things that God doesn’t reveal to us are because of our sin (we don’t allow blessings from God because we are not living in fellowship with God. How can God reveal His truths to us if we are battling against His Spirit which leads us into all truth?)"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Howbeit when he, the Spirit of truth, is come, he will guide you into all truth: for he shall not speak of himself; but whatsoever he shall hear, that shall he speak: and he will shew you things to come.","ref":"John 16:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The secret things belong unto the Lord our God: but those things which are revealed belong unto us and to our children for ever, that we may do all the words of this law.","ref":"Deuteronomy 29:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is said that the Bible reveals more things about Hell than it does about Heaven. I believe that’s on purpose. Heaven is a place that may seem mysterious to many, but it’s certainly a place that draws our attention because of what we don’t know about it. We know more about Hell, and because of this, we want to avoid it at all costs. The more we know about Hell, the more we understand we don’t want to go there. I believe the wait will be worth the mystery once we get to Heaven and are in the presence of the Lord."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I read that people have the belief that this depicts unity in God’s created order. One foot on the sea, one on the land, and the right hand raised to Heaven."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God said, Let there be a firmament in the midst of the waters, and let it divide the waters from the waters. And God made the firmament, and divided the waters which were under the firmament from the waters which were above the firmament: and it was so. And God called the firmament Heaven. And the evening and the morning were the second day. And God said, Let the waters under the heaven be gathered together unto one place, and let the dry land appear: and it was so. And God called the dry land Earth; and the gathering together of the waters called he Seas: and God saw that it was good.","ref":"Genesis 1:6-10"},{"kind":"para","text":"It may symbolize that, and it would be respectable too, because of the majesty of this angel and the way he (it?) was created. It especially would make sense in this chapter at this particular time with how the things are going. God is finishing his intended purpose for the world, and bringing all things to an end, and what better way to come full circle and visualize the finality of all things but with the unity between God and His creation?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Endeavouring to keep the unity of the Spirit in the bond of peace.","ref":"Ephesians 4:3"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“…that there should be no time longer…” or “no more delay.” God’s sovereignty knows that there are none else that will be saved, but God’s grace gives us chance after chance to receive it. There comes a point, though, where God must end it, because there is no more reason to delay. But even with God’s final ruling on the matter, we will see (in the next chapter) that God will allow (still) more opportunities for change, and nothing will come of it… (spoiler alert)."},{"kind":"para","text":"God cannot wait forever for those that won’t be saved. He must serve justice to those that are cruel and wicked. These people that were still alive are extremely wicked… In case we don’t remember as we’ve already read, these were what the people were like:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the rest of the men which were not killed by these plagues yet repented not of the works of their hands, that they should not worship devils, and idols of gold, and silver, and brass, and stone, and of wood: which neither can see, nor hear, nor walk: Neither repented they of their murders, nor of their sorceries, nor of their fornication, nor of their thefts.","ref":"Revelation 9:20-21"},{"kind":"para","text":"There comes a point where God must do what is right, and it would be wrong to continue to let these people go with their sins and not do anything about it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.","ref":"Romans 6:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"God has actually demonstrated this same patience and destruction before with Sodom and Gomorrah. When He let Abraham know that He would destroy the city, Abraham tried to plead with God (knowing that Lot, part of Abraham’s family, was living there). God told him, “If there are 10 just people, I will not destroy it.” However, when the angels get there, the people are so given to their wickedness that they try to rape the angels as soon as they find out they are there."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they called unto Lot, and said unto him, Where are the men which came in to thee this night? Bring them out unto us, that we may know them.","ref":"Genesis 19:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"They even try to break into Lots house to get to them…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they said, Stand back. And they said again, This one fellow came in to sojourn, and he will need be a judge: now will we deal worse with thee, than with them. And they pressed sore upon the man, even Lot, and came near to break the door.","ref":"Genesis 19:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"We know that the cities were destroyed after this, but Lot and his family were allowed a chance to escape, being told to “not look back.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And it came to pass, when they had brought them forth abroad, that he said, Escape for thy life; look not behind thee, neither stand thou in all the plain; escape to the mountain, lest thou be consumed.","ref":"Genesis 19:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"And of course we know that Lot’s wife looked back:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Jesus said unto him, No man, having put his hand to the plough, and looking back, is fit for the kingdom of God.","ref":"Luke 9:62"},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot afford to look back at our old life when God has given us a glorious and joyful new one. It does us no good to dream about the things which were before. Our flesh will tell us to look back, but the Spirit will tell us to keep moving forward, keeping our eyes on God. We see through this destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah that God knew there was no hope of salvation, and they needed to be killed off so they wouldn’t continue to destroy the world and the people that were in it."},{"kind":"para","text":"He’s going to see this at the end too, but the whole world will be in the same state of peril, and God will have no choice because of their sin which will continue to grow out of control. In fact, it was because of this that God had to flood the earth the first time in Genesis with Noah."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God saw that the wickedness of man was great in the earth, and that every imagination of the thoughts of his heart was only evil continually.","ref":"Genesis 6:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"This time of the world’s end (we are told) is supposed to be even worse than the time of Noah."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But as the days of Noah were, so shall also the coming of the Son of man be. For as in the days that were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noe entered into the ark, And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.","ref":"Matthew 24:37-39"},{"kind":"para","text":"But if we are to take anything from these scriptures, it would be that God purposely found favor in a few men who were able to be saved and were able to change the world. The world will not be destroyed as long as there is hope of salvation for those to come after us. There is still hope for us yet, but that hope dwindles more and more with each generation that comes and rejects God’s Will and salvation."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes, what we thought to be a mystery will eventually be revealed to us through another way, so that we are not left without hope. Eventually, the seven thunders mentioned above will be revealed to us, and we will be able to witness God’s fulfillment of everything He promised."}]}]},{"start":8,"end":11,"title":"The Little Book Eaten","entries":[{"start":8,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This description here, of “eating God’s Word,” is certainly symbolic in a few ways. First, it is how the believers are to take God’s Word."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thy words were found, and I did eat them; and thy word was unto me the joy and rejoicing of mine heart: for I am called by thy name, O Lord God of hosts.","ref":"Jeremiah 15:16"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Blessed are they which do hunger and thirst after righteousness: for they shall be filled.","ref":"Matthew 5:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"O taste and see that the Lord is good: blessed is the man that trusteth in him.","ref":"Psalm 34:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Second, it’s a direct reflection of which God ordains His prophets. John was ordained through this way to preach these things to those in his life, just as Ezekiel was to do the same."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, eat that thou findest; eat this roll, and go speak unto the house of Israel. So I opened my mouth, and he caused me to eat that roll. And he said unto me, Son of man, cause thy belly to eat, and fill thy bowels with this roll that I give thee. Then did I eat it; and it was in my mouth as honey for sweetness…Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, all of my words that I shall speak unto thee receive in thine heart, and hear with thine ears.","ref":"Ezekiel 3:1-3;10"},{"kind":"para","text":"It symbolizes that the child of God must receive God’s Word before we speak His Word."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth.","ref":"2 Timothy 2:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"If we are commanded to rightly divide God’s Word through reception of God’s Word, then it stands to reason that we can WRONGLY divide God’s Word by negligence of it. While this seems like a break from the craziness that we have been reading about through these chapters, this only sets up more craziness to take place. For God is not yet done with His work in this world, and He still has much to accomplish (though it may not take all that long when it comes to His Will) before He can give glory to all eternity without Satan ever being a problem (or solution in some cases as we will see) again…"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":11}],"verses":{"1":"And I saw another mighty angel come down from heaven, clothed with a cloud: and a rainbow was upon his head, and his face was as it were the sun, and his feet as pillars of fire:","2":"And he had in his hand a little book open: and he set his right foot upon the sea, and his left foot on the earth,","3":"And cried with a loud voice, as when a lion roareth: and when he had cried, seven thunders uttered their voices.","4":"And when the seven thunders had uttered their voices, I was about to write: and I heard a voice from heaven saying unto me, Seal up those things which the seven thunders uttered, and write them not.","5":"And the angel which I saw stand upon the sea and upon the earth lifted up his hand to heaven,","6":"And sware by him that liveth for ever and ever, who created heaven, and the things that therein are, and the earth, and the things that therein are, and the sea, and the things which are therein, that there should be time no longer:","7":"But in the days of the voice of the seventh angel, when he shall begin to sound, the mystery of God should be finished, as he hath declared to his servants the prophets.","8":"And the voice which I heard from heaven spake unto me again, and said, Go and take the little book which is open in the hand of the angel which standeth upon the sea and upon the earth.","9":"And I went unto the angel, and said unto him, Give me the little book. And he said unto me, Take it, and eat it up; and it shall make thy belly bitter, but it shall be in thy mouth sweet as honey.","10":"And I took the little book out of the angel's hand, and ate it up; and it was in my mouth sweet as honey: and as soon as I had eaten it, my belly was bitter.","11":"And he said unto me, Thou must prophesy again before many peoples, and nations, and tongues, and kings."}},
    "11": {"chapter":11,"intro":[],"previously":["We saw a supposedly giant angel (or mighty angel) having one foot in the sea, and one foot on land, raising a little book into the air towards Heaven, and we see John take the book and eat it. This opens up the rising of the anti-Christ and the end of all things."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"Gentiles Time to End in 42 Months","entries":[{"start":1,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There are people who believe this temple will be a rebuilding of the old Jewish temple in Jerusalem. This temple will be where the antichrist will take his seat and act as if he were God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who opposeth and exalteth himself above all that is called God, or that is worshipped; so that he as God sitteth in the temple of God, shewing himself that he is God.","ref":"2 Thessalonians 2:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"Others believe that this temple would represent a symbol for believers."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and that the Spirit of God dwelleth in you? If any man defile the temple of God, him shall God destroy; for the temple of God is holy, which temple ye are.","ref":"1 Corinthians 3:16-17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"To whom coming, as unto a living stone, disallowed indeed of men, but chosen of God, and precious, Ye also, as lively stones, are built up a spiritual house, an holy priesthood, to offer up spiritual sacrifices, acceptable to God by Jesus Christ. Wherefore also it is contained in the scripture, Behold, I lay in Sion a chief corner stone, elect, precious: and he that believeth on him shall not be confounded. Unto you therefore which believe he is precious: but unto them which be disobedient, the stone which the builders disallowed, the same is made the head of the corner, And a stone of stumbling, and a rock of offense, even to them which stumble at the word, being disobedient: whereunto also they were appointed. But ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people; that ye should shew forth the praises of him who hath called you out of darkness into his marvellous light; Which in time past were not a people, but are now the people of God: which had not obtained mercy, but now have obtained mercy.","ref":"1 Peter 2:4-10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Him that overcometh will I make a pillar in the temple of my God, and he shall go no more out: and I will write upon him the name of my God, and the name of the city of my God, which is new Jerusalem, which cometh down out of heaven from my God: and I will write upon him my new name.","ref":"Revelation 3:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw no temple therein: for the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are the temple of it.","ref":"Revelation 21:22"},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever the case may be, John is specifically instructed to not just measure the sanctuary and altar, but to also measure the people worshipping. When I worked in carpentry, the main portion of the job was to make measurements—precise measurements. If I was just a millimeter off, it would throw everything else off with it. The motto around the shop was always “Measure twice, cut once.” Because if you cut twice, the chances are you will not cut the right measurements. Basically, double-check your work."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes that is the way in which God works. He shows us our need for a proper measurement and cuts so that we are shaped exactly for His need and purpose. John is also instructed not to measure the outside of the temple because it will be given over to the nations anyway. Jesus speaks about this in Luke."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they shall fall by the edge of the sword, and shall be led away captive into all nations: and Jerusalem shall be trodden down of the Gentiles, until the times of the Gentiles be fulfilled.","ref":"Luke 21:24"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then I heard one saint speaking, and another saint said unto that certain saint which spake, How long shall be the vision concerning the daily sacrifice, and the transgression of desolation, to give both the sanctuary and the host to be trodden under foot?","ref":"Daniel 8:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s a lot of calculations of time here, which I won’t get too detailed with, but they are represented throughout the Bible as lining up to the actual events that are going to occur, which proves the authenticity of God’s prophecies. Equaling to 3 1/2 years or “1,260 days,” which is equivalent to about “42 months.”"}]}]},{"start":3,"end":14,"title":"The Two Witnesses to Prophesy 42 Months","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he shall speak great words against the most High, and shall wear out the saints of the most High, and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.","ref":"Daniel 7:25"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I heard the man clothed in linen, which was upon the waters of the river, when he held up his right hand and his left hand unto heaven, and swore by him that liveth for ever that it shall be for a time, times, and an half; and when he shall have accomplished to scatter the power of the holy people, all these things shall be finished.","ref":"Daniel 12:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"God has always made it relevant to require two witnesses to confirm or guarantee testimonies."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"One witness shall not rise up against a man for any iniquity, or for any sin, in any sin that he sinneth: at the mouth of two witnesses, or at the mouth of three witnesses, shall the matter be established.","ref":"Deuteronomy 19:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But if he will not hear thee, then take with thee one or two more, that in the mouth of two or three witnesses every word may be established.","ref":"Matthew 18:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Sackcloth is also a very biblical sign of repentance."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And it came to pass, when king Hezekiah heard it, that he rent his clothes, and covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the house of the Lord. And he sent Eliakim, who was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests covered with sackcloth, unto Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.","ref":"Isaiah 37:1-2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"So the people of Nineveh believed God, and proclaimed a fast, and put on sackcloth, from the greatest of them even to the least of them.","ref":"Jonah 3:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Woe unto thee, Chorazin! Woe unto thee, Bethsaida! For if the mighty works, which were done in you, had been done in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago in sackcloth and ashes.","ref":"Matthew 11:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is not a relevant practice today, though in some cultures, they might still engage in it. They would also pour ashes on their heads as a sign of distress and sometimes rip their clothes when upset."},{"kind":"para","text":"Maybe you have felt a desire, while hurt or sad, to tear at your clothes or simply lay on the floor in desperation. Because of the state of the world at that point, these two witnesses will serve as a sign of the difficulties during that time."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"John has been shown several objects since the beginning of this book as representations of Old Testament prophecies, as well as symbols of God’s holiness. These descriptions are no exceptions. The “two olive trees” comment here would likely represent the same vision in Zachariah as the “two anointed ones.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then answered I, and said unto him, What are these two olive trees upon the right side of the candlestick and upon the left side thereof? Then said he, These are the two anointed ones, that stand by the Lord of the whole earth.","ref":"Zechariah 4:11;14"},{"kind":"para","text":"One symbolized as a royal leader to rebuild God’s temple…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This is the word of the LORD unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts. Who art thou, O great mountain? before Zerubbabel thou shalt become a plain: and he shall bring forth the headstone thereof with shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto it. Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying, The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it; and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you. For who hath despised the day of small things? for they shall rejoice, and shall see the plummet in the hand of Zerubbabel with those seven; they are the eyes of the LORD, which run to and fro through the whole earth.","ref":"Zechariah 4:6-10"},{"kind":"para","text":"The other was a high priest who would lead worship in the temple…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he shewed me Joshua the high priest standing before the angel of the LORD, and Satan standing at his right hand to resist him. And the LORD said unto Satan, The LORD rebuke thee, O Satan; even the LORD that hath chosen Jerusalem rebuke thee: is not this a brand plucked out of the fire? Now Joshua was clothed with filthy garments, and stood before the angel. And he answered and spake unto those that stood before him, saying, Take away the filthy garments from him. And unto him he said, Behold, I have caused thine iniquity to pass from thee, and I will clothe thee with change of raiment. And I said, Let them set a fair mitre upon his head. So they set a fair mitre upon his head, and clothed him with garments. And the angel of the LORD stood by.","ref":"Zechariah 3:1-5"},{"kind":"para","text":"This gives us solidity in everyone who would be saved as represented by the Lamb to serve AS priests and rule as kings."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And hath made us kings and priests unto God and his Father; to him be glory and dominion for ever and ever. Amen.","ref":"Revelation 1:6"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And hast made us unto our God kings and priests: and we shall reign on the earth.","ref":"Revelation 5:10"}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The two witnesses will be hell-fire preachers like we’ve never seen before. We often think that many hell-fire preachers are very callous and judgmental (and no doubt they are), but these two witnesses will be far more lively than most preachers today. This also displays the grace and mercy of God once again. God continues to allow chance after chance for salvation and warning, yet at this point (during the end of everything as we know it), people will still reject God’s message."},{"kind":"para","text":"They will warn about a drought like Elijah did:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Elijah the Tishbite, who was of the inhabitants of Gilead, said unto Arab, As the Lord God of Israel liveth, before whom I stand, there shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to my word.","ref":"1 Kings 17:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"And they will turn water into blood like Moses:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the LORD said unto Moses, Pharaoh's heart is hardened, he refuseth to let the people go. Get thee unto Pharaoh in the morning; lo, he goeth out unto the water; and thou shalt stand by the river's brink against he come; and the rod which was turned to a serpent shalt thou take in thine hand. And thou shalt say unto him, The LORD God of the Hebrews hath sent me unto thee, saying, Let my people go, that they may serve me in the wilderness: and, behold, hitherto thou wouldest not hear. Thus saith the LORD, In this thou shalt know that I am the LORD: behold, I will smite with the rod that is in mine hand upon the waters which are in the river, and they shall be turned to blood. And the fish that is in the river shall die, and the river shall stink; and the Egyptians shall lothe to drink of the water of the river. And the LORD spake unto Moses, Say unto Aaron, Take thy rod, and stretch out thine hand upon the waters of Egypt, upon their streams, upon their rivers, and upon their ponds, and upon all their pools of water, that they may become blood; and that there may be blood throughout all the land of Egypt, both in vessels of wood, and in vessels of stone. And Moses and Aaron did so, as the LORD commanded; and he lifted up the rod, and smote the waters that were in the river, in the sight of Pharaoh, and in the sight of his servants; and all the waters that were in the river were turned to blood. And the fish that was in the river died; and the river stank, and the Egyptians could not drink of the water of the river; and there was blood throughout all the land of Egypt. And the magicians of Egypt did so with their enchantments: and Pharaoh's heart was hardened, neither did he hearken unto them; as the LORD had said. And Pharaoh turned and went into his house, neither did he set his heart to this also. And all the Egyptians digged round about the river for water to drink; for they could not drink of the water of the river. And seven days were fulfilled, after that the LORD had smitten the river.","ref":"Exodus 7:14-25"},{"kind":"para","text":"There have been many speculations as to who these two witnesses will be. I cannot affirm any of the speculations. I do believe one of them will be probably Elijah. It was promised that Elijah would return."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, I will send you Elijah the prophet before the coming of the great and dreadful day of the LORD: And he shall turn the heart of the fathers to the children, and the heart of the children to their fathers, lest I come and smite the earth with a curse.","ref":"Malachi 4:5-6"},{"kind":"para","text":"Some scholars believe that the second witness will be Enoch (who was also translated and never saw death like Elijah)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death; and was not found, because God had translated him: for before his translation he had this testimony, that he pleased God.","ref":"Hebrews 11:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve heard other scholars acclaim that it would be Moses who would appear in this last time because he was a faithful preacher, and these witnesses were doing a lot of the same things as Moses. It is also Elijah and Moses who are seen at Jesus’ transfiguration, which gives some more leverage to the idea that the second witness could be Moses. There is still not sufficient evidence to say that (though I’d probably lean more towards this idea)."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve also heard it said that the second witness could be John the Baptist (which is an interesting thought) because he paved the way for Christ, he was a faithful witness, and he never referred to himself as part of the bride, but as a friend of the bride."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that hath the bride is the bridegroom: but the friend of the bridegroom, which standeth and heareth him, rejoiceth greatly because of the bridegroom's voice: this my joy therefore is fulfilled.","ref":"John 3:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"This idea would also give more legitimacy to the fact that God ties the Old and New Testament scriptures together. Elijah being from the Old, and John the Baptist being from the New, exemplifies this connection. This is also not to mention that John the Baptist preached in many of the same ways that Elijah did, namely in the wilderness, and his message was similar, warning about the Son of Man and the lamb that will be slain."},{"kind":"para","text":"Other scholars believe that these two witnesses could just be angels created for this purpose, similar to how angels are created in Heaven solely to glorify God. They will undoubtedly have significant powers, and the Bible does not speak of angels dying, except to be cast out of Heaven for the rejection of God. Their death is eternal punishment."},{"kind":"para","text":"The choice is yours, and we won’t really know until we see them come and witness it for ourselves."}]},{"start":7,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This great city known as “Sodom and Egypt” will be a reference to what will be known as Babylon, which stands for “Rome.” This “Sodom” title is given because of the original Sodom, which was known for its sinfulness and rebellion. “Egypt” is titled here because it was also known for persecuting God’s people. We get a pretty apt description of where Christians stand at this point in time. There won’t be any room for them, obviously. It will more than likely be frowned upon to call yourself a Christian, and many will have died because of it, which is why there won’t be any found on Earth that will turn to Christianity."}]},{"start":11,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Some have the belief that the two witnesses will symbolize the church, which gives a picture of resurrection."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"So I prophesied as he commanded me, and the breath came into them, and they lived, and stood up upon their feet, an exceeding great army.","ref":"Ezekiel 37:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of man came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.","ref":"Daniel 7:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even if they are two individuals (which I believe to be the case), then we see the miraculous resurrection of God’s witnesses. This (as they are taken into Heaven) will be the last time the gospel is preached in the world again. This is a seriously scary thought because they will have had chance after chance, and yet they will continue to reject every opportunity they get."}]}]},{"start":15,"end":19,"title":"The Seventh Trumpet","entries":[{"start":15,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We’ve touched on pre-tribulation and post-tribulation rapture quite a bit already, but we understand that either way we will be saved from the wrath to come."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Much more then, being now justified by his blood, we shall be saved from wrath through him.","ref":"Romans 5:9"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And to wait for his Son from heaven, whom he raised from the dead, even Jesus, which delivered us from the wrath to come.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 1:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Some might ask, “What wrath did He save us from?” They acclaim that the wrath that is being spoken about by Paul in both of these verses refers to being saved specifically from Hell. Being sent to Hell is not God’s wrath being poured out on us, but rather God’s justice being executed. God’s wrath is poured out in the end of days, and we are saved from that. Either way, we are saved from ALL WRATH through Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"But does this give some assumption that the second return of Christ will happen at this moment during the seventh trumpet call? This is the last of the trumpets that will sound. Christ will come and judge the dead:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them. And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before God; and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works. And the sea gave up the dead which were in it; and death and hell delivered up the dead which were in them: and they were judged every man according to their works.","ref":"Revelation 20:11-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"He will reward His servants:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea. And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from God out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband. And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and God himself shall be with them, and be their God. And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away. And he that sat upon the throne said, Behold, I make all things new. And he said unto me, Write: for these words are true and faithful. And he said unto me, It is done. I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the end. I will give unto him that is athirst of the fountain of the water of life freely. He that overcometh shall inherit all things; and I will be his God, and he shall be my son.","ref":"Revelation 21:1-7"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of God and of the Lamb. In the midst of the street of it, and on either side of the river, was there the tree of life, which bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month: and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations. And there shall be no more curse: but the throne of God and of the Lamb shall be in it; and his servants shall serve him: And they shall see his face; and his name shall be in their foreheads. And there shall be no night there; and they need no candle, neither light of the sun; for the Lord God giveth them light: and they shall reign for ever and ever.","ref":"Revelation 22:1-5"},{"kind":"para","text":"And He will destroy the destroyers of the Earth:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And death and hell were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death. And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.","ref":"Revelation 20:14-15"},{"kind":"para","text":"This may sound cruel, but it’s something that we know must happen because of the sinfulness and wickedness of man. We all have an innate desire to see justice served to people who are murderers, rapists, and thieves. We want to see payback for things they have done to us or to others. This will be the same case in the last days."},{"kind":"para","text":"The world today has this so backwards, blaming those who harvest from forests, use fossil fuels, and don’t recycle as the ultimate problem of our Earth not being right. But the Bible makes it clear that we are to steward the earthly things God has given to us for His use, and that we are to use His creation to worship Him rather than the creation itself. Sadly, many worship the creation, and so because of this, THEY are the real problem with “destroying the earth.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"So does it signify the rapture? No. It signifies the triumph of God and His people."}]},{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s ark of the covenant makes a sudden appearance in this verse, which supposedly details visions that explain the church’s spiritual conflict (which will be labelled out heavily in the next chapter with even more symbolism and confirmed prophecies of the Old Testament). God makes revelations of all the Old Testament promises through this book, including the revelation of the “Tree of Life.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.","ref":"Revelation 22:14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In the midst of the street of it, and on either side of the river, was there the tree of life, which bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month: and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.","ref":"Revelation 22:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"This tree of life differs from the tree of “the Knowledge of Good and Evil.” I won’t get into the details of what this tree is for quite yet, but it has appeared before."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And out of the ground made the Lord God to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.","ref":"Genesis 2:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Though it seemed to be kind of just glanced over, there is certainly an importance to it, and the Ark of the Covenant (which God made with Moses) shares the same importance in Revelation as it did before."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19}],"verses":{"1":"And there was given me a reed like unto a rod: and the angel stood, saying, Rise, and measure the temple of God, and the altar, and them that worship therein.","2":"But the court which is without the temple leave out, and measure it not; for it is given unto the Gentiles: and the holy city shall they tread under foot forty and two months.","3":"And I will give power unto my two witnesses, and they shall prophesy a thousand two hundred and threescore days, clothed in sackcloth.","4":"These are the two olive trees, and the two candlesticks standing before the God of the earth.","5":"And if any man will hurt them, fire proceedeth out of their mouth, and devoureth their enemies: and if any man will hurt them, he must in this manner be killed.","6":"These have power to shut heaven, that it rain not in the days of their prophecy: and have power over waters to turn them to blood, and to smite the earth with all plagues, as often as they will.","7":"And when they shall have finished their testimony, the beast that ascendeth out of the bottomless pit shall make war against them, and shall overcome them, and kill them.","8":"And their dead bodies shall lie in the street of the great city, which spiritually is called Sodom and Egypt, where also our Lord was crucified.","9":"And they of the people and kindreds and tongues and nations shall see their dead bodies three days and an half, and shall not suffer their dead bodies to be put in graves.","10":"And they that dwell upon the earth shall rejoice over them, and make merry, and shall send gifts one to another; because these two prophets tormented them that dwelt on the earth.","11":"And after three days and an half the Spirit of life from God entered into them, and they stood upon their feet; and great fear fell upon them which saw them.","12":"And they heard a great voice from heaven saying unto them, Come up hither. And they ascended up to heaven in a cloud; and their enemies beheld them.","13":"And the same hour was there a great earthquake, and the tenth part of the city fell, and in the earthquake were slain of men seven thousand: and the remnant were affrighted, and gave glory to the God of heaven.","14":"The second woe is past; and, behold, the third woe cometh quickly.","15":"And the seventh angel sounded; and there were great voices in heaven, saying, The kingdoms of this world are become the kingdoms of our Lord, and of his Christ; and he shall reign for ever and ever.","16":"And the four and twenty elders, which sat before God on their seats, fell upon their faces, and worshipped God,","17":"Saying, We give thee thanks, O Lord God Almighty, which art, and wast, and art to come; because thou hast taken to thee thy great power, and hast reigned.","18":"And the nations were angry, and thy wrath is come, and the time of the dead, that they should be judged, and that thou shouldest give reward unto thy servants the prophets, and to the saints, and them that fear thy name, small and great; and shouldest destroy them which destroy the earth.","19":"And the temple of God was opened in heaven, and there was seen in his temple the ark of his testament: and there were lightnings, and voices, and thunderings, and an earthquake, and great hail."}},
    "12": {"chapter":12,"intro":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the temple of God was opened in heaven, and there was seen in his temple the ark of his testament: and there were lightnings, and voices, and thundering, and an earthquake, and great hail.","ref":"Revelation 11:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is where most scholars get the idea that the 144,000 that were mentioned before will be from the twelve tribes of Israel and why they will be mostly Jewish people saved during that time. It comes out of:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ask ye now, and see whether a man doth travail with child? Wherefore do I see every man with his hands on his loins, as a woman in travail, and all faces are turned into paleness? Alas! For that day is great, so that none is like it: it is even the time of Jacob’s trouble, but he shall be saved out of it. For it shall come to pass in that day, saith the Lord of hosts, that I will break his yoke from off thy neck, and will burst thy bonds, and strangers shall no more serve themselves of him:","ref":"Jeremiah 30:6-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is known as “Jacob’s Trouble,” and most scholars believe that Jacob’s trouble starts in this chapter of Revelation."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we read about the two witnesses who will preach to the people here on Earth and will be killed. People will rejoice because of their death because they hated everything they were preaching. It said that fires would come out of their mouths and consume those that disobeyed. Whether it will be literal fire or not, I don’t know, but it’s sufficient to say that it won’t bode well with those that are disobedient to the warnings that God is providing before He puts an end to all things. After three and a half days, the witnesses come back to life, and people will be terrified. They will be lifted into the clouds to never be seen again, and it will be the last time that God’s Word will be proclaimed. In this chapter, it will provide an opening for many signs and symbols and will showcase what the last battle will be like. What we’ve read so far has been somewhat literal (with only a few verses of symbolism here and there for reference), but in this chapter, we see many things that aren’t necessarily going to be exactly like they are pictured here, but they will be revealed to us as part of the promises God has already given throughout His Word. Most of what we read about in Revelation has been given to us as prophecy during the Old Testament. We can really draw everything that happens from past history and also line up (through God’s grace) the warnings that have been passed down from generation to generation. Whether the things depicted in this chapter are literal or not, they are certainly proven through God’s Word already and revealed beforehand through Scripture. But even while we read through this chapter, we must remember the focal point of all Scripture is on Jesus Christ and God’s salvation through Him. Even in the book of Revelation. We must remember that during this time, there will be no more chance for the world to be saved because no one will willingly be saved. We must keep our hearts tender as we read and be sure to keep the main thing the main thing, which is Christ and His salvation. It would do us well to read the last verse of the previous chapter because it leads directly into what we are reading through this chapter."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":2,"title":"The Woman (Israel)","entries":[{"start":1,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This woman is a great sign in heaven. Her clothing is the sun, moon, and twelve stars. Some religions have the belief that this woman interprets the Virgin Mary (whom did not stay a virgin, mind you (I won’t get into that in this particular study, but there’s ample evidence of this throughout scripture, plus the fact that the books of James and Jude are literally written by Jesus’ brothers… I digress)). Going back to the symbolism again, this lady is to symbolize Israel. Compare this to Joseph’s dream:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he dreamed yet another dream, and told it his brethren, and said, Behold, I have dreamed a dream more; and, behold, the sun and the moon and the eleven stars made obeisance to me.","ref":"Genesis 37:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is obviously not speaking about a literal woman, but a symbol of Israel."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulder: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace.","ref":"Isaiah 9:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s evident throughout Scripture that this lady symbolizes much more than just the future or the church. She symbolizes the promises of God through the people of God, namely Israel. Isaiah (when he spoke the words above) was not just specifically speaking about the whole world or the reader when he says, “unto us…” Though we can personally take this verse to heart (a preacher that says you can’t misunderstands the point of Scripture)."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"All scripture is given by the inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness: That the man of God may be perfect, thoroughly furnished unto all good works.","ref":"2 Timothy 3:16-17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Isaiah is speaking specifically about Israel and is literally addressing Israel about the promise of the Savior. The “US” Isaiah uses here refers specifically to the Israelites through whom Christ would be born."}]}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"title":"Satan","entries":[{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The word “wonder” in this verse comes from the Greek word “Semeion (Say-mi-on),” which means “a sign, mark, or token.” John has made it clear that the things that are being written here are not literal, but are signs given to us to mean something else. Almost like a parable of sorts. This is obviously speaking about the Devil (Verse 9 gives the clarification). These examples of Satan are shown to be his true character. It is who Satan really is. Someone said it like this:"},{"kind":"para","text":"He is called “great” because of his vast power. He is called “red” because of the fact that he was a murderer from the beginning."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.","ref":"John 8:44"},{"kind":"para","text":"He is called “dragon” because of the viciousness of his character."},{"kind":"para","text":"This verse provides a depiction of Satan that many movies have attempted to replicate today. Although they don’t quite capture his scariness, they strive to convey this image of Satan through CGI or sometimes cartoons. However, they often miss the “seven heads, horns, and crowns.” The “seven heads” symbolize perfection and wisdom, as we’ve mentioned before. This is actually the appearance of Satan’s character when he was created."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Son of man, take up a lamentation upon the king of Tyrus, and say unto him, Thus saith the Lord God; Thou sealest up the sum, full of wisdom, and perfect in beauty.","ref":"Ezekiel 28:12"},{"kind":"para","text":"The world has no idea what Satan actually looks like. He is not what you think he is. He is attractive, not ugly. How else can he be so deceiving to God’s children?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.","ref":"2 Corinthians 11:14"},{"kind":"para","text":"The “ten horns” represent the final division of the Roman Empire, which is dominated by Satan and which is his final effort to rule the world. The crowns are on the horns, not on the heads, since it is delegated power from Satan. The crowns would then have to represent kingly authority and rulership. The “third of the stars of heaven” would indicate the rebellion of the angels when satan took a third of them to their own destruction."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And it waxed great, even to the host of heaven; and it cast down some of the host and of the stars to the ground, and stamped upon them.","ref":"Daniel 8:10"}]}]},{"start":5,"end":6,"title":"The Child (Christ)","entries":[{"start":5,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The “man-child” (as if not evident enough at this point) is a picture of Christ. There should be no question about that, for He is the only one that is “caught up” to God’s throne. In case there are some that would like to argue this idea, we can break this verse down and determine it based on the Bible. It’s wise to always compare the Bible with itself. Look at how it says, “who was to rule all nations with a rod of iron:”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter’s vessel.","ref":"Psalm 2:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Even more so, we can view the “rod iron” as a shepherd’s club, used to shatter the nations like pottery. It also speaks of the “child” being “caught up unto God and His throne,” which directly relates to:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when he had spoken these things, while they beheld, he was taken up; and a cloud received him out of their sight. And while they looked stedfastly toward heaven as he went up, behold, two men stood by them in white apparel; Which also said, Ye men of Galilee, why stand ye gazing up into heaven? This same Jesus, which is taken up from you into heaven, shall so come in like manner as ye have seen him go into heaven.","ref":"Acts 1:9-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"J. Vernon McGee said, “The book of Revelation is the unveiling of the ascended Christ, the glorified Christ, the Christ who is coming in glory.” All of the book of Revelation, this far, has been centered around the power and workings of God through Jesus Christ. He was the only one that had the power to open the seals, remember?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw a strong angel proclaiming with a loud voice, Who is worthy to open the book, and to loose the seals thereof? And no man in heaven, nor in earth, neither under the earth, was able to open the book, neither to look there on. And I wept much, because no man was found worthy to open and to read the book, neither to look thereon.","ref":"Revelation 5:2-4"},{"kind":"para","text":"John even cried because they thought all hope was lost."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is set down at the right hand of the throne of God.","ref":"Hebrews 12:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s sufficient to say that scripture has given ample information about what is being talked about in these particular verses. This one thousand two hundred and sixty, spoken about in verse 6 (which equates to three and a half years), is to represent the second half of the tribulation."}]}]},{"start":7,"end":12,"title":"The Archangel","entries":[{"start":7,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Should it be any surprise that Satan and his demons are defeated? If this is a surprise to you, you have a weak faith in the God of the Bible, or perhaps no faith at all. But may it be reminded to you, Satan had already been defeated before this battle."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And having spoiled principalities and powers, he made a shew of them openly, triumphing over them in it.","ref":"Colossians 2:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s a pretty intense belief by many scholars that once Satan and his demons are cast down to Earth, there will be an insane amount of demonic influence on Earth. Whether it is the case or not, can I just submit that the purpose that Satan is so detailed in this chapter (maybe more than any other) is to put to bed any excuse that would assume there is no Satan or Hell? God has this in His Word for a reason, and that was because He knew there would be many false preachers and pastors today who would try and do away with the idea of Satan or the repercussions of sin. God has put the false preachers in their place multiple times through His Word because we cannot contend against God and win."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Shall he that contendeth with the Almighty instruct him? He that reproveth God, let him answer it.","ref":"Job 40:2"}]},{"start":10,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, when Heaven has the victory, it will be a rejoicing matter. Everyone will be excited and happy about this because Satan is put in his place. Whenever God has the victory, it’s an exciting thing for the Christian to witness. Even if the victory is small. But we notice in verse 12 that Satan (after his defeat in this battle) will take the time that he has left to destroy everything he can on Earth so that God cannot save them. Even more so, it says that he knew that he has “but a short time.” This is why Satan has been so active today. He went on a rampage when Jesus was born…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then Herod, when he saw that he was mocked of the wise men, was exceeding wroth, and sent forth, and slew all the children that were in Bethlehem, and in all the coasts thereof, from two years old and under, according to the time which he had diligently inquired of the wise men.","ref":"Matthew 2:16"},{"kind":"para","text":"And he’s been on a rampage ever since Jesus rose again. Our generation is seeing the fruit of Satan’s labor and is following after him left and right. We’ve seen an increase in wickedness simply since I’ve been alive, not a decrease. Because of this, we know that Satan has been doing everything he can to get people away from God, away from the church, and away from the truth because he already knows his time is short. He takes the return of Jesus more seriously than most Christians…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Therefore be ye also ready: for in such an hour ye think not the Son of man cometh.","ref":"Matthew 24:44"}]}]},{"start":13,"end":16,"title":"Satan and Israel in the Tribulation","entries":[{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"As we’ve already determined the woman to be, Satan is going after Israel because he hates it so much. He hates it because Christ came from this nation. “The wings of the eagle” terminology is reminiscent of God’s provision to the Israelites in Exodus."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye have seen what I did unto the Egyptians, and how I bare you on eagles’ wings, and brought you unto myself.","ref":"Exodus 19:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s proven through Exodus that they did not come out of Egypt through their own power. If that were the case, the smoke and fire of God would not have blinded the sight of the pursuers of Israel, nor given them sight during the night travels. The water would not have cleared for them to cross the sea, nor killed the enemies of God’s children that were trying to stop them from serving God. The Israelites during the time of the tribulation will be in the same ship as those of the Old Testament, except they will have cover from God if they so choose to follow His lead."}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There is a belief that this could be literal water spoken of here, or it could be a flood of Satan’s army going after the people of Israel."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now therefore, behold, the Lord bringeth up upon them the waters of the river, strong and many, even the king of Assyria, and all his glory: and he shall come up over all his channels, and go over all his banks: and he shall pass through Judah; he shall overflow and go over, and he shall reach even to the neck; and the stretching out of his wings shall fill the breadth of thy land, O Immanuel.","ref":"Isaiah 8:7-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"I like to think it might be the former, simply because God has promised never to flood the earth again to kill everything, yet here is satan trying to flood everything, only to be unsuccessful, proving that God keeps all His promises. Either way, we know that Satan will not have the victory in this matter."}]}]},{"start":17,"end":17,"title":"The Jewish Remnant","entries":[{"start":17,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“The rest of her seed” is supposedly referring to the one hundred and forty-four thousand Israelites that will be saved. This further proves the idea that Israel will be the remnant of God’s people on Earth, and the rapture will take place before the tribulation. Satan will do whatever it takes to get as many as possible away from God and away from serving Him. But we see that Satan is weak, even when he is seen as this great, scary dragon. He has no power over God or the people of God. It’s because of this that every person on Earth continues to have hope."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":17}],"verses":{"1":"And there appeared a great wonder in heaven; a woman clothed with the sun, and the moon under her feet, and upon her head a crown of twelve stars:","2":"And she being with child cried, travailing in birth, and pained to be delivered.","3":"And there appeared another wonder in heaven; and behold a great red dragon, having seven heads and ten horns, and seven crowns upon his heads.","4":"And his tail drew the third part of the stars of heaven, and did cast them to the earth: and the dragon stood before the woman which was ready to be delivered, for to devour her child as soon as it was born.","5":"And she brought forth a man child, who was to rule all nations with a rod of iron: and her child was caught up unto God, and to his throne.","6":"And the woman fled into the wilderness, where she hath a place prepared of God, that they should feed her there a thousand two hundred and threescore days.","7":"And there was war in heaven: Michael and his angels fought against the dragon; and the dragon fought and his angels,","8":"And prevailed not; neither was their place found any more in heaven.","9":"And the great dragon was cast out, that old serpent, called the Devil, and Satan, which deceiveth the whole world: he was cast out into the earth, and his angels were cast out with him.","10":"And I heard a loud voice saying in heaven, Now is come salvation, and strength, and the kingdom of our God, and the power of his Christ: for the accuser of our brethren is cast down, which accused them before our God day and night.","11":"And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony; and they loved not their lives unto the death.","12":"Therefore rejoice, ye heavens, and ye that dwell in them. Woe to the inhabiters of the earth and of the sea! for the devil is come down unto you, having great wrath, because he knoweth that he hath but a short time.","13":"And when the dragon saw that he was cast unto the earth, he persecuted the woman which brought forth the man child.","14":"And to the woman were given two wings of a great eagle, that she might fly into the wilderness, into her place, where she is nourished for a time, and times, and half a time, from the face of the serpent.","15":"And the serpent cast out of his mouth water as a flood after the woman, that he might cause her to be carried away of the flood.","16":"And the earth helped the woman, and the earth opened her mouth, and swallowed up the flood which the dragon cast out of his mouth.","17":"And the dragon was wroth with the woman, and went to make war with the remnant of her seed, which keep the commandments of God, and have the testimony of Jesus Christ."}},
    "13": {"chapter":13,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 13"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: Chapter 12 really sets up the events taking place here in chapter 13. I think a lot of people get their error in reading the book of Revelation because they pick and choose specific verses to recite from, trying to line it up with their own personal understanding, or their religions traditions, rather than lining it up with what the Bible actually says."},{"kind":"para","text":"In our last chapter we saw the symbol of the woman (which would be related to Israel), the rise of the dragon (which would be Satan), the depiction of the child (which would be Christ), the throwing down of Satan (which is the Archangel), then the trials of Satan against Israel during the time of tribulation (which is why most believe in a pre-tribulation rapture)."},{"kind":"para","text":"This book has plenty more symbolism to look at especially as it depicts this Great War that is suppose to take place in the end days. In chapter 13 we get a picture of a beast which nearly coincides with the dragon that was spoken about in the last chapter."}],"previously":["Chapter 12 really sets up the events taking place here in Chapter 13. I think a lot of people get their error in reading the Book of Revelation because they pick and choose specific verses to recite from, trying to line it up with their own personal understanding (or their religion’s traditions), rather than lining it up with what the Bible actually says. In our last chapter, we saw the symbol of the woman (which would be related to Israel), the rise of the dragon (which would be Satan), the depiction of the child (which would be Christ), the throwing down of Satan (which is the Archangel), then the trials of Satan against Israel during the time of tribulation (which is why most believe in a pre-tribulation rapture). This book has plenty more symbolism to look at, especially as it depicts this Great War that is supposed to take place in the end days. In Chapter 13, we get a picture of a beast which nearly coincides with the dragon that was spoken about in the last chapter."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":10,"title":"The First Beast","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, the “name of blasphemy” will be written on this beast’s head. It’s really not that hard to recognize Satan. I know he has disguised himself as an “angel of light,” but we don’t have to be fooled by his disguise. We should be matching everything up with the Bible to see if those things are right. When the first church came to be, there were people who were attentive to the preaching of God’s Word, but they also didn’t want to be led astray. So, they took what was being taught and looked it up themselves."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These were more noble than those in Thessalonica, in that they received the word with all readiness of mind, and searched the scriptures daily, whether those things were so.","ref":"Acts 17:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"We should be in equal amounts as prepared to study these things out ourselves. Don’t let the same mundane, everyday stresses and Satan’s schemes to make you lazy keep you from rigorously studying out God’s Word and looking into things that you don’t know for sure. We should always be willing to study, and we should always be ready to answer tough questions. And when you think you have learned it all, don’t close your mind to the possibility of being wrong or learning more."},{"kind":"para","text":"This beast will be easily identified because of the way it looks, but also because Satan has no problem blaspheming God’s beautiful name."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This beast nearly mimics the one that is shown in Daniel."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In the first year of Belshazzar king of Babylon Daniel had a dream and visions of his head upon his bed: then he wrote the dream, and told the sum of the matters. Daniel spake and said, I saw in my vision by night, and, behold, the four winds of the heaven strove upon the great sea. And four great beasts came up from the sea, diverse one from another. The first was like a lion, and had eagle's wings: I beheld till the wings thereof were plucked, and it was lifted up from the earth, and made stand upon the feet as a man, and a man's heart was given to it. And behold another beast, a second, like to a bear, and it raised up itself on one side, and it had three ribs in the mouth of it between the teeth of it: and they said thus unto it, Arise, devour much flesh. After this I beheld, and lo another, like a leopard, which had upon the back of it four wings of a fowl; the beast had also four heads; and dominion was given to it. After this I saw in the night visions, and behold a fourth beast, dreadful and terrible, and strong exceedingly; and it had great iron teeth: it devoured and brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with the feet of it: and it was diverse from all the beasts that were before it; and it had ten horns. I considered the horns, and, behold, there came up among them another little horn, before whom there were three of the first horns plucked up by the roots: and, behold, in this horn were eyes like the eyes of man, and a mouth speaking great things.","ref":"Daniel 7:1-8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I beheld, and the same horn made war with the saints, and prevailed against them;","ref":"Daniel 7:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"However, the beasts in Daniel gave a symbol of kingdoms…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These great beasts, which are four, are four kings, which shall arise out of the earth.","ref":"Daniel 7:17"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thus he said, The fourth beast shall be the fourth kingdom upon earth, which shall be diverse from all kingdoms, and shall devour the whole earth, and shall tread it down, and break it in pieces.","ref":"Daniel 7:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"The beast in Revelation (here) will symbolize human empires that demand absolute allegiance and enforce its demands. We have been seeing this happen even in our current age. We have seen this with Russia (and the invasion of Ukraine) and soon to be (probably more than likely) China. They are willing to do whatever it takes to get others to obey their commands, and they are willing to kill as many people as possible to prove their strength."},{"kind":"para","text":"This will include Egypt, Assyria, Babylon, Persia, Greece, Rome, and their successors. The 10 horns and seven heads replicate the dragon in the last chapter."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And there appeared another wonder in heaven; and behold a great red dragon, having seven heads and ten horns, and seven crowns upon his heads.","ref":"Revelation 12:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"It says in this verse that the dragon gives the beast great authority. Remember, these are symbols. I don’t know if there will be a literal giant dragon that is blatantly obvious to be Satan (I already said to assume not), but I do know that those that are saved will see who he truly is. So these verses would assume that Satan (after his rule and his attempt at taking over the entire world through nations) will then give power to the nations here on Earth that have obeyed his commands. But something will ultimately keep people impressed with Satan, which we will read in the next verse."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"One of the nations will be struck. “Wounded to death” would imply that one of the nations was utterly destroyed to the point where it seemed it could never come back. During the time that John was writing this, Rome represented the beast. Some scholars have come to believe that it was mortally wounded by Nero’s suicide (Nero was in charge during this time and an extremely vile, yet prominent figure during the time of the early church (literally responsible for burning entire cities if there was one Christian found in it)). Because of his suicide, people became chaotic. But once Rome was taken over by Vespasian and his sons, it was said to have experienced a “resurrection” of sorts. But this also brought back the persecution of the church again."},{"kind":"para","text":"Other scholars believe this will represent a remarkable recovery of the antichrist after it was badly injured. My assumption is (as I know history repeats itself all too often) that this wound will be a representation of a city during the end times that will somehow come back to life even though it seemed all was lost for it. It will join in the ranks to (just like the time of Nero) spring forth chaos on the children of Israel and the church."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Because of the seemingly powerful “resurrection” of this city, people will be so astounded that they will be tricked (once more) into believing that Satan is God, and that he is taking care of his people by bringing back to life a city that shouldn’t have even survived. This also mimics the praise of Israel during Exodus."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who is like unto thee, O Lord, among the gods? Who is like thee, glorious in holiness, fearful in praises, doing wonders?","ref":"Exodus 15:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan is literally able to mock God’s Word through this time of amazing power, and will use it to try and continually persuade people away from God. And the people will, of course, fall for it."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The beast (rather than cities in this time who are evil) will be able to be heard by everyone, and will use their voice to literally blaspheme God. They will be prideful, and they will give encouragement to those that are at battle against him, tricking them into thinking they are unstoppable. But notice the wording here (which makes me laugh)… “…power was given unto him to continue forty and two months.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"What power do they have? And where does it come from? God knows the end. He has it all figured out. God will let them play their little game for another 42 months (3.5 years) so that they think they have the victory. But as we already know, because we’ve been promised more times than not, Satan does not get the victory at the end of this book."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"These things I have spoken unto you, that in me ye might have peace. In the world ye shall have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world.","ref":"John 16:33"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Through God we shall do valiantly: for he it is that shall tread down our enemies.","ref":"Psalm 108:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But thanks be to God, which giveth us the victory through our Lord Jesus Christ.","ref":"1 Corinthians 15:57"},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan can believe he has all the power he wants, but in the end he will never hold a candle to our God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who is like unto the Lord our God, who dwelleth on high,","ref":"Psalm 113:5"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Satan can blaspheme against me all he wants. I know to whom I belong, and as we’ve already established, we know who has the victory."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For ye are bought with a price: therefore glorify God in your body, and in your spirit, which are God’s.","ref":"1 Corinthians 6:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"Some people are afraid to speak about Satan because they are afraid that Satan will start to attack if they do. Satan may attack, he may be upset, he may call you out for your sins, he may try and wound this mortal body, he may have some sort of ultimate agenda, but in the end he can do nothing without God giving him permission. We can square up and confidently say, “I am in the Lord, and if you want me, you’ll have to go through Him.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The Lord is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, and my high tower.","ref":"Psalm 18:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can be confident and just as powerful through Christ as Jesus was."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I can do all things through Christ which strengtheneth me.","ref":"Philippians 4:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"We can say as well…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Jesus answered and said unto him, Get thee behind me, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve.","ref":"Luke 4:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But he turned, and said unto Peter, Get thee behind me, Satan: thou art an offense unto me: for thou savourest not the things that be of God, but those that be of men.","ref":"Matthew 16:23"},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan has no control over you, and you have every right to mock him and turn him away. He can do nothing when you have the Lord in your life. Those that may fear Satan are those that don’t have Christ. Even if it were so (that Satan could hurt your flesh), he cannot touch your Spirit because it belongs to someone much more powerful."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And fear not them which kill the body, but are not able to kill the soul: but rather fear him which is able to destroy both soul and body in hell.","ref":"Matthew 10:28"}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This insinuates that there will be some (probably not specifically of the 144,000 that was spoken of previously, which we’ve already talked about) that will be saved during the end times. We’ve already established that the church will be resurrected, and there will be a remnant of people who still have opportunities to be saved. Some will be saved, but it seems during this 42-week period, Satan is going to make a public example out of them and kill them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, this proves that Satan can do nothing to the soul, and we know that really upsets him. This should be a sobering thought to those who are saved and unsaved alike. Today could be the last day for any of us. This could be my last day of going through Revelation, and God may call me home. Whether by revelation through translation (or rather through rapture) or by my death day, which no man knows save for God, this could be a finality to this series and this message, and I may not be able to finish writing these notes."},{"kind":"para","text":"We live in a free country (for now) in America, but there may be a day coming when being a Christian will be looked down upon (like in so many countries already, and it has been increasingly prevalent in our country today), and we may be made an example through martyrdom. May we learn how to stand strong, knowing that our fates are sealed in the Lord, and that He will repay for the crimes and murders that this world has committed and will continue to commit. The authority that Satan has now is nothing compared to the type of authority that will be given to him in the end times. He will act like he’s providing peace because of the people he’s killing, but ultimately, those who know God and know the anti-Christ will know his ultimate ploy is to destroy God and His people."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I know we’ve talked about this before, but this gives further validity to what was previously mentioned. The end will come when no one else will be saved."},{"kind":"para","text":"“And all that dwell upon the earth shall worship him…”"},{"kind":"para","text":"When the Bible says “all,” I truly believe it means “all.” There won’t be a single soul left on this earth who will not have fallen head over heels for Satan and his desires to destroy and kill, and reject everything God has given to us. These will be people who are not saved, nor were ever going to be saved. This is why I honestly and truly believe that the “Lamb’s book of life” was written when the world was formed."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has every single person’s name written down in this book whom He already knew would be saved. This belief is also backed up biblically. Aside from the fact that it’s literally written in this verse…"},{"kind":"para","text":"“…whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"We have some proofs throughout other parts of the Bible as well!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:","ref":"Matthew 25:34"},{"kind":"para","text":"Or if we looked to Ephesians:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"According as he hath chosen us in him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blame before him in love: Having predestinated us unto the adoption of children by Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his will, To the praise of the glory of his grace, wherein he hath made us accepted in the beloved. In whom we have redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of sins, according to the riches of his grace; Wherein he hath abounded toward us in all wisdom and prudence; Having made known unto us the mystery of his will, according to his good pleasure which he hath purposed in himself: That in the dispensation of the fulness of times he might gather together in one all things in Christ, both which are in heaven, and which are on earth; even in him: In whom also we have obtained an inheritance, being predestinated according to the purpose of him who worketh all things after the counsel of his own will: That we should be to the praise of his glory, who first trusted in Christ. In whom ye also trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation: in whom also after that ye believed, ye were sealed with that holy Spirit of promise, Which is the earnest of our inheritance until the redemption of the purchased possession, unto the praise of his glory.","ref":"Ephesians 1:4-14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The beast that thou sawest was, and is not; and shall ascend out of the bottomless pit, and go into perdition: and they that dwell on the earth shall wonder, whose names were not written in the book of life from the foundation of the world, when they behold the beast that was, and is not, and yet is.","ref":"Revelation 17:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"This “book of life” appears several times through scripture."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Yet now, if thou wilt forgive their sin—; and if not, blot me, I pray thee, out of thy book which thou hast written. And the Lord said unto Moses, Whosoever hath sinned against me, him will I blot out of my book.","ref":"Exodus 32:32-33"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.","ref":"Daniel 12:1"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Notwithstanding in this rejoice not, that the spirits are subject unto you; but rather rejoice, because your names are written in heaven.","ref":"Luke 10:20"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.","ref":"Revelation 3:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.","ref":"Revelation 20:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"I do not stand with the hyper-Calvinistic mindset that God specifically chose a select amount of people to be saved. If this were the case, preaching, teaching, and reaching would all be vain. God will save whom He will, so therefore what would be the point of Jesus commissioning us? Why would our Bibles say that God is not willing that any should perish, yet He has seemingly rejected them? Why would our Bibles tell us that “whosoever” calls out to God will be saved? Why does Jesus, Himself, say that He died for the whole world and “ANYBODY” that would believe in Him won’t perish but will have everlasting life?"},{"kind":"para","text":"No. It will only be those that have made their choice, and God has always known who will do that, because He is all-knowing. Even furthermore, to help really capitulate what is being written, John further details these events in the next two verses."}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a wake-up call to those that are not fully studied to endure those things which are to come. Revelation has been a book of endurance and perseverance. It’s a book about overcoming. We need to really mentally, physically, and spiritually prepare ourselves for the things that are going to come. Those that will be left behind on Earth for the things that will take place will have to really prepare themselves for the worst of the worst, and they could never be prepared for it."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":18,"title":"The Second Beast","entries":[{"start":11,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, Satan will try and disguise himself like a lamb, but once again (because Satan can’t help himself), his words will imitate his real being. He is no different than the dragon."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the serpent cast out of his mouth water as a flood after the woman, that he might cause her to be carried away of the flood.","ref":"Revelation 12:15"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw three unclean spirits like frogs come out of the mouth of the dragon, and out of the mouth of the beast, and out of the mouth of the false prophet. For they are the spirits of devils, working miracles, which go forth unto the kings of the earth and of the whole world, to gather them to the battle of the great day of God Almighty.","ref":"Revelation 16:13-14"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the beast was taken, and with him the false prophet that wrought miracles before him, with which he deceived them that had received the mark of the beast, and them that worshipped his image. These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone.","ref":"Revelation 19:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because he will come looking innocent, he will turn everybody’s attention back to the beast and how seemingly innocent it is."},{"kind":"para","text":"I’ve never been one for politics in my life until the last few years with COVID and the issues plaguing our government about what to do next. I now understand the necessity to be politically ready for those things to come and what to look out for. Our current leadership has given a great picture of those things that will eventually take place. I love the office of the president, and I pray for him every day, but man does he trip over himself a lot, and everyone that is around him constantly tries to make him look good. But to those that know and understand abortion is not okay, and child-grooming is unacceptable, and murder, lies, and blasphemy (and I can really go down a list here that our president has openly been for), we can see through the lies and deceit. Those that can’t, prove how gullible people are, and further prove the Bible right. (Usually, those that can’t see through the lies are those that don’t believe in the God of the Bible anyway, once again further proving the authenticity of God’s Word.) I’m not saying this to be mean or rude against one side or the other because there is extremism on both sides. I’m saying this to open your hearts and minds to the truth that is being written here in this book of Revelation."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Satan, of course, tries to mimic an Old Testament miracle."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then the fire of the Lord fell, and consumed the burnt sacrifice, and the wood, and the stones, and the dust, and licked up the water that was in the trench.","ref":"1 Kings 18:38"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And Elijah answered and said to the captain of fifty, If I be a man of God, then let fire come down from heaven, and consume thee and thy fifty. And there came down fire from heaven, and consumed him and his fifty.","ref":"2 Kings 1:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s nothing original with Satan. It’s just too easy. (Pardon my French, but…) You’d have to be a complete idiot to fall for his traps… Yet there they are… And we are often seen just as moronic as they are. Yet, they won’t have repentance, whereas we are given chance after chance by the Lord."}]},{"start":14,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Not only has God written (as the 2nd commandment) that we should not worship statues made to look like God, He also warns against this over and over again through His Word."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"They have mouths, but they speak not: eyes have they, but they see not:","ref":"Psalm 115:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Catholic Church today is filled with idols, whether they be of Jesus Christ (which still goes against the 2nd commandment) or saints, or Mary, or angels, or anything that was warned about being a sin in the moral law. Here, we see Satan literally tell them to make a false image to the beast (their false god) and the people (knowing that it’s wrong but snuffing out their conscience, maybe even being trained to accept this by religion today) obliges! Then, to further prove how powerful and great he is, Satan brings it to life. If you didn’t worship it, you would be put to death."}]},{"start":16,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"And thou shalt bind them for a sign upon thine hand, and they shall be as frontlets between thine eyes.","ref":"Deuteronomy 6:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"In case you weren’t sure why Satan would require this to be the case, what he is doing is mocking God’s law. In Deuteronomy, God’s law was written upon their hands and on their foreheads to prove God’s authority over their thoughts and actions, displaying how dedicated they were to God. Satan is doing this to mock (once again) something that happened in the Old Testament with God’s children."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the Lord said unto him, Go through the midst of the city, through the midst of Jerusalem, and set a mark upon the foreheads of the men that sigh and that cry for all the abominations that be done in the midst thereof.","ref":"Ezekiel 9:4"},{"kind":"para","text":"These marks do not have to be physical features. They might be physical, we are not sure (though a lot of what we have been reading lately is symbolic). Either way, the markings of 666, and the markings of the law both symbolize spiritual control."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I honestly believe that this number was chosen because it contrasts divine completeness. We’ve mentioned this before, but God has used “seven” to showcase those things that are “complete,” and seeing as Satan just enjoys being the opposite of God and wrecking havoc, 666 is just short of God’s completeness. Really, the joke is on him, because (just like the number he has chosen) he always comes short of God’s glory."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18}],"verses":{"1":"And I stood upon the sand of the sea, and saw a beast rise up out of the sea, having seven heads and ten horns, and upon his horns ten crowns, and upon his heads the name of blasphemy.","2":"And the beast which I saw was like unto a leopard, and his feet were as the feet of a bear, and his mouth as the mouth of a lion: and the dragon gave him his power, and his seat, and great authority.","3":"And I saw one of his heads as it were wounded to death; and his deadly wound was healed: and all the world wondered after the beast.","4":"And they worshipped the dragon which gave power unto the beast: and they worshipped the beast, saying, Who is like unto the beast? who is able to make war with him?","5":"And there was given unto him a mouth speaking great things and blasphemies; and power was given unto him to continue forty and two months.","6":"And he opened his mouth in blasphemy against God, to blaspheme his name, and his tabernacle, and them that dwell in heaven.","7":"And it was given unto him to make war with the saints, and to overcome them: and power was given him over all kindreds, and tongues, and nations.","8":"And all that dwell upon the earth shall worship him, whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world.","9":"If any man have an ear, let him hear.","10":"He that leadeth into captivity shall go into captivity: he that killeth with the sword must be killed with the sword. Here is the patience and the faith of the saints.","11":"And I beheld another beast coming up out of the earth; and he had two horns like a lamb, and he spake as a dragon.","12":"And he exerciseth all the power of the first beast before him, and causeth the earth and them which dwell therein to worship the first beast, whose deadly wound was healed.","13":"And he doeth great wonders, so that he maketh fire come down from heaven on the earth in the sight of men,","14":"And deceiveth them that dwell on the earth by the means of those miracles which he had power to do in the sight of the beast; saying to them that dwell on the earth, that they should make an image to the beast, which had the wound by a sword, and did live.","15":"And he had power to give life unto the image of the beast, that the image of the beast should both speak, and cause that as many as would not worship the image of the beast should be killed.","16":"And he causeth all, both small and great, rich and poor, free and bond, to receive a mark in their right hand, or in their foreheads:","17":"And that no man might buy or sell, save he that had the mark, or the name of the beast, or the number of his name.","18":"Here is wisdom. Let him that hath understanding count the number of the beast: for it is the number of a man; and his number is Six hundred threescore and six."}},
    "14": {"chapter":14,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 14"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: The last chapter looked at the rise of the two beasts. The first beast (symbolizing kingdoms) were going to rule and reign with the anti-Christ, whereas the second beast (Satan) gave people the proclamation to worship the first beast (which a head of is ultimately destroyed and then miraculously restored). We were also introduced to the sign of markings of the beast, and the number of 666, defying God’s completeness of 7."},{"kind":"para","text":"This chapter continues from the previous two chapters and the utter destruction of Satan, along with the brutal killing and destroying of Christians in the land, we will have had a reminder of hope showcased through this chapter of Revelation. Every chapter of the Bible is filled with hope from God."}],"previously":["The last chapter looked at the rise of the two beasts. The first beast (symbolizing kingdoms) was going to rule and reign with the anti-Christ, whereas the second beast (Satan) gave people the proclamation to worship the first beast (which a head of is ultimately destroyed and then miraculously restored). We were also introduced to the sign of the markings of the beast, and the number of 666, defying God’s completeness of 7. This chapter continues from the previous two chapters and the utter destruction of Satan, along with the brutal killing and destroying of Christians in the land. We will have had a reminder of hope showcased through this chapter of Revelation. Every chapter of the Bible is filled with hope from God."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"The Lamb and the 144,000","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus and His 144,000, previously mentioned in chapter 7, will be standing before the world with the seal of God upon their foreheads. While the rest of the world will have Satan’s number marking their life and legacy, the remaining Christians will have the mark of God to reveal their legacy! The name pictures who you belong to."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are standing on top of “Mount Zion,” which is a direct reference from David in the book of Psalms."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion.","ref":"Psalm 2:6"}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This new song will be specifically given to God’s triumph, and those that followed through in the Lamb’s Redemption."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"O give thanks unto the Lord, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever. Let the redeemed of the Lord say so, whom he hath redeemed from the hand of the enemy; And gathered them out of the lands, from the east, and from the west, from the north, and from the south.","ref":"Psalm 107:1-3"},{"kind":"para","text":"God’s biggest seal of worship is always through song, and when there is victory, there is plenty of reason to sing."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"O sing unto the Lord a new song; for he hath done marvellous things: his right hand, and his holy arm, hath gotten him the victory.","ref":"Psalm 98:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"Though Satan may have been having a field day with destroying and torturing Christians, the people of God were already living in victory. They already knew who was going to win. This also further indicates (as we’ve said before) that the one hundred and forty-four thousand that are redeemed would not insinuate a literal number, but rather an implication of a large quantity who are redeemed."}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Whether they are literal virgins or not is not implied. My assumption is that they were, for their lives were focused mainly on war, and this also implicates that they were all members of both genders. Even in the Old Testament, whenever God commanded a war, the people remained virgins."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"When the host goeth forth against thine enemies, then keep thee from every wicked thing. If there be among you any man, that is not clean by reason of uncleanness that chanceth him by night, then shall he go abroad out of the camp, he shall not come within the camp: But it shall be, when evening cometh on, he shall wash himself with water: and when the sun is down, he shall come into the camp again.","ref":"Deuteronomy 23:9-11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And David answered the priest, and said unto him, Of a truth women have been kept from us about these three days, since I came out, and the vessels of the young men are holy, and the bread is in a manner common, yea, though it were sanctified this day in the vessel.","ref":"1 Samuel 21:5"}]}]},{"start":6,"end":13,"title":"The Messages of the Three Angels","entries":[{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Another chance for salvation, yet it will be rejected by the world. God’s mercy never ends, even when His judgement comes to pass."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Babylon was extremely powerful in its day. Though during the time that John wrote Revelation, Rome was the biggest power, Babylon represents a higher power during that day which will have fallen, copying Isaiah’s announcement."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And, behold, here cometh a chariot of men, with a couple of horsemen. And he answered and said, Babylon is fallen, is fallen; and all the graven images of her gods he hath broken unto the ground.","ref":"Isaiah 21:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Babylon the prostitute represents the temptations of material wealth and pleasure. These things entice the people into serving something other than God. If that doesn’t sound like our culture today, I don’t know what does…"}]},{"start":9,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Just like Heaven is eternal and never-ending, so is Hell. God made both and had a specific purpose for both. Because of our sin, we have a home in Hell, but God has given us freedom from it and has allowed us access to make our home in Heaven. These people (in the last days who worship the beast) will have a torturous eternity. They will constantly be tormented forever without stopping."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"John, yet again, reminds the Christians to continue to endure. Continue to hang on and stand strong. Continue to love God and serve Him with everything you have. Never give up. Even if the world is ending."}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s Spirit reminds us how blessed we are to have died in Christ. There is true spiritual rest for those who have given their lives over to Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest. Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls. For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.","ref":"Matthew 11:28-30"}]}]},{"start":14,"end":20,"title":"The Harvest of the Earth","entries":[{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is obviously representing Jesus. The sickle is the tool that is used in farming for harvesting crops. Jesus is the Lord of the harvest."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Pray ye therefore the Lord of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest.","ref":"Matthew 9:38"},{"kind":"para","text":"Because Jesus sowed the gospel to the world, He will return to gather what He sowed."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He answered and said unto them, He that soweth the good seed is the Son of man;","ref":"Matthew 13:37"},{"kind":"para","text":"This verse is also represented in the book of Daniel:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of man came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him. And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.","ref":"Daniel 7:13-14"}]},{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It’s assumed that the harvest of the earth is Christ gathering believers."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Let both grow together until the harvest: and in the time of harvest I will say to the reapers, Gather ye together first the tares, and bind them in bundles to burn them: but gather the wheat into my barn.","ref":"Matthew 13:30"},{"kind":"para","text":"Notice that Christ does not send an angel to reap His harvest. Only Christ reaps His own harvest. It was His labor that supplied for the harvest to begin with, and it will be His labor that gathers in His fruit."},{"kind":"para","text":"Before you ask, I do see (as many have pointed out) the fact that Jesus says to collect the “tares” first. Some have said, “This proves a post-tribulation rapture.” Again, they misuse this verse. This speaks about the final gathering at the end. Jesus will remove the tares and throw them into hell, and then will gather the wheat and store them in Heaven. This will be the second judgment. But even still, when we view this verse, we notice that it speaks about sending “reapers” to gather. Jesus is not doing that here, which makes the obvious assumption that Jesus was not talking specifically about this time mentioned here. Either way, we come to the conclusion that this event is separate from the event of the rapture, which means the rapture has already taken place before this occasion."}]},{"start":17,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, this is a gruesome picture of the enemies of God being crushed under God’s judgement like grapes are crushed for wine. This was a promise that was made by Isaiah."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who is this that cometh from Edom, with dyed garments from Bozrah? this that is glorious in his apparel, travelling in the greatness of his strength? I that speak in righteousness, mighty to save. Wherefore art thou red in thine apparel, and thy garments like him that treadeth in the winefat? I have trodden the winepress alone; and of the people there was none with me: for I will tread them in mine anger, and trample them in my fury; and their blood shall be sprinkled upon my garments, and I will stain all my raiment. For the day of vengeance is in mine heart, and the year of my redeemed is come. And I looked, and there was none to help; and I wondered that there was none to uphold: therefore mine own arm brought salvation unto me; and my fury, it upheld me. And I will tread down the people in mine anger, and make them drunk in my fury, and I will bring down their strength to the earth.","ref":"Isaiah 63:1-6"},{"kind":"para","text":"One thousand six hundred furlongs is equivalent to two hundred miles. That’s a lot of blood. God has given warning after warning about every possible thing that will happen in the end. He is still warning today through His Word. This should give us patience to serve and love people into knowing Christ as verse 12 says…"},{"kind":"para","text":"“Here is the patience of the saints: here are they that keep the commandments of God, and the faith of Jesus.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"May we use this chapter as preparation to get into the harvest before the Lord of it returns to collect the last of His harvest. Spurgeon said, “Those who are to be crowned in heaven must bear the cross on earth. No cross, no reward…Those who are to sing Christ’s praise in heaven must first be willing to bear Christ’s shame below.”"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":20}],"verses":{"1":"And I looked, and, lo, a Lamb stood on the mount Sion, and with him an hundred forty and four thousand, having his Father's name written in their foreheads.","2":"And I heard a voice from heaven, as the voice of many waters, and as the voice of a great thunder: and I heard the voice of harpers harping with their harps:","3":"And they sung as it were a new song before the throne, and before the four beasts, and the elders: and no man could learn that song but the hundred and forty and four thousand, which were redeemed from the earth.","4":"These are they which were not defiled with women; for they are virgins. These are they which follow the Lamb whithersoever he goeth. These were redeemed from among men, being the firstfruits unto God and to the Lamb.","5":"And in their mouth was found no guile: for they are without fault before the throne of God.","6":"And I saw another angel fly in the midst of heaven, having the everlasting gospel to preach unto them that dwell on the earth, and to every nation, and kindred, and tongue, and people,","7":"Saying with a loud voice, Fear God, and give glory to him; for the hour of his judgment is come: and worship him that made heaven, and earth, and the sea, and the fountains of waters.","8":"And there followed another angel, saying, Babylon is fallen, is fallen, that great city, because she made all nations drink of the wine of the wrath of her fornication.","9":"And the third angel followed them, saying with a loud voice, If any man worship the beast and his image, and receive his mark in his forehead, or in his hand,","10":"The same shall drink of the wine of the wrath of God, which is poured out without mixture into the cup of his indignation; and he shall be tormented with fire and brimstone in the presence of the holy angels, and in the presence of the Lamb:","11":"And the smoke of their torment ascendeth up for ever and ever: and they have no rest day nor night, who worship the beast and his image, and whosoever receiveth the mark of his name.","12":"Here is the patience of the saints: here are they that keep the commandments of God, and the faith of Jesus.","13":"And I heard a voice from heaven saying unto me, Write, Blessed are the dead which die in the Lord from henceforth: Yea, saith the Spirit, that they may rest from their labours; and their works do follow them.","14":"And I looked, and behold a white cloud, and upon the cloud one sat like unto the Son of man, having on his head a golden crown, and in his hand a sharp sickle.","15":"And another angel came out of the temple, crying with a loud voice to him that sat on the cloud, Thrust in thy sickle, and reap: for the time is come for thee to reap; for the harvest of the earth is ripe.","16":"And he that sat on the cloud thrust in his sickle on the earth; and the earth was reaped.","17":"And another angel came out of the temple which is in heaven, he also having a sharp sickle.","18":"And another angel came out from the altar, which had power over fire; and cried with a loud cry to him that had the sharp sickle, saying, Thrust in thy sharp sickle, and gather the clusters of the vine of the earth; for her grapes are fully ripe.","19":"And the angel thrust in his sickle into the earth, and gathered the vine of the earth, and cast it into the great winepress of the wrath of God.","20":"And the winepress was trodden without the city, and blood came out of the winepress, even unto the horse bridles, by the space of a thousand and six hundred furlongs."}},
    "15": {"chapter":15,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 15"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: In our last chapter, we got a picture of the gruesomeness of God’s wrath, referring to those that take the mark of the beast as grapes in a wine press, that once completely squished would bleed to the amount of 1,600 furlongs up to the bridle of a horse, which is 200 miles. Obviously, the last chapter didn’t leave much hope for the evil in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"This chapter picks up with the same attitude, but in a more victorious note. We know that God has the victory, and we understand that Christ’s completed work on the cross gives us affirmation and hope during this particular time that is pictured in this book of the Bible. We have assurance and faith in Christ that allows us to see victory in some of the harshest trials the earth can face because we know the victor and we have joined His side. This chapter is a chapter of victory, and should be looked at as the same for those that are saved and know Christ."}],"previously":["In our last chapter, we got a picture of the gruesomeness of God’s wrath, referring to those that take the mark of the beast as grapes in a wine press, that once completely squished would bleed to the amount of 1,600 furlongs up to the bridle of a horse (which is 200 miles). Obviously, the last chapter didn’t leave much hope for the evil in this world. This chapter picks up with the same attitude, but in a more victorious note. We know that God has the victory, and we understand that Christ’s completed work on the cross gives us affirmation and hope during this particular time that is pictured in this book of the Bible. We have assurance and faith in Christ that allows us to see victory in some of the harshest trials the earth can face because we know the victor and we have joined His side. This chapter is a chapter of victory, and should be looked at as the same for those that are saved and know Christ."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":8,"title":"The Seven Angels with Seven Plagues","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"A key note to remember is when John says the word “sign” or “wonder,” it means this symbolizes something else. These are the seven “last” plagues of God which will be “poured out” on the Earth. They are represented as vials or bowls to give a depiction of how they will be poured out. It will be emptied without measure (other than the bowls being of that measurement). These bowls will be represented in the next chapter and will give a conclusion to the great tribulation period, which will lead into the final battle of Armageddon (which I won’t spoil quite yet because that will come in the next chapter shortly). These angels, represented in this verse, are the representation of God’s completion in the destruction of His enemies."}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We’ve talked about this before in previous chapters of this study, but the “Song of the Lamb” will be music that was created by God’s redeemed people for this specific occasion. These were the ones who conquered the beast by holding fast to their faith even when threatened with death."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they overcame him by the blood of the Lamb, and by the word of their testimony; and they loved not their lives unto the death.","ref":"Revelation 12:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"The Bible tells us repeatedly to stand fast in the faith, and to have our faith always at the ready to defeat Satan and his ploys to drag you away from God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For now we live, if ye stand fast in the Lord.","ref":"1 Thessalonians 3:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Watch ye, stand fast in the faith, quit you like men, be strong.","ref":"1 Corinthians 16:13"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith Christ hath made us free, and be not entangled again to the yoke of bondage.","ref":"Galatians 5:1"},{"kind":"para","text":"When we stand fast, and we aren’t willing to waver in our faith and position in Christ, we will be rewarded and blessed while those who don’t will have a much worse reward…"}]},{"start":3,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"QUESTION: What are you looking forward to most in eternity?"},{"kind":"para","text":"The song of Moses celebrated Israel’s exodus from Egypt."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then sang Moses and the children of Israel this song unto the LORD, and spake, saying, I will sing unto the LORD, for he hath triumphed gloriously: the horse and his rider hath he thrown into the sea. The LORD is my strength and song, and he is become my salvation: he is my God, and I will prepare him an habitation; my father's God, and I will exalt him. The LORD is a man of war: the LORD is his name. Pharaoh's chariots and his host hath he cast into the sea: his chosen captains also are drowned in the Red sea. The depths have covered them: they sank into the bottom as a stone. Thy right hand, O LORD, is become glorious in power: thy right hand, O LORD, hath dashed in pieces the enemy. And in the greatness of thine excellency thou hast overthrown them that rose up against thee: thou sentest forth thy wrath, which consumed them as stubble. And with the blast of thy nostrils the waters were gathered together, the floods stood upright as an heap, and the depths were congealed in the heart of the sea. The enemy said, I will pursue, I will overtake, I will divide the spoil; my lust shall be satisfied upon them; I will draw my sword, my hand shall destroy them. Thou didst blow with thy wind, the sea covered them: they sank as lead in the mighty waters. Who is like unto thee, O LORD, among the gods? Who is like thee, glorious in holiness, fearful in praises, doing wonders? Thou stretchedst out thy right hand, the earth swallowed them. Thou in thy mercy hast led forth the people which thou hast redeemed: thou hast guided them in thy strength unto thy holy habitation. The people shall hear, and be afraid: sorrow shall take hold on the inhabitants of Palestina. Then the dukes of Edom shall be amazed; the mighty men of Moab, trembling shall take hold upon them; all the inhabitants of Canaan shall melt away. Fear and dread shall fall upon them; by the greatness of thine arm they shall be as still as a stone; till thy people pass over, O LORD, till the people pass over, which thou hast purchased. Thou shalt bring them in, and plant them in the mountain of thine inheritance, in the place, O LORD, which thou hast made for thee to dwell in, in the Sanctuary, O Lord, which thy hands have established. The LORD shall reign for ever and ever.","ref":"Exodus 15:1-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"This song (here in Revelation) will be for the end of the judgement of God, and will display our awe and rejoicing in the final victory, knowing that God will have abolished all evil and sin for the rest of eternity. It will be a weight that is lifted from our shoulders."},{"kind":"para","text":"The truth is, whether we like to admit it or not, sin is weighty. When we live a life of sin, we think it’s fun and uplifting. We are tricked into believing it makes things easier and better for us. In reality, sin causes an extreme weight to burden us, and makes us weak and wilting. I look forward to the day when sin will cease to exist."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The book of Hebrews gives a really good look at the Old Testament tabernacle comparative to Jesus Christ. Everything in the Old Testament tabernacle was a picture and representation of Christ and His salvation, including the tent itself!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now of the things which we have spoken this is the sum: We have such an high priest, who is set on the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in the heavens; A minister of the sanctuary, and of the true tabernacle, which the Lord pitched, and not man.","ref":"Hebrews 8:1-2"},{"kind":"para","text":"While the children of Israel had a great covenant promise from God through their sacrifices, WE (those that live today through God’s salvation) have a BETTER covenant promise through Jesus Christ. This “true tent” that is spoken of in this verse pictures Heaven. No man has built Heaven. The holiest of holies (which is often referenced in the Old Testament about where the Ark of the Covenant would be kept for the sin sacrifices of the people and where the presence of God would dwell) was built by man, and it was to represent a Heavenly throne and picture of an eternal Ark made through Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But now hath he obtained a more excellent ministry, by how much also he is the mediator of a better covenant, which was established upon better promises.","ref":"Hebrews 8:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus already gave a vision to John once before in a previous chapter of this promised covenant ark…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the temple of God was opened in heaven, and there was seen in his temple the ark of his testament: and there were lightnings, and voices, and thundering, and an earthquake, and great hail.","ref":"Revelation 11:19"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The linen represents the purity of God’s church or His “bride,” rather. White has always symbolized purity to God. He has made that clear even in His Word."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Come now, and let us reason together, saith the Lord: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.","ref":"Isaiah 1:18"}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"He’s given God’s wrath to pour out on all those that have rejected Him and have desired to die a most painful death. They wanted the world more than Christ. They wanted life more than eternity. They wanted temporary pleasures rather than heavenly gain. They will get what they want, but it won’t be worth it. Nothing in this Earth is ever worth holding onto."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Imagine that. His power (at this point) and glory will be so intense that no one will be able to enter His presence. Not even those who are already dead and in eternity. Even if we look at the Old Testament, and all the times God reveals Himself, no one can see who He is or they would die!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"No man hath seen God at any time, the only begotten Son, which is in the bosom of the Father, he hath declared him.","ref":"John 1:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"No man hath seen God at any time. If we love one another, God dwelleth in us, and his love is perfected in us.","ref":"1 John 4:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live.","ref":"Exodus 33:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are supposed to be without sin when we enter eternity, yet God’s glory will be so powerful that not even those without sin in Heaven will be able to see Him at this moment. I imagine that they may be vaporized to never exist again if they did. Though I don’t think God will even allow anyone to come into His presence until this is all finished."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8}],"verses":{"1":"And I saw another sign in heaven, great and marvellous, seven angels having the seven last plagues; for in them is filled up the wrath of God.","2":"And I saw as it were a sea of glass mingled with fire: and them that had gotten the victory over the beast, and over his image, and over his mark, and over the number of his name, stand on the sea of glass, having the harps of God.","3":"And they sing the song of Moses the servant of God, and the song of the Lamb, saying, Great and marvellous are thy works, Lord God Almighty; just and true are thy ways, thou King of saints.","4":"Who shall not fear thee, O Lord, and glorify thy name? for thou only art holy: for all nations shall come and worship before thee; for thy judgments are made manifest.","5":"And after that I looked, and, behold, the temple of the tabernacle of the testimony in heaven was opened:","6":"And the seven angels came out of the temple, having the seven plagues, clothed in pure and white linen, and having their breasts girded with golden girdles.","7":"And one of the four beasts gave unto the seven angels seven golden vials full of the wrath of God, who liveth for ever and ever.","8":"And the temple was filled with smoke from the glory of God, and from his power; and no man was able to enter into the temple, till the seven plagues of the seven angels were fulfilled."}},
    "16": {"chapter":16,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 16"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: We were introduced to the opening and build up of God’s wrath being poured out, through the scene of seven angels holding each stage of his wrath. In this chapter, we will see what each vial (or bowl depending on the translation) emphasizes, and how that will hold for all those that appear on Earth."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are led into a horrifying, yet, justifying climactic conclusion to God’s wrath being poured out. These next few chapters will see the defeat of the evil people of Earth, and we will get a look at their ultimate legacy and what that will lead them to. They have had chance after chance for salvation, but they chose to go against it over and over again. Actually, it seemed the more that God provided salvation, and prodded them to turn to Him, the more rebellious they became."},{"kind":"para","text":"Many wonder how they could do that knowing that all these things were taking place, but our world does this even right now. God can put the whole world to a stop through some global pandemic, and make it impossible to thrive and survive on bad leadership (leadership that doesn’t look towards God’s Will and way) and yet people are still capable of claiming that God doesn’t exist, and/or are hateful towards God and His people."}],"previously":["We were introduced to the opening and build-up of God’s wrath being poured out, through the scene of seven angels holding each stage of his wrath. In this chapter, we will see what each vial (or bowl depending on the translation) emphasizes, and how that will hold for all those that appear on Earth. We are led into a horrifying, yet justifying, climactic conclusion to God’s wrath being poured out. These next few chapters will see the defeat of the evil people of Earth, and we will get a look at their ultimate legacy and what that will lead them to. They have had chance after chance for salvation, but they chose to go against it over and over again. Actually, it seemed the more that God provided salvation and prodded them to turn to Him, the more rebellious they became. Many wonder how they could do that knowing that all these things were taking place, but our world does this even right now. God can put the whole world to a stop through some global pandemic and make it impossible to thrive and survive on bad leadership (leadership that doesn’t look towards God’s Will and way), and yet people are still capable of claiming that God doesn’t exist and/or are hateful towards God and His people."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":1,"title":"The Vials of God’s Wrath","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"John hears an audible voice that announces the end of this great battle and life as everyone knows it. God is hereafter finished with His open invitation of salvation, and will have shut the door to it forever. Those that have not been saved will not be saved even if the door was still open for them. But because God is announcing the pouring out of His wrath here, it proves that the door has been shut, just as it was in the days of Noah."}]}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"title":"The First Vial","entries":[{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Our best bet when navigating this chapter is to section verses to their vials (or bowls) of wrath. This particular verse speaks about the first bowl, which affects the Earth. I’m going out on a limb here, but these vials of wrath demonstrate not only God’s anger towards humanity but His conclusion to all things. The first vial gives conclusion to the beginning."},{"kind":"para","text":"“In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.”"},{"kind":"para","text":"It also depicts the sixth plague of Egypt."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the LORD said unto Moses and unto Aaron, Take to you handfuls of ashes of the furnace, and let Moses sprinkle it toward the heaven in the sight of Pharaoh. And it shall become small dust in all the land of Egypt, and shall be a boil breaking forth with blains upon man, and upon beast, throughout all the land of Egypt. And they took ashes of the furnace, and stood before Pharaoh; and Moses sprinkled it up toward heaven; and it became a boil breaking forth with blains upon man, and upon beast. And the magicians could not stand before Moses because of the boils; for the boil was upon the magicians, and upon all the Egyptians. And the LORD hardened the heart of Pharaoh, and he hearkened not unto them; as the LORD had spoken unto Moses.","ref":"Exodus 9:8-12"}]}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"title":"The Second Vial","entries":[{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The second vial is poured into the sea, causing the sea to become blood and death. This gives conclusion to the creation of the sea!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God said, Let the waters bring forth abundantly the moving creature that hath life, and fowl that may fly above the earth in the open firmament of heaven. And God created great whales, and every living creature that moveth, which the waters brought forth abundantly, after their kind, and every winged fowl after his kind: and God saw that it was good.","ref":"Genesis 10:20-21"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is also a depiction of another event in Exodus:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the fish that was in the river died; and the river stank, and the Egyptians could not drink of the water of the river; and there was blood throughout all the land of Egypt.","ref":"Exodus 7:21"}]}]},{"start":4,"end":7,"title":"The Third Vial","entries":[{"start":4,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The third bowl causes the rivers and springs to become blood, so that they are no longer drinkable. This brings a conclusion to sustainability on Earth:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God said, Let the earth bring forth grass, the herb yielding seed, and the fruit tree yielding fruit after his kind, whose seed is in itself, upon the earth: and it was so. And the earth brought forth grass, and herb yielding seed after his kind, and the tree yielding fruit, whose seed was in itself, after his kind: and God saw that it was good. And the evening and the morning were the third day.","ref":"Genesis 1:11-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is literally cutting the entire Earth off of every drinkable source possible. You would not have a good time thriving off of blood to drink. Not only so, but the angel openly admits and says, “They are worthy” to drink this blood. In other words, “This is what they get for the amount of blood they shed of God’s children. They wanted blood, they will get blood.”"}]}]},{"start":8,"end":9,"title":"The Fourth Vial","entries":[{"start":8,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The fourth vial is going to affect the sun. The sun will be even hotter than it ever has been (people talk about global warming now and blaspheme God’s name, it will be way worse at this point). And this will be but a slight taste of their eternities, and they seemingly won’t be happy about it because it says they continued to “blaspheme the name of God.” This gives conclusion to God’s creation of the sun as well."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God made two great lights; the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night: he made the stars also.","ref":"Genesis 1:16"}]}]},{"start":10,"end":11,"title":"The Fifth Vial","entries":[{"start":10,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This bowl gives darkness to the seat of the world’s leader (Satan) and causes everyone that worships this false god to be in utter pain. It says they were in so much pain that they were literally biting down on their tongues hard and blasphemed God still. This gives conclusion to God’s day of rest!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And on the seventh day God ended his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work he had made.","ref":"Genesis 2:2"}]}]},{"start":12,"end":16,"title":"The Sixth Vial","entries":[{"start":12,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The term “Armageddon” means “Mount Megiddo” in Hebrew. During the Old Israel, Megiddo was a plain, not a mountain. It was also the site of some large battles mentioned in the Bible."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The kings came and fought, then fought the kings of Canaan in Taanach by the waters of Megiddo; they took no gain of money.","ref":"Judges 5:19"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"In his days Pharaohnechoh king of Egypt went up against the king of Assyria to the river Euphrates: and king Josiah went against him; and he slew him at Megiddo, when he had seen him.","ref":"2 Kings 23:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"In John’s vision, it will symbolize the final conflict between Christ and Satan, and where it will be fought. This bowl gives conclusion to God’s creation of the water."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the earth was without form, and void; and darkness was upon the face of the deep. And the Spirit of God moved upon the face of the waters.","ref":"Genesis 1:2"}]}]},{"start":17,"end":21,"title":"The Seventh Vial","entries":[{"start":17,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“It is done,” declares God, has completed His ultimate plan! When Jesus said “It is finished,” He completed the sin payment forever. When God says “It is done,” He completes creation forever. His wrath against evil is completely finished. An earthquake will shatter the city where Jesus was crucified and His martyrs were murdered."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when they shall have finished their testimony, the beast that ascendeth out of the bottomless pit shall make war against them, and shall overcome them, and kill them. And their dead bodies shall lie in the street of the great city, which spiritually is called Sodom and Egypt, where also our Lord was crucified. And they of the people and kindreds and tongues and nations shall see their dead bodies three days and an half, and shall not suffer their dead bodies to be put in graves. And they that dwell upon the earth shall rejoice over them, and make merry, and shall send gifts one to another; because these two prophets tormented them that dwelt on the earth.","ref":"Revelation 11:7-10"},{"kind":"para","text":"All human civilization will end when the Lord comes with thunder, lightning, and earthquakes."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the temple of God was opened in heaven, and there was seen in his temple the ark of his testament: and there were lightnings, and voices, and thundering, and an earthquake, and great hail.","ref":"Revelation 11:19"},{"kind":"para","text":"This last vial attacks the air to complete the firmament of God’s creation and everything that was living as we know it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And God called the firmament Heaven. And the evening and the morning were the second day.","ref":"Genesis 1:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"There, of course, will be more that unfolds in the next few chapters that weren’t directly mentioned in this one. This chapter only covered the wrath of God and the battle of the end. The next chapters will explain what happened to the people and places during these times, and remind us once more about why they deserve this ultimate finish. God brings all things to a close, but notice He never touched a single human being to end them."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even while He is pouring out His wrath, God gives them mercy for salvation, but God also knows that they will not take it, and they prove His foreknowledge by blaspheming Him continually while He proves His Word. He attacks His own creation instead, proving that it’s not US that can survive by our own works."},{"kind":"para","text":"We breathe His air, we drink His water, we live on His earth, and we eat His plants and animals, we see HIS creation, and we have the audacity to think we are better without Him. He will prove this wrong. This was all forewarned. God created all mankind and all things as we know it in the beginning, but He also will end all things He created."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the ending, saith the Lord, which is, and which was, and which is to come, the Almighty.","ref":"Revelation 1:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"I love the contrast as well between Genesis 1:8 and Revelation 1:8. If we have Christ, though, we have the beginning, of course, but we are secure in the end. We may lose everything this world has to offer, but we can never lose Him."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":21}],"verses":{"1":"And I heard a great voice out of the temple saying to the seven angels, Go your ways, and pour out the vials of the wrath of God upon the earth.","2":"And the first went, and poured out his vial upon the earth; and there fell a noisome and grievous sore upon the men which had the mark of the beast, and upon them which worshipped his image.","3":"And the second angel poured out his vial upon the sea; and it became as the blood of a dead man: and every living soul died in the sea.","4":"And the third angel poured out his vial upon the rivers and fountains of waters; and they became blood.","5":"And I heard the angel of the waters say, Thou art righteous, O Lord, which art, and wast, and shalt be, because thou hast judged thus.","6":"For they have shed the blood of saints and prophets, and thou hast given them blood to drink; for they are worthy.","7":"And I heard another out of the altar say, Even so, Lord God Almighty, true and righteous are thy judgments.","8":"And the fourth angel poured out his vial upon the sun; and power was given unto him to scorch men with fire.","9":"And men were scorched with great heat, and blasphemed the name of God, which hath power over these plagues: and they repented not to give him glory.","10":"And the fifth angel poured out his vial upon the seat of the beast; and his kingdom was full of darkness; and they gnawed their tongues for pain,","11":"And blasphemed the God of heaven because of their pains and their sores, and repented not of their deeds.","12":"And the sixth angel poured out his vial upon the great river Euphrates; and the water thereof was dried up, that the way of the kings of the east might be prepared.","13":"And I saw three unclean spirits like frogs come out of the mouth of the dragon, and out of the mouth of the beast, and out of the mouth of the false prophet.","14":"For they are the spirits of devils, working miracles, which go forth unto the kings of the earth and of the whole world, to gather them to the battle of that great day of God Almighty.","15":"Behold, I come as a thief. Blessed is he that watcheth, and keepeth his garments, lest he walk naked, and they see his shame.","16":"And he gathered them together into a place called in the Hebrew tongue Armageddon.","17":"And the seventh angel poured out his vial into the air; and there came a great voice out of the temple of heaven, from the throne, saying, It is done.","18":"And there were voices, and thunders, and lightnings; and there was a great earthquake, such as was not since men were upon the earth, so mighty an earthquake, and so great.","19":"And the great city was divided into three parts, and the cities of the nations fell: and great Babylon came in remembrance before God, to give unto her the cup of the wine of the fierceness of his wrath.","20":"And every island fled away, and the mountains were not found.","21":"And there fell upon men a great hail out of heaven, every stone about the weight of a talent: and men blasphemed God because of the plague of the hail; for the plague thereof was exceeding great."}},
    "17": {"chapter":17,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Previous: In our last chapter, we see the wrath of God being poured out in incredible triumph over all things, depicted as vials (or bowls depending on translation). While 16 seemed to end as the close of God’s wrath, 17 picks up with the final battle (and the events taking place during God’s wrath being poured out). Of course, as we have already mentioned in time past (and specifically as we went over chapter 14), the prostitute is a resemblance of the nation of Babylon. It will be a “Great City” where Satan will build his empire."},{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter 17 gives a vision of the battle, chapter 18 gives the destruction of Babylon and the end of the battle, and then chapter 19 gives the rejoicing of those in Heaven over the victory of the battle, rounding it off with chapter 20 and Christ’s reign for 1,000 years, the defeat and finality of Satan, the Great White Throne Judgement, and then chapter 21 creating a new Heaven, and new Earth, with the “New Jerusalem” finishing everything off with chapter 22, and the river of life adding to the coming of Christ’s return, and the preparation of us TODAY for His second coming. But I’m getting ahead of myself."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our focus, now, is on the battle of this terrible, yet mighty city and the wrath that God had stored up and poured out on it."}],"previously":[],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":8,"title":"The Seven Dooms","entries":[{"start":1,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The term “many waters” in verse 1 symbolizes the multiple nations and people who will follow the rules and strength of Babylon. This is covered later in this chapter. Most countries desire to follow the strengths of another country even today, and it will be no different in the end times when they see a mighty country expanding, building, and thriving even during a time where there are great plagues and conflict everywhere else. God will allow Satan to build up as strong as he’d like, and I think this is on purpose."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who is this King of glory? The Lord strong and mighty, the Lord mighty in battle.","ref":"Psalm 24:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"See, Satan can think himself as strong as he’d like, but in the end he will never be more powerful than God. God will give him his time in power, but it won’t last for very long. Satan may enjoy it, and he may have a rush of authority coming over him, but there will always be the thought of his losing lingering in the back of his mind. He knows he will lose. I believe God will give him power to be strong, simply because the bigger you think you are, the harder you fall."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And whosoever shall exalt himself shall be abased; and he that shall humble himself shall be exalted.","ref":"Matthew 23:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.","ref":"Proverbs 16:18"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Holy Ghost was giving John a prophetic vision, much in the same way that He did with Ezekiel."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then the spirit took me up, and I heard behind me a voice of a great rushing, saying, Blessed be the glory of the Lord from his place.","ref":"Ezekiel 3:12"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Afterwards the spirit took me up, and brought me in a vision by the Spirit of God into Chaldea, to them of the captivity. So the vision that I had seen went up from me.","ref":"Ezekiel 11:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"We’ve spoken about this beast prior to this in chapter 13, but now it has become a “scarlet beast,” on which the woman sits. There have been scholars who acclaim that this lady is to be the antichrist, which supports Babylon. I wouldn’t disagree. During this time, this great city, or “woman,” was thought to (more than likely) be Rome. We won’t know for sure until it happens, however."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The things in which this “prostitute” is portrayed are things that would normally portray an extremely rich and formal wedding. This is a facade to symbolize or display the appeal of worldly pleasures and wealth, which will actually be spoken about more in the next chapter."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the merchants of the earth shall weep and mourn over her; for no man buyeth their merchandise any more: The merchandise of gold, and silver, and precious stones, and of pearls, and fine linen, and purple, and silk, and scarlet, and all thyine wood, and all manner vessels of ivory, and all manner vessels of most precious wood, and of brass, and iron, and marble,","ref":"Revelation 18:11-12"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is what ultimately will keep people interested in the things of this world rather than eternity and the power of God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye adulterers and adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God? Whosoever therefore will be a friend of the world is the enemy of God.","ref":"James 4:4"}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"She’s obviously labeled plainly for the Christian to understand and know, but those who are blinded by the pleasures of the world will not see the deceit and lies that she is really telling. It will be a “mystery” to them. They may even be mystified by the fact that this city is so strong somehow during difficult times."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Those that are wealthy and prosperous during that time will be the ones that kill the followers of Christ. They will physically and literally kill anyone that associates with Christ and Christianity as a whole. We see a large growth of hate for Christians today throughout the whole world. Why would it suddenly stop during the tribulation?"}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We have to remember that this beast was struck and wounded back in chapter 13, nearly to death. Yet, somehow, it heals and comes back to life “miraculously.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he exerciseth all the power of the first beast before him, and causeth the earth and them which dwell therein to worship the first beast, whose deadly wound was healed. And he doeth great wonders, so that he maketh fire come down from heaven on the earth in the sight of men, And deceiveth them that dwell on the earth by the means of those miracles which he had power to do in the sight of the beast; saying to them that dwell on the earth, that they should make an image to the beast, which had the wound by a sword, and did live.","ref":"Revelation 13:12-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"The people were amazed that the beast (or the city) was able to recover from such great damage, and they are tricked into thinking it is some sort of cosmic blessing, rather than seeing the truth of scripture. At this point, those that aren’t saved will be slaughtered, only because they are amazed and hold the “beast” in reverence as a miracle in itself. They will be tricked by Satan into making them think he (Satan) is the real god. But Satan’s power to persecute Christians will be limited, and his future violence to those that don’t believe will also be limited, which we will read about in chapter 19 (If you want to skip ahead (Rev. 19:19-21; Rev. 20:7-10))"}]}]},{"start":9,"end":18,"title":"The Last Form of Gentile World-Power","entries":[{"start":9,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"As an interesting insight, the city of Rome rests on seven mountains (or seven hills). If you read through Old Testament prophecies, mountains usually symbolized a place of power."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will render unto Babylon and to all the inhabitants of Chaldea all their evil that they have done in Zion in your sight, saith the LORD. Behold, I am against thee, O destroying mountain, saith the LORD, which destroyest all the earth: and I will stretch out mine hand upon thee, and roll thee down from the rocks, and will make thee a burnt mountain.","ref":"Jeremiah 51:24-25"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then was the iron, the clay, the brass, the silver, and the gold, broken to pieces together, and became like the chaff of the summer threshingfloors; and the wind carried them away, that no place was found for them: and the stone that smote the image became a great mountain, and filled the whole earth…And in the days of these kings shall the God of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed: and the kingdom shall not be left to other people, but it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever. Forasmuch as thou sawest that the stone was cut out of the mountain without hands, and that it brake in pieces the iron, the brass, the clay, the silver, and the gold; the great God hath made known to the king what shall come to pass hereafter: and the dream is certain, and the interpretation thereof sure.","ref":"Daniel 2:35;44-45"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, as the beast’s seven heads symbolize the power of the nations (seven kings), this will give these rulers power over the people that are not written in the Lamb’s book of Life. Satan’s time is “short,” because he knows he’s headed for an eternity of torment. So he wrecks havoc as much as he can with his limited time to drag as many people as possible with him."}]},{"start":12,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Whether or not it will be a literal “10 rulers” is not quite clear, but it certainly seems to symbolize that the majority (if not all) of the rulers of this Earth during this time will have joined sides with Satan foolishly. These people in authority will lead their own people into destruction and war seemingly out of a desire for more riches and pleasure. They will use their power to kill and destroy anything and anybody who calls out to the Lamb or shows credence to the Lamb (or Jesus Christ)."}]},{"start":15,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Eventually, the partnership between the prostitute and the beast will end. At this point, the armies will destroy the economic system it was supporting once before, and the people will suffer greatly because of it. It says that the beast and its allies will strip this city “desolate and naked,” leaving it with nothing but ruin. They will “eat her flesh” and “burn her with fire.”"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will also give thee into their hand, and they shall throw down thine eminent place, and shall break down thy high places: they shall strip thee also of thy clothes, and shall take thy fair jewels, and leave thee naked and bare. They shall also bring up a company against thee, and they shall stone thee with stones, and thrust thee through with their swords. And they shall burn thine houses with fire, and execute judgments upon thee in the sight of many women: and I will cause thee to cease from playing the harlot, and thou also shalt give no hire any more.","ref":"Ezekiel 16:38-41"},{"kind":"para","text":"This is amazing, not because of the destruction, betrayal, deception, and death. It’s amazing because God has this set up on purpose so that the enemies of God will destroy each other, and He literally doesn’t have to do anything because this ultimately was His purpose and promise fulfilled. God literally uses His own enemies to complete His purpose."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Commit thy works unto the Lord, and thy thoughts shall be established. The Lord hath made all things for himself: yea, even the wicked for the day of evil.","ref":"Proverbs 16:3-4"},{"kind":"para","text":"The wicked in this world have a purpose for God, and it’s not to create more wickedness, but to bring an ultimate end to it through their own deceit and vain attempts to rid the world of evil while promoting evil without God."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is why the city is believed to be Rome, because during the time of this writing, Rome had dominion over the kings of the earth. Rome was a very powerful and very great city. Though terrible, it was great."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18}],"verses":{"1":"And there came one of the seven angels which had the seven vials, and talked with me, saying unto me, Come hither; I will shew unto thee the judgment of the great whore that sitteth upon many waters:","2":"With whom the kings of the earth have committed fornication, and the inhabitants of the earth have been made drunk with the wine of her fornication.","3":"So he carried me away in the spirit into the wilderness: and I saw a woman sit upon a scarlet coloured beast, full of names of blasphemy, having seven heads and ten horns.","4":"And the woman was arrayed in purple and scarlet colour, and decked with gold and precious stones and pearls, having a golden cup in her hand full of abominations and filthiness of her fornication:","5":"And upon her forehead was a name written, MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS AND ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.","6":"And I saw the woman drunken with the blood of the saints, and with the blood of the martyrs of Jesus: and when I saw her, I wondered with great admiration.","7":"And the angel said unto me, Wherefore didst thou marvel? I will tell thee the mystery of the woman, and of the beast that carrieth her, which hath the seven heads and ten horns.","8":"The beast that thou sawest was, and is not; and shall ascend out of the bottomless pit, and go into perdition: and they that dwell on the earth shall wonder, whose names were not written in the book of life from the foundation of the world, when they behold the beast that was, and is not, and yet is.","9":"And here is the mind which hath wisdom. The seven heads are seven mountains, on which the woman sitteth.","10":"And there are seven kings: five are fallen, and one is, and the other is not yet come; and when he cometh, he must continue a short space.","11":"And the beast that was, and is not, even he is the eighth, and is of the seven, and goeth into perdition.","12":"And the ten horns which thou sawest are ten kings, which have received no kingdom as yet; but receive power as kings one hour with the beast.","13":"These have one mind, and shall give their power and strength unto the beast.","14":"These shall make war with the Lamb, and the Lamb shall overcome them: for he is Lord of lords, and King of kings: and they that are with him are called, and chosen, and faithful.","15":"And he saith unto me, The waters which thou sawest, where the whore sitteth, are peoples, and multitudes, and nations, and tongues.","16":"And the ten horns which thou sawest upon the beast, these shall hate the whore, and shall make her desolate and naked, and shall eat her flesh, and burn her with fire.","17":"For God hath put in their hearts to fulfil his will, and to agree, and give their kingdom unto the beast, until the words of God shall be fulfilled.","18":"And the woman which thou sawest is that great city, which reigneth over the kings of the earth."}},
    "18": {"chapter":18,"intro":[{"kind":"scripture","text":"And a mighty angel took a stone like a great millstone, and cast it into the sea, saying, Thus with violence shall that great city Babylon be thrown down, and shall be found no more at all.","ref":"Revelation 18:21"},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be THAT quickly. Looking through the time, lineage, and growth of America recently, we have become such a prosperous nation because of the Christian beliefs that were set before us so many years ago. If it hadn’t been for God’s providence on the matter, America would not be standing today. In fact, there is so much historical proof and legitimate documentation about the foundation of America being guarded and led by God that it’s impossible to separate Christianity from America today (though many have tried). We are a prosperous nation, but we are decaying, and the reason we have seen decay is simple… We are no longer looking to the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"During the end times, there will be a city even greater than America. One where the highest source of providence will come from, and the only way any other nation can survive is by selling and trading to this specific city which will be great, and not because they looked to God. The city that is spoken about here will be great because they trusted in Satan. They were blinded by material wealth, and in the end that is all they had in this life. This chapter brings a great conclusion for those that are in Heaven, but a treacherous one to those that remain on Earth."}],"previously":["After the wrath takes place, there will still be life on Earth, but things will have changed drastically before the Lord’s second coming. While we will get into that soon, John will now reveal the things that will be happening during the middle of all the wrath that was being poured out. We’ve seen a lot of the finality that God will be committing, but we have not really gotten the overall detail of everything happening on Earth with the people. In this chapter, we will be taken right into the middle of it all and see how the people react to these issues and what that will ultimately lead them to. We see in this chapter, one of the greatest cities (if not THE greatest city) during the end times completely come to waste. Literally within just a few minutes, the largest, strongest, wealthiest, and most glorious cities in all of existence is taken down in the blink of an eye. The verse that demonstrates this the best is found in verse 21:"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":8,"title":"A Warning to God’s People","entries":[{"start":1,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The falling of Babylon will give the destroyed city over to every kind of unclean spirit, bird, and beast."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And, behold, here cometh a chariot of men, with a couple of horsemen. And he answered and said, Babylon is fallen, is fallen; and all the graven images of her gods he hath broken unto the ground.","ref":"Isaiah 21:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s sufficient to say, this city will not be a place that anyone will want to live in at this point. In fact, the chances of them being able to live here will be 0 because there will be nothing left. God will literally destroy and bring down their only source of material possession. The rest of the world literally depended on this city, and now that it’s gone, they won’t know what to do. They will be surprised to see that this city didn’t make it considering how great this city was (more on this in verse 9)."}]},{"start":4,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is likely referring to the one hundred and forty-four thousand that were chosen later on (which, if you don’t remember, may not depict a literal amount of people, but a small remnant). God is letting it be known that He doesn’t want them to be a part of their destruction and sin. He wants His people to be set apart, and He warns this to His people throughout all of history."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Depart ye, depart ye, go ye out from thence, touch no unclean thing; go ye out of the midst of her; be ye clean, that bear the vessels of the Lord.","ref":"Isaiah 52:11"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"My people, go ye out of the midst of her, and deliver ye every man his soul from the fierce anger of the Lord.","ref":"Jeremiah 51:45"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers: for what fellowship hath righteousness with unrighteousness? and what communion hath light with darkness? And what concord hath Christ with Belial? or what part hath he that believeth with an infidel? And what agreement hath the temple of God with idols? for ye are the temple of the living God; as God hath said, I will dwell in them, and walk in them; and I will be their God, and they shall be my people. Wherefore come out from among them, and be ye separate, saith the Lord, and touch not the unclean thing; and I will receive you, And will be a Father unto you, and ye shall be my sons and daughters, saith the Lord Almighty.","ref":"2 Corinthians 6:14-18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Dearly beloved, I beseech you as strangers and pilgrims, abstain from fleshly lusts, which war against the soul; Having your conversation honest among the Gentiles: that, whereas they speak against you as evildoers, they may by your good works, which they shall behold, glorify God in the day of visitation.","ref":"1 Peter 2:11-12"},{"kind":"para","text":"God does not desire His children, even during the end times of judgement, to be a part of His wrath. He desires that all would be saved, but He also must serve justice to those that go against Him and the truth of what is truly right and wrong. God starts with “144,000” (so-to-speak) people and He will end with “144,000” (so-to-speak) people. He will not lose one."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That the saying might be fulfilled, which he spake, Of them which thou gavest me have I lost none.","ref":"John 18:9"}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is a justified call for judgement on this city. This was a terrible city of large quantities of murder and adultery, and all sorts of perverse and disgusting things that society will soon call “normal” to the world. It’s already started to consider much of the things that have been labeled throughout Revelation as normal, so it’s no surprise that it will be quite evident during the last days to the callousness of truth and righteousness."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And if any mischief follow, then thou shalt give life for life, Eye for eye, tooth for tooth, hand for hand, foot for foot, Burning for burning, wound for wound, stripe for stripe.","ref":"Exodus 21:23-25"},{"kind":"para","text":"But not only will they be paid back for their acts of cruelty to their own, they will get a “double portion” of what this crooked city gave because of the murdering of the saints."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Speak ye comfortably to Jerusalem, and cry unto her, that her warfare is accomplished, that her iniquity is pardoned: for she hath received of the Lord’s hand double for all her sins.","ref":"Isaiah 40:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"God will have every right to give them what they desired, and to give them more than they expected."}]},{"start":7,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"And this is why (as I said in the last chapter) I believe God allows Satan to become so prosperous in his building. The one thing Satan cannot (and will not) do is humble himself. So because of his pride, he will fall harder than I think he was even anticipating. Even if he knows everything there is to know about Revelation (and I do believe Satan knows), he still won’t be prepared for what is to come."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And thou saidst, I shall be a lady for ever: so that thou didst not lay these things to thy heart, neither didst remember the latter end of it. Therefore hear now this, thou that art given to pleasures, that dwellest carelessly, that sayest in thine heart, I am, and none else beside me; I shall not sit as a widow, neither shall I know the loss of children: But these two things shall come to thee in a moment in one day, the loss of children, and widowhood: they shall come upon thee in their perfection for the multitude of thy sorceries, and for the great abundance of thine enchantments.","ref":"Isaiah 47:7-9"}]}]},{"start":9,"end":19,"title":"What “Babylon” Represents","entries":[{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These verses prove my previous comment about how surprised the rest of the world will be to see this city go to destruction. They weren’t prepared for this kind of turmoil. They assumed, at the very least, this city would remain and be stronger than anything that has ever been seen before. Furthermore, look at the countenance of the rest of the world because this city has fallen."}]},{"start":11,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It says in verse 11 that they are “weeping and mourning” over the destruction of this city. Why? Not because people died. Not because of the unity this city brought to the world. Not even because of the amount of freedom and sin-sick living they provided. They were sad because they were losing out on their main source of material gain. That was it. They depended on this city so much that now that the city was in destruction, they were concerned about how they were going to get their slaves, flour, and precious metals… They didn’t care about the thousands of lives lost, they only cared about the fact that they lost their income."},{"kind":"para","text":"May this be a lesson to you, friend. If you lean on your job, your money, your skills, or anything under your power, you won’t have to wait long to see it fall apart. Lean on the Lord and you will never fall. When you have the Lord, the furthest you can fall is on Him, and He is a firm foundation. Don’t trust your income or job more than Him and you won’t be disappointed when it inevitably falls apart."}]},{"start":14,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, this is pathetic… The world will become so adept at worldly living that they don’t even see the issue with abusing material possession over loving one another. It will be a cold and cruel place to live, and if you are not like them in this way during this time, you will be used as cargo (or a slave), or you will be murdered for your incompetence in their way of thinking. At this point, I would rather be killed, because I wouldn’t want to think and behave like these people crying over the loss of their greed…"}]}]},{"start":20,"end":24,"title":"The Heavenly View of “Babylon”","entries":[{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To them, the world is dark, cruel, miserable, and only because they will no longer be able to live as comfortably as they did before. To US (those that are saved), we will have the opportunity to “rejoice,” because the judgement that was given was not for God’s benefit, but for ours. God executed judgement on our behalf because the people are evil and only desire to do evil and heinous things."}]},{"start":21,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"That “bloop” in the water will be how quickly the judgement will last. It will be over in the blink of an eye. The world will go silent, and the people will be completely dumbfounded. The final judgement will have taken place."}]},{"start":24,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God will have judged the world, Babylon, and the Beast because of the blood that was shed with God’s prophets and saints, which was already promised by God through this book of Revelation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And they cried with a loud voice, saying, How long, O Lord, holy and true, dost thou not judge and avenge our blood on them that dwell on the earth?","ref":"Revelation 6:10"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And their dead bodies shall lie in the street of the great city, which spiritually is called Sodom and Egypt, where also our Lord was crucified.","ref":"Revelation 11:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I saw the woman drunken with the blood of the saints, and with the blood of the martyrs of Jesus: and when I saw her, I wondered with great admiration.","ref":"Revelation 17:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"This will be when God cleans up all of it, and there will be no more evil to triumph over left on Earth. The next chapter represents this…"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":24}],"verses":{"1":"And after these things I saw another angel come down from heaven, having great power; and the earth was lightened with his glory.","2":"And he cried mightily with a strong voice, saying, Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen, and is become the habitation of devils, and the hold of every foul spirit, and a cage of every unclean and hateful bird.","3":"For all nations have drunk of the wine of the wrath of her fornication, and the kings of the earth have committed fornication with her, and the merchants of the earth are waxed rich through the abundance of her delicacies.","4":"And I heard another voice from heaven, saying, Come out of her, my people, that ye be not partakers of her sins, and that ye receive not of her plagues.","5":"For her sins have reached unto heaven, and God hath remembered her iniquities.","6":"Reward her even as she rewarded you, and double unto her double according to her works: in the cup which she hath filled fill to her double.","7":"How much she hath glorified herself, and lived deliciously, so much torment and sorrow give her: for she saith in her heart, I sit a queen, and am no widow, and shall see no sorrow.","8":"Therefore shall her plagues come in one day, death, and mourning, and famine; and she shall be utterly burned with fire: for strong is the Lord God who judgeth her.","9":"And the kings of the earth, who have committed fornication and lived deliciously with her, shall bewail her, and lament for her, when they shall see the smoke of her burning,","10":"Standing afar off for the fear of her torment, saying, Alas, alas, that great city Babylon, that mighty city! for in one hour is thy judgment come.","11":"And the merchants of the earth shall weep and mourn over her; for no man buyeth their merchandise any more:","12":"The merchandise of gold, and silver, and precious stones, and of pearls, and fine linen, and purple, and silk, and scarlet, and all thyine wood, and all manner vessels of ivory, and all manner vessels of most precious wood, and of brass, and iron, and marble,","13":"And cinnamon, and odours, and ointments, and frankincense, and wine, and oil, and fine flour, and wheat, and beasts, and sheep, and horses, and chariots, and slaves, and souls of men.","14":"And the fruits that thy soul lusted after are departed from thee, and all things which were dainty and goodly are departed from thee, and thou shalt find them no more at all.","15":"The merchants of these things, which were made rich by her, shall stand afar off for the fear of her torment, weeping and wailing,","16":"And saying, Alas, alas, that great city, that was clothed in fine linen, and purple, and scarlet, and decked with gold, and precious stones, and pearls!","17":"For in one hour so great riches is come to nought. And every shipmaster, and all the company in ships, and sailors, and as many as trade by sea, stood afar off,","18":"And cried when they saw the smoke of her burning, saying, What city is like unto this great city?","19":"And they cast dust on their heads, and cried, weeping and wailing, saying, Alas, alas, that great city, wherein were made rich all that had ships in the sea by reason of her costliness! for in one hour is she made desolate.","20":"Rejoice over her, thou heaven, and ye holy apostles and prophets; for God hath avenged you on her.","21":"And a mighty angel took up a stone like a great millstone, and cast it into the sea, saying, Thus with violence shall that great city Babylon be thrown down, and shall be found no more at all.","22":"And the voice of harpers, and musicians, and of pipers, and trumpeters, shall be heard no more at all in thee; and no craftsman, of whatsoever craft he be, shall be found any more in thee; and the sound of a millstone shall be heard no more at all in thee;","23":"And the light of a candle shall shine no more at all in thee; and the voice of the bridegroom and of the bride shall be heard no more at all in thee: for thy merchants were the great men of the earth; for by thy sorceries were all nations deceived.","24":"And in her was found the blood of prophets, and of saints, and of all that were slain upon the earth."}},
    "19": {"chapter":19,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 19"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: We studied the defeat of Satan’s overthrow by revealing the ultimate destruction of one of the most powerful cities that Satan has ever built and will ever build up. People from all around the world see this destruction and weep over it because it means they lose out on material and financial gain."},{"kind":"para","text":"People complain about the slavery issues of America’s past (as if it originated in America and never ceased… even though America was one of the first countries to abolish slavery as soon as it became a nation, but I digress…) during this time of Revelation, slavery will just be common practice, and at an all time high. Higher than this world has ever experienced before."},{"kind":"para","text":"But with the destruction of this city, comes the destruction of evil, and that is why we have this chapter today. That is why people are rejoicing over the fall of so many, and so much envy, pride, and murder. Evil will no longer be tolerated from now through eternity…"},{"kind":"para","text":"The events that take place in this chapter, are ones to pay attention to, because they are ones that WE will be a part of."}],"previously":[", we studied the defeat of Satan’s overthrow by revealing the ultimate destruction of one of the most powerful cities that Satan has ever built and will ever build. People from all around the world see this destruction and weep over it because it means they lose out on material and financial gain. During this time of Revelation, people complain about the slavery issues of America’s past (as if it originated in America and never ceased… even though America was one of the first countries to abolish slavery as soon as it became a nation, but I digress…). However, during this period, slavery will just be common practice and at an all-time high, higher than this world has ever experienced before. But with the destruction of this city comes the destruction of evil, and that is why we have this chapter today. That is why people are rejoicing over the fall of so many, and the fall of all this envy, pride, and murder. Evil will no longer be tolerated from now through eternity… The events that take place in this chapter are ones to pay attention to because they are ones that WE (the saved) will be a part of."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"Rejoicing in Heaven","entries":[{"start":1,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"John clarifies that after all the events that have taken place, we will be singing Alleluia with the hosts of Heaven to the Lord, all in one accord, as if we were one voice! Heaven’s unity is unmatched, and it’s something we should strive for here on Earth to prepare ourselves for this event in eternity."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Finally, be ye all of one mind, having compassion one of another, love as brethren, be pitiful, be courteous:","ref":"1 Peter 3:8"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Finally, brethren, farewell. Be perfect, be of good comfort, be of one mind, live in peace; and the God of love and peace shall be with you.","ref":"2 Corinthians 13:11"},{"kind":"para","text":"This will ultimately prepare the way for Jesus to come back to Earth and put an end to the tribulation and all of Satan’s ploys and divisions."}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Because the smoke goes on forever and ever, we know and understand that this judgement is permanent. There’s no coming back from an event like this. The fact that we will be praising God for this destruction proves the grotesque and awful evil that this “great prostitute” or city has done and will deserve its final judgement."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is where things start to connect back to previous visions from earlier in this book. We’ve already linked quite a bit back to previous visions, but we see some things brought up that we haven’t touched on in quite some time."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when he had taken the book, the four beasts and four and twenty elders fell down before the Lamb, having every one of them harps, and golden vials full of odours, which are the prayers of saints. And they sung a new song, saying, Thou art worthy to take the book, and to open the seals thereof: for thou wast slain, and hast redeemed us to God by thy blood out of every kindred, and tongue, and people, and nation; And hast made us unto our God kings and priests: and we shall reign on the earth.","ref":"Revelation 5:8-10"},{"kind":"para","text":"The elders are represented by the church, but that image will change now because the church will now become the Bride of Christ."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If we have no reason to praise God, even during His judgments and wrath, we have something wrong in us. We know and understand that God is a righteous judge. Every decision He makes is intricate and perfect. He has all things purposed for His Will and timing, and if we disagree with it, and we think that God is wrong for doing such, we don’t have to look much farther than ourselves as the problem."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is always right, and if we think He’s wrong, we must understand that WE are the ones that are wrong. Not only so, but if this be the case (and we think that He has done a horrible thing by killing these horrible people who have abused His children and all of humanity and this Earth), then we will be right alongside them here on Earth as these events unroll. And it won’t look good from this point of view either."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":10,"title":"The Marriage Supper of the Lamb","entries":[{"start":6,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, this is the part that every child of God is looking forward to! Before Christ returns to Earth, He will have a wedding, and we will be a part of it! Some people may look at this and think, “Why would Jesus want to marry a bunch of people, and doesn’t marriage implicate intimacy, and why would Jesus choose to have that kind of a relationship with millions of others? This picture doesn’t quite match up…” Honestly, the picture doesn’t match up because their view of marriage is absolutely wrong."},{"kind":"para","text":"The view of marriage we are supposed to have is not based on physical appeal or value, but on a spiritual one alone. Without spiritual value in the marriage (that’s from both partners), the marriage is a sham. It’s not Godly, and the home cannot be Godly without it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus’s marriage to us means we will be forever in unity with Him. This allows us full access to everything He has full access to. We become one with Christ. Imagine that! EVERYTHING He has full access to!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For I am jealous over you with godly jealousy: for I have espoused you to one husband, that I may present you as a chaste virgin to Christ.","ref":"2 Corinthians 11:2"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the church, and gave himself for it; That he might sanctify and cleanse it with the washing of water by the word, That he might present it to himself a glorious church, not having spot, or wrinkle, or any such thing; but that it should be holy and without blemish.","ref":"Ephesians 5:25-27"},{"kind":"para","text":"This has always been the representation of marriage since the beginning of time with Adam and Eve. It was a picture of oneness through Christ and the church. This event will be the biggest we experience as believers!"}]},{"start":9,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"I want to just make a few notes here… One, John (who knows better than to worship anything but God) is seen here bowing down before an angel. Does the angel accept worship, or praise, or honor? No! Of course not! He tells him who to worship! He will mistakingly do it again later in this book, and the same correction is made:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I John saw these things, and heard them. And when I had heard and seen, I fell down to worship before the feet of the angel which shewed me these things. Then saith he unto me, See thou do it not: for I am thy fellowservant, and of thy brethren the prophets, and of them which keep the sayings of this book: worship God.","ref":"Revelation 22:8-9"},{"kind":"para","text":"Second (or two), John literally experienced this same kind of false worship himself before and was found telling people to worship God alone. He and Peter both saw this happen together and understood the necessity placed on worshipping God over everything!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But Peter took him up, saying, Stand up; I myself also am a man.","ref":"Acts 10:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"I certainly don’t want to draw away from the important note to make here though, which is the invitation to this supper. How do we get invited to this supper? We must be the bride! How do we be the bride? We must be the church! How do we be the church? We must be saved and born-again! And when we are saved through Christ, we are “blessed” to be invited to this amazing wedding and supper!"}]}]},{"start":11,"end":18,"title":"The Rider on a White Horse","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Remember in chapter 3, we talked about white being the color of victory? This rider (obviously representing Christ Himself) is already victorious. If you read through the book of John (especially when Jesus speaks), He always talks as if He had already done specific things… Jesus was living in the present and the future. He is in all places at once!"}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"God’s greatness exceeds even eternal knowledge, so He Himself is the only one that can know this name because He still sits above His bride in Heaven."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name: Which were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God.","ref":"John 1:12-13"},{"kind":"para","text":"His name doesn’t just mean “Jesus,” but it means everything that is true to His name and His Word. We can’t just simply believe in Jesus, but we have to believe everything about Him and God’s Word!"}]},{"start":13,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"John has made mention several times already, and specifically in the gospel of John, that Jesus is God’s Word in the flesh. He will still be God’s Word in the flesh, even in eternity, and as He comes back to Earth to rule and reign. The robe sprinkled with blood more than likely represents His anger and judgement for the war that is to take place."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who is this that cometh from Edom, with dyed garments from Bozrah? this that is glorious in his apparel, travelling in the greatness of his strength? I that speak in righteousness, mighty to save. Wherefore art thou red in thine apparel, and thy garments like him that treadeth in the winefat? I have trodden the winepress alone; and of the people there was none with me: for I will tread them in mine anger, and trample them in my fury; and their blood shall be sprinkled upon my garments, and I will stain all my raiment. For the day of vengeance is in mine heart, and the year of my redeemed is come. And I looked, and there was none to help; and I wondered that there was none to uphold: therefore mine own arm brought salvation unto me; and my fury, it upheld me. And I will tread down the people in mine anger, and make them drunk in my fury, and I will bring down their strength to the earth.","ref":"Isaiah 63:1-6"}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, the fact that we, too, get white horses shows our connection to Christ and our own victory through Him."}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Further proving that the blood sprinkled on His robe is from His enemies. From His mouth coming a sharp sword, I believe will indicate that He will just have to speak and destroy those that are at battle with Him. It won’t be much in regards to His physical strength. He won’t have to lift a single finger."}]},{"start":16,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, we have covered this verse before! This is another representation that this isn’t just some random rider from Heaven, but this is IN FACT, Jesus Christ and His second coming. When He came to Earth the first time, it was in gentleness and meekness, serving those that needed it, and being the Savior. When He comes the second time, it will be in judgement and righteousness, putting an end to those that reject Him."}]},{"start":17,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This particular scene links back to an Old Testament covenant judgement."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And thy carcass shall be meat unto all fowls of the air, and unto the beasts of the earth, and no man shall fray them away.","ref":"Deuteronomy 28:26"},{"kind":"para","text":"Ezekiel speaks specifically about this as well:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And, thou son of man, thus saith the Lord GOD; Speak unto every feathered fowl, and to every beast of the field, Assemble yourselves, and come; gather yourselves on every side to my sacrifice that I do sacrifice for you, even a great sacrifice upon the mountains of Israel, that ye may eat flesh, and drink blood. Ye shall eat the flesh of the mighty, and drink the blood of the princes of the earth, of rams, of lambs, and of goats, of bullocks, all of them fatlings of Bashan. And ye shall eat fat till ye be full, and drink blood till ye be drunken, of my sacrifice which I have sacrificed for you. Thus ye shall be filled at my table with horses and chariots, with mighty men, and with all men of war, saith the Lord GOD.","ref":"Ezekiel 39:17-20"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, as gross and heinous as this seems, there is a biblical importance to this, and it’s one that further displays God’s ultimate justice being served. The king’s death will equal out to no more than birds eating their flesh, and an eternity in torment and torture because they helped support the enemy."}]}]},{"start":19,"end":21,"title":"The Capture of the Beast","entries":[{"start":19,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is just funny. I don’t really have much to comment on this particular verse, because we’ve already seen how fighting against God has played out for them. They still think they have what it takes to contend with God."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But if it be of God, ye cannot overthrow it; lest haply ye be found even to fight against God.","ref":"Acts 5:39"}]},{"start":20,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously (in case you don’t remember), the beast and the false prophet (like we’ve spoken previously about the great prostitute) will represent evil and corrupt people and institutions (probably, and not limited to, false churches)."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"“The rest” being the rulers of the earth and their allies (or armies). Obviously, only Christ and His Bride will survive this battle against Satan, and the remnant will be those who will have to be ruled under Christ’s authority for 1,000 years. This starts off the one thousand year reign that God had already promised throughout His Word. It wasn’t specifically promised that He would reign for 1,000 years, but it was promised that when He came back, He would reign over the Earth. I won’t go into that particular purpose yet, because that is the main theme of the next chapter, but it’s an interesting study that I hope to spend a great deal of time on."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":12},{"start":13,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15},{"start":16,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":20},{"start":21,"end":21}],"verses":{"1":"And after these things I heard a great voice of much people in heaven, saying, Alleluia; Salvation, and glory, and honour, and power, unto the Lord our God:","2":"For true and righteous are his judgments: for he hath judged the great whore, which did corrupt the earth with her fornication, and hath avenged the blood of his servants at her hand.","3":"And again they said, Alleluia. And her smoke rose up for ever and ever.","4":"And the four and twenty elders and the four beasts fell down and worshipped God that sat on the throne, saying, Amen; Alleluia.","5":"And a voice came out of the throne, saying, Praise our God, all ye his servants, and ye that fear him, both small and great.","6":"And I heard as it were the voice of a great multitude, and as the voice of many waters, and as the voice of mighty thunderings, saying, Alleluia: for the Lord God omnipotent reigneth.","7":"Let us be glad and rejoice, and give honour to him: for the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made herself ready.","8":"And to her was granted that she should be arrayed in fine linen, clean and white: for the fine linen is the righteousness of saints.","9":"And he saith unto me, Write, Blessed are they which are called unto the marriage supper of the Lamb. And he saith unto me, These are the true sayings of God.","10":"And I fell at his feet to worship him. And he said unto me, See thou do it not: I am thy fellowservant, and of thy brethren that have the testimony of Jesus: worship God: for the testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy.","11":"And I saw heaven opened, and behold a white horse; and he that sat upon him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness he doth judge and make war.","12":"His eyes were as a flame of fire, and on his head were many crowns; and he had a name written, that no man knew, but he himself.","13":"And he was clothed with a vesture dipped in blood: and his name is called The Word of God.","14":"And the armies which were in heaven followed him upon white horses, clothed in fine linen, white and clean.","15":"And out of his mouth goeth a sharp sword, that with it he should smite the nations: and he shall rule them with a rod of iron: and he treadeth the winepress of the fierceness and wrath of Almighty God.","16":"And he hath on his vesture and on his thigh a name written, KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS.","17":"And I saw an angel standing in the sun; and he cried with a loud voice, saying to all the fowls that fly in the midst of heaven, Come and gather yourselves together unto the supper of the great God;","18":"That ye may eat the flesh of kings, and the flesh of captains, and the flesh of mighty men, and the flesh of horses, and of them that sit on them, and the flesh of all men, both free and bond, both small and great.","19":"And I saw the beast, and the kings of the earth, and their armies, gathered together to make war against him that sat on the horse, and against his army.","20":"And the beast was taken, and with him the false prophet that wrought miracles before him, with which he deceived them that had received the mark of the beast, and them that worshipped his image. These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone.","21":"And the remnant were slain with the sword of him that sat upon the horse, which sword proceeded out of his mouth: and all the fowls were filled with their flesh."}},
    "20": {"chapter":20,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 20"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: We looked at the rejoicing that will take place in Heaven over the victory won against Satan and the enemies of God. We saw the marriage supper of the Lamb that every believer will be a part of. It characterizes Jesus returning as a rider on a white horse. Ending it off with the capture of the beast for a season allowing this chapter to pick up where the last left off."},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s certainly easy to read Revelation and forget the purpose of it all. God loves us so much that He wants to spend an eternity with us. He wants His creation to be perfected to the point that we can remain in His presence for all of eternity to glorify Him and be with Him. Since Genesis, that was the plan. It was to get all of His creation to a point where we will purposefully go to Him for salvation, and then lead us to His presence in eternal glory and unity. There’s nothing more important and exciting than to spend forever with our Father in Heaven, and that’s what we need to remember when we are reading this account."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have seen the fall and destruction of so much of Satan’s power and people. We’ve seen the ultimate rebellion of the people as they continuously reject God without even thinking about who God is. They fall for the ploys and traps of Satan so many times that they don’t even realize they are doing it. In fact, they are doing it with a smile! Smiling as they cause division. Smiling as they kill Christians. Smiling as they destroy the Earth that God has given to them. They are so far under the rule of Satan that they will think they have one over on God, but (as we’ve already seen) God has the final say."},{"kind":"para","text":"This chapter will be no different. God will be cleaning up the mess at this point and providing a perfect ending to the ultimate redemptive story. The next three chapters will be focused on God’s ultimate goal and purpose for all of these which are to come to pass (which we already know at this point is for Christ and our presence with Him) but there are still some things that haven’t been talked about fully…"}],"previously":["We looked at the rejoicing that will take place in Heaven over the victory won against Satan and the enemies of God. We saw the marriage supper of the Lamb that every believer will be a part of. It characterizes Jesus returning as a rider on a white horse. Ending it off with the capture of the beast for a season, allowing this chapter to pick up where the last left off. It’s certainly easy to read Revelation and forget the purpose of it all. God loves us so much that He wants to spend an eternity with us. He wants His creation to be perfected to the point that we can remain in His presence for all of eternity to glorify Him and be with Him. Since Genesis, that was the plan. It was to get all of His creation to a point where we will purposefully go to Him for salvation, and then lead us to His presence in eternal glory and unity. There’s nothing more important and exciting than to spend forever with our Father in Heaven, and that’s what we need to remember when we are reading this account. We have seen the fall and destruction of so much of Satan’s power and people. We’ve seen the ultimate rebellion of the people as they continuously reject God without even thinking about who God is. They fall for the ploys and traps of Satan so many times that they don’t even realize they are doing it. In fact, they are doing it with a smile! Smiling as they cause division. Smiling as they kill Christians. Smiling as they destroy the Earth that God has given to them. They are so far under the rule of Satan that they will think they have one over on God, but (as we’ve already seen) God has the final say. This chapter will be no different. God will be cleaning up the mess at this point and providing a perfect ending to the ultimate redemptive story. The next three chapters will be focused on God’s ultimate goal and purpose for all of these, which are to come to pass (which we already know at this point is for Christ and our presence with Him), but there are still some things that haven’t been talked about fully…"],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":6,"title":"The Thousand Years","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This chapter of scripture divides a lot of scholars. The division is categorized by “Premillennialists,” “Postmillennialists,” and “Amillennialists.” I will do my best to showcase each line of thinking and pull references for each."},{"kind":"para","text":"“Premillennialists” believe Christ will return before the millennium. They assume this thousand years is a future time of great peace and justice. They usually consider this to be the literal 1,000-year period that will begin when Christ returns to reign on Earth. He will be King, and resurrected believers will reign with Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"“Postmillennialists” believe that Christ will return AFTER the millennial period. They think that before Christ returns to Earth, the gospels will spread and triumph. Societies will be transformed. Peace and justice will reign on Earth for a thousand years. Afterward, Christ will return for His final judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"“Amillennialists” believe a non-literal millennial view. They think this thousand years is the same period as this present church age. They believe there will be no future “millennium” before Christ returns for the final judgement."},{"kind":"para","text":"I will not say which is right and which is not, but I will assume (solemnly based off of Scripture) the one I believe to be most accurate as we go through this chapter (you make the decision for yourself)."},{"kind":"para","text":"1 And I saw an angel come down from heaven, having the key of the bottomless pit and a great chain in his hand. 2 And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years, 3 And cast him into the bottomless pit, and shut him up, and set a seal upon him, that he should deceive the nations no more, till the thousand years should be fulfilled: and after that he must be loosed a little season."},{"kind":"para","text":"Satan will be sealed up in Hell while Christ reigns over the Earth for a thousand years, proving His victory and showing His lordship. Of course, this insinuates a premillennial mindset. Hell won’t just be shut; it will be sealed, and we already know that the only one that can open seals from the Lord is Christ Himself. This also proves that God has the power and authority to restrict Satan and to allow Satan to do what only God will prove."},{"kind":"para","text":"4 And I saw thrones, and they sat upon them, and judgment was given unto them: and I saw the souls of them that were beheaded for the witness of Jesus, and for the word of God, and which had not worshipped the beast, neither his image, neither had received his mark upon their foreheads, or in their hands; and they lived and reigned with Christ a thousand years."},{"kind":"para","text":"Seeing as we are told that these angels are “coming down” from heaven, and it references the “nations” in verse 3, my assumption is that these judges will be on Earth at this point. This further provides a defense of premillennialism. Everything we have read so far through Revelation has been taken at face value unless otherwise stated."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And out of his mouth goeth a sharp sword, that with it he should smite the nations: and he shall rule them with a rod of iron: and he treadeth the winepress of the fierceness and wrath of Almighty God.","ref":"Revelation 19:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"We understand this is not speaking of a literal sword coming out of Jesus’ mouth."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God:","ref":"Ephesians 6:17"},{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, when it comes to dealing with time (one thousand years), we come to the conclusion that time is not a construct that God lives by. Heavenly time is not human time."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But, beloved, be not ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with the Lord as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.","ref":"2 Peter 3:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Seeing as Christ will be on Earth (which is obviously the case as this verse insinuates), then the thousand years are more than likely literal."},{"kind":"para","text":"5 But the rest of the dead lived not again until the thousand years were finished. This is the first resurrection."},{"kind":"para","text":"Look at what the Bible says about the resurrection of the dead right after Jesus’ death and resurrection."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the graves were opened; and many bodies of the saints which slept arose,","ref":"Matthew 27:52"},{"kind":"para","text":"I honestly believe that this is a picture of this verse in Revelation here. We will have our bodily resurrection. But those that experience this with Christ on Earth, it says, were the ones that were beheaded and didn’t receive the beast’s mark in verse 5. We will get there ourselves later…"},{"kind":"para","text":"6 Blessed and holy is he that hath part in the first resurrection: on such the second death hath no power, but they shall be priests of God and of Christ, and shall reign with him a thousand years."},{"kind":"para","text":"To reign with God is the ultimate desire. Those that experience this will have earned their position once the tribulation is over. It will be a rightful place for them to be while they are helping Christ end the evil that this world will have been clinging onto for so long. It will likely take one thousand years from the sound of it… This is when they will be cast in the lake of fire, forever…"}]}]},{"start":7,"end":10,"title":"The Defeat of Satan","entries":[{"start":7,"end":9,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is the last time Satan will be allowed to rebel against God. Obviously, the one thousand years provides a large time of testing before the judgement takes place. According to these verses, there will be a large army that tries to stand with Satan during this time. After so many people have died, and so much has been destroyed, where do you think these people will come from? My guess is it’s from those that have had children during the thousand years. One thousand years is a long time to live on Earth and not have kids. And this is scripturally backed as well!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"The wolf also shall dwell with the lamb, and the leopard shall lie down with the kid; and the calf and the young lion and the fatling together; and a little child shall lead them… There shall be no more thence an infant of days, nor an old man that hath not filled his days: for the child shall die an hundred years old; but the sinner being an hundred years old shall be accursed.","ref":"Isaiah 11:6;65:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, with Christ’s ruling, these people will be taken care of, but because of the sin nature of the world, they will still turn their backs on God… This is not a surprise because this already happens today. In fact, the Bible is full of stories of God taking care of the people, even giving them food out of the sky to eat, and they still turn their backs on God and deny Him. Why would anything be different in the last days?"},{"kind":"para","text":"It’s supposed that the “Gog and Magog” reference links back to Old Testament pagan oppressors that Israel fought against. Like, for instance, we have a “World War I” and a “World War 2” today, they will have a “Gog 1” and a “Gog and Magog 2.”"}]},{"start":10,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"And this is the verse that every single child of God looks forward to. To see the end of Satan forever. He will never be able to deceive or hurt, or divide anything or anybody again. It’s a verse that should be highlighted in our Bibles. It’s one that should be thought on and recognized because we know that at that moment (which seems can’t come soon enough) Satan will be banished forever, and he will be in torment for all of eternity, getting what he deserves for all of the evil he forced and provided to this Earth."}]}]},{"start":11,"end":15,"title":"Judgement Before the Great White Throne","entries":[{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Remember, “White” displays “purity” and “wisdom.” This is no different with this throne. There’s nothing impure about this judgement seat. And it’s done in all wisdom. Proverbs speaks very highly about wisdom, and Solomon is right when he mentions it in the way he does. A lot of people believe that wisdom is something that is achieved through hard work and loyal attention. Wisdom is not these things, though. Wisdom is a person. Christ is wisdom. Because of this, the throne in which He makes His final judgement will only be seated by the embodiment of purity and wisdom."}]},{"start":12,"end":13,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Every single person that has passed on in life since the beginning of time will be before this judgement. Those that didn’t have Christ will be sent back to an eternal torment and torture, and will be reminded of their opportunity to accept Him before it was too late and to repent from their sins. Those that knew Christ will be there too, and they will be judged based on the life they led for Christ. These books will be records of their deeds."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.","ref":"Daniel 7:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"It will be evidence as to why they are being judged as such, and will leave the party being judged without excuse."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Who will render to every man according to his deeds: To them who by patient continuance in well doing seek for glory and honour and immortality, eternal life: But unto them that are contentious, and do not obey the truth, but obey unrighteousness, indignation and wrath, Tribulation and anguish, upon every soul of man that doeth evil, of the Jew first, and also of the Gentile; But glory, honour, and peace, to every man that worketh good, to the Jew first, and also to the Gentile: For there is no respect of persons with God.","ref":"Romans 2:6-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"Then the book of life will be opened, and we have spoken quite frequently about that already. It’s mentioned several times throughout Revelation."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.","ref":"Revelation 3:5"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And all that dwell upon the earth shall worship him, whose names are not written in the book of life of the Lamb slain from the foundation of the world.","ref":"Revelation 13:8"},{"kind":"para","text":"Just a couple of references…"}]},{"start":14,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"No more death, no more grave. Christ had already defeated death and the grave…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"O death, where is thy sting? O grave, where is thy victory? The sting of death is sin; and the strength of sin is the law.","ref":"1 Corinthians 15:55-56"},{"kind":"para","text":"But now we will get to see the victory take place when death will be banished for all of eternity, and the grave with it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But every man in his own order: Christ the firstfruits; afterward they that are Christ's at his coming. Then cometh the end, when he shall have delivered up the kingdom to God, even the Father; when he shall have put down all rule and all authority and power. For he must reign, till he hath put all enemies under his feet. The last enemy that shall be destroyed is death.","ref":"1 Corinthians 15:23-26"}]},{"start":15,"end":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The saddest verse in all of the Bible. We think about all the murder that was accounted for through Biblical record, including the one of Jesus Christ taking place (an innocent man dying for the sins of the entire world), and it doesn’t even compare to this verse right here. John 3:16 is a great verse for hope. But Revelation 20:15 is the verse that should give every Christian fervency."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":7,"end":9},{"start":10,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":13},{"start":14,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":15}],"verses":{"7":"And when the thousand years are expired, Satan shall be loosed out of his prison,","8":"And shall go out to deceive the nations which are in the four quarters of the earth, Gog and Magog, to gather them together to battle: the number of whom is as the sand of the sea.","9":"And they went up on the breadth of the earth, and compassed the camp of the saints about, and the beloved city: and fire came down from God out of heaven, and devoured them.","10":"And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever.","11":"And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them.","12":"And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before God; and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.","13":"And the sea gave up the dead which were in it; and death and hell delivered up the dead which were in them: and they were judged every man according to their works.","14":"And death and hell were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death.","15":"And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire."}},
    "21": {"chapter":21,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 21"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: We spoke about the 1,000 years that Jesus will be reigning on Earth, the ultimate demise and defeat of Satan, and the final judgement called “The Great White Throne Judgement.” There was certainly plenty to unpack, and now we will be looking at what is to come after all of this is said and done and there will be no more death, or pain, or suffering, or sin."}],"previously":["We spoke about the thousand years that Jesus will be reigning on Earth, the ultimate demise and defeat of Satan, and the final judgement called “The Great White Throne Judgement.” There was certainly plenty to unpack, and now we will be looking at what is to come after all of this is said and done, and there will be no more death, pain, suffering, or sin."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":8,"title":"A New Heaven and a New Earth","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"When it speaks of a “New Heaven” and “New Earth,” I don’t believe it is talking about a new creation altogether. I believe it speaks on the idea that things will be “Renewed.” God won’t have to start over with His creation; that would defeat the purpose of the things that took place here, and the fact that we are still alive today (He should just destroy us now if that is what He plans on doing anyway to start completely over)."},{"kind":"para","text":"No, He is taking the old creation and making it new again, better. Something with no sin, no death, no pain, no difficulties. Something where we will work, but we will enjoy our work. We will enjoy our toils and lives. We will enjoy our time and purpose. We will never grow old, and we will never have to worry about supplication or necessities again. Everything will be provided to us in perfect harmony and unity."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"So also is the resurrection of the dead. It is sown in corruption; it is raised in incorruption: It is sown in dishonour; it is raised in glory: it is sown in weakness; it is raised in power:","ref":"1 Corinthians 15:42-43"}]},{"start":2,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"As we’ve clarified before, the bride of Christ is the church, and this “New Jerusalem” is symbolic of the US, His bride."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But ye are come unto mount Sion, and unto the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, and to an innumerable company of angels, To the general assembly and church of the firstborn, which are written in heaven, and to God the Judge of all, and to the spirits of just men made perfect, And to Jesus the mediator of the new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling, that speaketh better things than that of Abel.","ref":"Hebrews 12:22-24"}]},{"start":3,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This will be the greatest blessing of all that we will receive in Heaven. We will be in constant fellowship with God, and will be able to be near Him like we never could before. We will have a closer relationship with Him than we do today. This has always been God’s ultimate purpose and goal. For us to be His people, and for Him to be our God."}]},{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Though we will be talking about the look of this New Jerusalem in a moment, the more important thoughts are found in this verse here. The way the city will look, and the place we will dwell is not nearly as important as how the people will be. We all desire to have a nice house, we all want to live in a beautiful neighborhood, but how are the people? You can have a really nice-looking house on one of the most deadly streets in the world. This verse tells us how we will live together in this city made by God."}]},{"start":5,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Everything will be renewed. Everything will have a fresh start and a new purpose."}]},{"start":6,"end":6,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus said, “It is finished.” When He completed His work on the cross. Now Jesus said, “It is done.” When He completes His work for all of life as we know it."}]},{"start":7,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The new Heaven and Earth are ours for the taking if we have conquered with Christ through the sins of the world and the battle of Satan. We are currently in a battle with Satan; it doesn’t just start when the anti-Christ comes."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Little children, it is the last time: and as ye have heard that antichrist shall come, even now are there many antichrists; whereby we know that it is the last time.","ref":"1 John 2:18"},{"kind":"para","text":"The battle will be completely finished once Satan is in his eternal resting place forever."}]},{"start":8,"end":8,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, those that are labeled in the list here have already received their second death. Most of whom were those that died in times past by rejecting Christ."}]}]},{"start":9,"end":27,"title":"The New Jerusalem","entries":[{"start":9,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We are now viewing the city in which the people of God will be able to dwell with God. I think of it like church. We don’t necessarily live in the church; we go to a place to worship, and we call that “church.” This is a symbol of the city in which God dwells (if the church is correctly moving in the right direction of the Lord)."},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s a lot of symbolism that could be mentioned here, but the gist of it is that this city represents the adoration that Christ places on the Bride, which is the church. The assembly of believers. The city seems to be literal, seeing as there are measurements and key specificities of it, but each item that is mentioned in the city resembles something significant to the Lord and His perfection."}]},{"start":12,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The city’s high walls and twelve gates symbolize absolute perfection. The gates have the names of the twelve tribes of Israel, and the names of the twelve apostles are on the foundations, which gives us clarity that the Old Testament and the New Testament are in unity with each other."}]},{"start":15,"end":17,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"It being in equal shape and length draws a strand to 1 Kings and the perfect shape of the Old Testament sanctuary."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the oracle in the forepart was twenty cubits in length, and twenty cubits in breadth, and twenty cubits in the height thereof: and he overlaid it with pure gold; and so covered the altar which was of cedar.","ref":"1 Kings 6:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"There’s no need for a temple in this city because the whole city is God’s most holy place. The length, width, and height of this city are equal to one thousand three hundred and eighty miles. It’s obviously a very large city, and if we think of this like a church, it would be MASSIVE. Lancaster Baptist Church (one I used to go to in California) gets a lot of flack because of its size. People think it’s a cult because of how big it is and they assume the attendees of that church live right there on the church grounds because of the amount of buildings it has. Granted, as we know, most of those buildings are college and school buildings, but others don’t know that. This New Jerusalem will be a very large city, even bigger than most states! It’s about three thousand miles from coast to coast of the United States. If we took half of the US and squared it up, it would be about the size of this city."}]},{"start":18,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, pure gold is clear because there would be no impurities in it. The reason gold is a yellow color today is because there are too many impurities in it. But the reason it’s so valuable is because of its pliability and usefulness. Whether the streets will be labeled with literal gold or if this is just symbolic of the bride’s purity is up for you to decide."}]},{"start":19,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"These twelve jewels resemble stones associated with Eden…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Thou hast been in Eden the garden of God; every precious stone was thy covering, the sardius, topaz, and the diamond, the beryl, the onyx, and the jasper, the sapphire, the emerald, and the carbuncle, and gold: the workmanship of thy tabrets and of thy pipes was prepared in thee in the day that thou wast created. Thou art the anointed cherub that covereth; and I have set thee so: thou wast upon the holy mountain of God; thou hast walked up and down in the midst of the stones of fire.","ref":"Ezekiel 28:13-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"And they resemble the names that are engraved on the breastplate of the high priest…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And thou shalt set in it settings of stones, even four rows of stones: the first row shall be a sardius, a topaz, and a carbuncle: this shall be the first row. And the second row shall be an emerald, a sapphire, and a diamond. And the third row a ligure, an agate, and an amethyst. And the fourth row a beryl, and an onyx, and a jasper: they shall be set in gold in their inclosings.","ref":"Exodus 28:17-20"},{"kind":"para","text":"Another interesting bit of information is that each gate will be made from one pearl. I don’t know if you know how small a pearl is or how they work, but to have a large gate of this size made out of ONE pearl is a miraculous thing in itself. Why pearls? I don’t know. It’s just another interesting design feature that God is capable of doing, and it’s an astounding one at that."}]},{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, the proof that this whole city will be God’s temple is the fact that there is none, and the fact that God will reside there with His people."}]},{"start":23,"end":23,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Of course, light does not exist simply because of a source. TO US, we understand light, and we understand its source. If we see the sun, we know that there is light all around us. When the sun is gone, the light is also gone except by the reflection of the moon. However, God made light before the sun in Genesis, and so in Revelation, when the sun and moon are gone, we will always have light because God IS light. That’s why we are light. We are like the moon. We don’t produce the light, we just reflect it as Jesus has commanded."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid. Neither do men light a candle, and put it under a bushel, but on a candlestick; and it giveth light unto all that are in the house. Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.","ref":"Matthew 5:14-26"},{"kind":"para","text":"My daughter and I love to go outside and see a full moon. We are fascinated by the size and brightness of it. I have used the moon as an example of faith. “The moon is a great representation of us,” I would say. “It’s an example of how we are supposed to be. The universe does not circle around us; we circle around the sun (or the Son). We do not provide light; we just reflect the light. Sometimes the world gets in the way, but we must always come back to the light in fullness, displaying hope and salvation for everyone every day. Don’t ever let your light go completely out.” It’s a sad sight when we go out to see a full moon and can’t find it…"}]},{"start":24,"end":27,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There’s no need for gates, there’s no need for walls. The reason the gates will never be shut is because there will be no more enemies left to threaten the city. Once again, a lot of symbolism, but the most important thing to focus on is the fact that this dwelling place of the Lord will be near enough to His people that we are able to dwell with Him and be with Him all the time."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":1},{"start":2,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":4},{"start":5,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":6},{"start":7,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":8},{"start":9,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":17},{"start":18,"end":18},{"start":19,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":22},{"start":23,"end":23},{"start":24,"end":27}],"verses":{"1":"And I saw a new heaven and a new earth: for the first heaven and the first earth were passed away; and there was no more sea.","2":"And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from God out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.","3":"And I heard a great voice out of heaven saying, Behold, the tabernacle of God is with men, and he will dwell with them, and they shall be his people, and God himself shall be with them, and be their God.","4":"And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away.","5":"And he that sat upon the throne said, Behold, I make all things new. And he said unto me, Write: for these words are true and faithful.","6":"And he said unto me, It is done. I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the end. I will give unto him that is athirst of the fountain of the water of life freely.","7":"He that overcometh shall inherit all things; and I will be his God, and he shall be my son.","8":"But the fearful, and unbelieving, and the abominable, and murderers, and whoremongers, and sorcerers, and idolaters, and all liars, shall have their part in the lake which burneth with fire and brimstone: which is the second death.","9":"And there came unto me one of the seven angels which had the seven vials full of the seven last plagues, and talked with me, saying, Come hither, I will shew thee the bride, the Lamb's wife.","10":"And he carried me away in the spirit to a great and high mountain, and shewed me that great city, the holy Jerusalem, descending out of heaven from God,","11":"Having the glory of God: and her light was like unto a stone most precious, even like a jasper stone, clear as crystal;","12":"And had a wall great and high, and had twelve gates, and at the gates twelve angels, and names written thereon, which are the names of the twelve tribes of the children of Israel:","13":"On the east three gates; on the north three gates; on the south three gates; and on the west three gates.","14":"And the wall of the city had twelve foundations, and in them the names of the twelve apostles of the Lamb.","15":"And he that talked with me had a golden reed to measure the city, and the gates thereof, and the wall thereof.","16":"And the city lieth foursquare, and the length is as large as the breadth: and he measured the city with the reed, twelve thousand furlongs. The length and the breadth and the height of it are equal.","17":"And he measured the wall thereof, an hundred and forty and four cubits, according to the measure of a man, that is, of the angel.","18":"And the building of the wall of it was of jasper: and the city was pure gold, like unto clear glass.","19":"And the foundations of the wall of the city were garnished with all manner of precious stones. The first foundation was jasper; the second, sapphire; the third, a chalcedony; the fourth, an emerald;","20":"The fifth, sardonyx; the sixth, sardius; the seventh, chrysolite; the eighth, beryl; the ninth, a topaz; the tenth, a chrysoprasus; the eleventh, a jacinth; the twelfth, an amethyst.","21":"And the twelve gates were twelve pearls; every several gate was of one pearl: and the street of the city was pure gold, as it were transparent glass.","22":"And I saw no temple therein: for the Lord God Almighty and the Lamb are the temple of it.","23":"And the city had no need of the sun, neither of the moon, to shine in it: for the glory of God did lighten it, and the Lamb is the light thereof.","24":"And the nations of them which are saved shall walk in the light of it: and the kings of the earth do bring their glory and honour into it.","25":"And the gates of it shall not be shut at all by day: for there shall be no night there.","26":"And they shall bring the glory and honour of the nations into it.","27":"And there shall in no wise enter into it any thing that defileth, neither whatsoever worketh abomination, or maketh a lie: but they which are written in the Lamb's book of life."}},
    "22": {"chapter":22,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"Chapter: Chapter 22"},{"kind":"para","text":"Group: Friday, Thursday"},{"kind":"para","text":"Status: Complete"},{"kind":"para","text":"## Previously: We have finally finished the tribulation and the 1,000 year reign. We have seen all evil and pain come to an end, and sin be completely demolished. We’ve gotten a glimpse at a new Heaven and Earth, and we are coming to the final portrayal of Heaven, and the last warning to the churches of that day (and today)."}],"previously":["We have finally finished the tribulation and the one thousand year reign. We have seen all evil and pain come to an end, and sin be completely demolished. We’ve gotten a glimpse at a new Heaven and Earth, and we are coming to the final portrayal of Heaven, and the last warning to the churches of that day (and today)."],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":5,"title":"The River of Life","entries":[{"start":1,"end":2,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Bringing it back full circle. In the beginning, in the garden, there was a river that ran through it."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became into four heads.","ref":"Genesis 2:10"},{"kind":"para","text":"Now we see a different kind of river, and it represents purity, holiness, and it only comes from God’s throne. This water does not divide but provides purity to the city in which it originates (being the New Jerusalem, whether literal or not). On both sides of this river was the tree of life, which draws us back (yet again) to the beginning."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And out of the ground made the Lord God to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.","ref":"Genesis 2:9"},{"kind":"para","text":"This gives further reference to the fact that we will eat and drink when we go to Heaven. Pure water, and life-giving fruit from a tree (with twelve different kinds of fruit that grow on one tree). Not only do we have a tree of life, we also have a river of life, which will be talked about more in the coming verses."},{"kind":"para","text":"The part that I find interesting though, is in verse 2 when it says, “…and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations…” If pain and suffering has been cast into Hell (which was spoken of in the chapter before last), then why would the leaves on this tree need to have the power of healing? There’s no clear-cut explanation of this. But we do know that the New Jerusalem will be like a place of worship. It will be the church for the people of the New Earth. My assumption is, we would have to eventually go back to church to receive a constant renewing and healing. This may be why the people of Earth continuously have access to it."}]},{"start":3,"end":5,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This concludes the vision of the tribulation and the start of an eternal living that we will continuously look forward to until the world ends and all of this starts to appear. Multiple times, we are told that no one has seen God and lived."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"No man hath seen God at any time, the only begotten Son, which is in the bosom of the Father, he hath declared him.","ref":"John 1:18"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he said, Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live.","ref":"Exodus 33:20"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Then flew one of the seraphims unto me, having a live coal in his hand, which he had taken with the tongs from off the altar: And he laid it upon my mouth, and said, Lo, this hath touched thy lips; and thine iniquity is taken away, and thy sin purged.","ref":"Isaiah 6:6-7"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are even told that people would die if they simply touched the Ark of the Covenant made by Moses."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And when they came to Nachon’s threshingfloor, Uzzah put forth his hand to the ark of God, and took hold of it; for the oxen shook it. And the anger of the Lord was kindled against Uzzah; and God smote him there for his error; and there he died by the ark of God.","ref":"2 Samuel 5:5-7"},{"kind":"para","text":"God is too holy for us to behold. Even when Jesus was with some of the host from Heaven, he was “transfigured” because of the presence of holiness around Him."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And after six days Jesus taketh Peter, James, and John his brother, and bringeth them up into an high mountain apart, And was transfigured before them: and his face did shine as the sun, and his raiment was white as the light. And, behold, there appeared unto them Moses and Elias talking with him.","ref":"Matthew 17:1-3"},{"kind":"para","text":"But here, at the end of it all, it says, “They shall see his face…” What a day it will be to be able to look into the face of God and live. What a perfect ending to an imperfect world. We will be in such holiness and divinity that we won’t even have to worry about looking God directly in the face. That’s what God wants the most… His light will shine bright for us in those days so we won’t even have to worry about seeing or turning on a light. There won’t be a need for electricity to see in those days because God will be present with us and we will continuously reflect His presence forever."}]}]},{"start":6,"end":21,"title":"Jesus is Coming","entries":[{"start":6,"end":7,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, Jesus warns about coming quickly. In the beginning of this book, He tells us…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Blessed is he that readeth, and they that hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein: for the time is at hand.","ref":"Revelation 1:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"He warns us, yet again, in this last chapter that we must be prepared. May we be a prepared people. The church must be a prepared church. The churches that John was writing to still exist today. They are the majority of churches around us. They are the people we interact with all the time who are so casual about their lifestyle in Christ. They are the ones who never study, pray, or have a necessity to serve or be around other Christians, and they think it’s all okay and their walk is still great. These are the people that Christ wrote this book for."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wrote it for the churches who need to rethink their purposes and goals. He wrote it for the Christians who have fallen out of love with God. He wrote it for the Christians who need to wake up and realize the necessity of proclaiming God’s Word and loving God more! He wrote it for us, to be prepared, and for others so that they will get serious about the Lord, because He was warning about how quickly He was coming to John back in AD 96… two thousand years later now, and the warning is even more dire…"}]},{"start":8,"end":10,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"John falls for the same stupid trap he fell for before and tries to worship an angel. We know this angel is legitimate; otherwise, he would have accepted worship. John has the opportunity at this point to refocus on what this was all about. Remember our ten rules at the beginning? The last rule was, everything in this book has the same focus as the rest of the Bible, the center being Jesus Christ. We need not seal this book up, but remember that the time is at hand!"}]},{"start":11,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"We should never be in the business of trying to change someone else the way we think they should be. Tell people the truth, and then let God do the rest. If they continue to reject God, that’s up to them. We must water the seed and stop trying to plant new ones in places where there are already seeds."},{"kind":"para","text":"If they want to live unjustly, let them live in their unrighteousness, let them live in their filth. If they want to live in righteousness, let them live in their righteousness (in fact, encourage them in their righteousness), and let them continue to seek after holiness. Eventually these things will come to pass anyway, and when it does, there will be nobody with an excuse as to what is happening and why they shouldn’t suffer through it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Too many churches are like those of the time John was writing this book… Not only so, but John literally writes this not too long after the first church is established. It didn’t take long for the churches to start to fall behind in sin. The church today is running rampant in these sins, and there is even more of them than there was before, a majority of them being right here in America! This was quite a sight for John to see. It was something that made him obviously undone to falsely worship an angel twice. The angel reminds him here of his ultimate purpose and goal with this information."}]},{"start":12,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The angel is further sealing the sayings here by connecting it with Jesus Himself. This isn’t just the angel’s saying; this is from the mouth of Christ! Jesus brings it full circle once more to the beginning, yet again speaking about the bright and morning star (if you don’t remember this portion of the study, you can find it in chapter 2):"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I will give him the morning star.","ref":"Revelation 2:28"},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not (currently) at this point of the rapture or tribulation yet, and so it gives us vitality to be more prepared, better equipped, more compassionate, and increasingly earnest to love God more and share the truth with others. We look forward to the day when we get to enter through those gates and take part in the tree of life with the other believers."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"That I may know him, and the power of his resurrection, and the fellowship of his sufferings, being made conformable unto his death; If by any means I might attain unto the resurrection of the dead. Not as though I had already attained, either were already perfect: but I follow after, if that I may apprehend that for which also I am apprehended of Christ Jesus. Brethren, I count not myself to have apprehended: but this one thing I do, forgetting those things which are behind, and reaching forth unto those things which are before, I press toward the mark for the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus.","ref":"Philippians 3:10-14"},{"kind":"para","text":"May we seek the perfection that we will receive in eternity while we are continuing here on Earth."}]},{"start":17,"end":19,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The invitation is still open. Both Christ and the church are crying for the lost to come to this water of life and to be partakers of this free everlasting gift. There’s coming a day when it will be closed off… What do we do then? Who do we know that needs to hear this message? Who do we claim to love that we’ve never shared the gospel with? It can be anybody. Our parents? Our children? Our spouses? Our friends? Our neighbors? Our coworkers? Our church?"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me.","ref":"Revelation 3:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"He invites everyone to come to this free gift of life. But He also warns all those that don’t take part in sharing this gift by removing words, or adding words to this book. Whether simply to the book of Revelation, or simply to the Bible as a whole, may we be watchful and cautious about God’s Word being properly distributed…"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth.","ref":"2 Timothy 2:15"}]},{"start":20,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, we get the warning of Jesus stating the speed in which He will be returning. It’s “quickly.” He’s coming sooner than we think. We are ill-prepared for it, but it won’t stop Him from coming. Some are under the impression that waiting on Jesus’ coming is to deny our duties as Christians and relaxing in a form of “escapism.” But look how the Bible as a whole ends, “…Even so, come Lord Jesus…” This needs to be highlighted in every Bible."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are ill-prepared, but that is exactly why we look forward to when Jesus returns. This world is not prepared, and it seems to be falling apart more and more. The churches have lost their love, and so it’s vital that we hope for the return of Christ coming back for His saints. We should all be under the same impression as John is here, and say, “Even so, come Lord Jesus…” But until then, strive for grace and love of Christ… for eventually it will be exchanged for judgement and suffering…"}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":2},{"start":3,"end":5},{"start":6,"end":7},{"start":8,"end":10},{"start":11,"end":11},{"start":12,"end":16},{"start":17,"end":19},{"start":20,"end":21}],"verses":{"1":"And he shewed me a pure river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of God and of the Lamb.","2":"In the midst of the street of it, and on either side of the river, was there the tree of life, which bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month: and the leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations.","3":"And there shall be no more curse: but the throne of God and of the Lamb shall be in it; and his servants shall serve him:","4":"And they shall see his face; and his name shall be in their foreheads.","5":"And there shall be no night there; and they need no candle, neither light of the sun; for the Lord God giveth them light: and they shall reign for ever and ever.","6":"And he said unto me, These sayings are faithful and true: and the Lord God of the holy prophets sent his angel to shew unto his servants the things which must shortly be done.","7":"Behold, I come quickly: blessed is he that keepeth the sayings of the prophecy of this book.","8":"And I John saw these things, and heard them. And when I had heard and seen, I fell down to worship before the feet of the angel which shewed me these things.","9":"Then saith he unto me, See thou do it not: for I am thy fellowservant, and of thy brethren the prophets, and of them which keep the sayings of this book: worship God.","10":"And he saith unto me, Seal not the sayings of the prophecy of this book: for the time is at hand.","11":"He that is unjust, let him be unjust still: and he which is filthy, let him be filthy still: and he that is righteous, let him be righteous still: and he that is holy, let him be holy still.","12":"And, behold, I come quickly; and my reward is with me, to give every man according as his work shall be.","13":"I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the end, the first and the last.","14":"Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.","15":"For without are dogs, and sorcerers, and whoremongers, and murderers, and idolaters, and whosoever loveth and maketh a lie.","16":"I Jesus have sent mine angel to testify unto you these things in the churches. I am the root and the offspring of David, and the bright and morning star.","17":"And the Spirit and the bride say, Come. And let him that heareth say, Come. And let him that is athirst come. And whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely.","18":"For I testify unto every man that heareth the words of the prophecy of this book, If any man shall add unto these things, God shall add unto him the plagues that are written in this book:","19":"And if any man shall take away from the words of the book of this prophecy, God shall take away his part out of the book of life, and out of the holy city, and from the things which are written in this book.","20":"He which testifieth these things saith, Surely I come quickly. Amen. Even so, come, Lord Jesus.","21":"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all. Amen."}},
  },
};
